        "766": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "767": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "770": {"synopsis":"Returns to the editor from NextZXOS ROM 0's menu (its $093C, through CALL_ALT_ROM):\n1. With bit 0 of E set (ROM 0 passes the flags of its test at $0924-$092B in E: carry),\nFLAGS bit 5 set.\n2. When A equals the mode at $D5B8: with A = 5 the editor started afresh in mode 4\n(START_MODE_A); otherwise the columns applied (ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY) and the editor\nresumed as it was (EDITOR_RESUME).\n3. Otherwise $D5B8 = A and the editor started afresh in that mode (EDITOR_START).\nEntry: A = the mode, E = ROM 0's flags.","comment":"ROM 0's carry in bit 0 of E?"},
        "774": {"comment":"Then FLAGS bit 5 set"},
        "778": {"synopsis":"Same mode as before?","comment":"HL = the mode now"},
        "781": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "782": {"comment":"Another mode: stored, started afresh"},
        "784": {"comment":"Mode 5?"},
        "788": {"comment":"Then mode 4, started afresh"},
        "791": {"comment":"The columns applied (COLUMNS_APPLY)","synopsis":"The same mode: the columns applied (ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY), the editor resumed as it was."},
        "794": {"comment":"The editor as it was"},
        "796": {"synopsis":"Another mode: stored; A made even for EDITOR_START.","comment":"The new mode"},
        "797": {"comment":"A even"},
        "798": {"synopsis":"Starts the editor in mode 2A (0 NextBASIC, 4 the Calculator, 8 a third mode): reached from\nthe menu action table at $216F with A = 2i for its entries i0-i2, and from NextZXOS ROM 0's\nBROWSER_RESUME ($2C3D) with A = 0.\n1. E_PPC = 0; $D5B8 = $D5EC = the mode; $D752 = E_PPC.\n2. Bank 7's $C000-$D5AD zeroed; $D5B7 = $80; TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared.\n3. The columns applied (ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY) and the window set (WINDOW_SETUP).\n4. Mode 0: the upper screen (SCREEN_TO_UPPER); mode 4: the cursor at 0, 0 first; mode 8:\n   SCREEN_TO_UPPER, $136A and SCREEN_TO_LOWER.\n5. $1059, then EDITOR_RESUME.\nEntry: A = 2 x the mode number.","comment":"A = the mode: 0, 4 or 8"},
        "799": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0","synopsis":"EDITOR_START with A already the mode, not doubled (from REENTER_MODE with A = 4)."},
        "805": {"synopsis":"EDITOR_START with E_PPC kept: from $13B5 with A = ($D5EC).","comment":"The mode stored"},
        "808": {"comment":"And as the rows' mode"},
        "811": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "814": {"comment":"$D752 = it"},
        "817": {"comment":"Bank 7 from $C000"},
        "820": {"comment":"To $D5AD"},
        "823": {"comment":"The count less one"},
        "826": {"comment":"The first byte 0"},
        "828": {"comment":"Zeroed"},
        "830": {"comment":"$D5B7 = $80"},
        "835": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "839": {"comment":"The mode kept"},
        "840": {"comment":"The columns applied (COLUMNS_APPLY)"},
        "843": {"comment":"The window set up"},
        "846": {"comment":"The mode back"},
        "847": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "850": {"comment":"Mode 4?"},
        "854": {"comment":"Mode 8: the upper screen set up"},
        "857": {"comment":"$136A (ROM 0's $0D2A on the window's rows)"},
        "860": {"comment":"Then the lower screen"},
        "863": {"comment":"On"},
        "865": {"synopsis":"Mode 4: the cursor at row 0, column 0 (CURSOR_STORE).","comment":"Row 0, column 0, remembered column 0"},
        "868": {"comment":"The cursor stored"},
        "871": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: the upper screen.","comment":"The upper screen"},
        "874": {"synopsis":"$1059 for all modes.","comment":"$D7DB = 1, $D7DC = 5 ($1059)"},
        "877": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "878": {"synopsis":"Resumes the editor:\n1. $D5B7 bit 3 (the line changed) cleared.\n2. Editing in the upper screen ($D5B7 bit 6 clear): the title bar (ROM 0's EDIT_TITLE_BAR),\n   the columns applied, the key mode reset (ROM 0's KEY_MODE_RESET).\n3. IX = $D7DD, DF_SZ = 2, both row buffers emptied, $D5B5 = 0.\n4. Mode 4: the cursor shown, then MAIN_KEY_LOOP.\n5. Otherwise E_PPC = the number of the first line at or after it (ROM 3's FIND_LINE and\n   LINE_NO, in bank 0), the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), the cursor shown and moved to a new\n   row after the line (KEY_ENTER); then MAIN_KEY_LOOP.","comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "881": {"comment":"The line not changed"},
        "883": {"comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "887": {"comment":"The title bar (EDIT_TITLE_BAR)"},
        "890": {"comment":"The columns applied (COLUMNS_APPLY)"},
        "893": {"comment":"The key mode reset (KEY_MODE_RESET)"},
        "896": {"synopsis":"IX, DF_SZ and the buffers; the way on by the mode.","comment":"IX = the window's block"},
        "900": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "904": {"comment":"No rows below the window"},
        "907": {"comment":"No rows above it"},
        "910": {"comment":"No places to move the cursor on"},
        "916": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "919": {"comment":"The Calculator?"},
        "921": {"comment":"Then the cursor shown"},
        "924": {"comment":"On to the key loop"},
        "926": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "929": {"comment":"Bank 0 with the program"},
        "930": {"comment":"The first line at or after E_PPC (FIND_LINE)"},
        "933": {"comment":"DE = its number (LINE_NO)"},
        "936": {"comment":"Bank 7 again"},
        "937": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "941": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt and drawn"},
        "944": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "947": {"comment":"The cursor to a new row after the line"},
        "950": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key with a click (ROM 0's WAIT_KEY_CLICK) and handles it (KEY_DISPATCH);\nforever, the stack reset to $5BFF each time.","comment":"The stack reset"},
        "953": {"comment":"A = the key (WAIT_KEY_CLICK)"},
        "956": {"comment":"Handled"},
        "959": {"comment":"Forever"},
        "961": {"synopsis":"Handles key A: looked up in the key table at $143C (TABLE_DISPATCH); a routine that returns\nno carry gets a click (KEY_REFUSED). A code not in the table is a character (KEY_INSERT), or\na click when $D5B7 bit 0 is set (the rows are full). Keeps AF for table keys.\nEntry: A = the key code.","comment":"HL = the key table"},
        "964": {"comment":"The key kept"},
        "965": {"comment":"In the table?"},
        "968": {"comment":"Not in the table"},
        "970": {"comment":"Refused: a click"},
        "973": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "975": {"synopsis":"Not in the table: a character.","comment":"The key back"},
        "976": {"comment":"The rows full ($D5B7 bit 0)?"},
        "981": {"comment":"Then a click"},
        "984": {"comment":"Otherwise put in"},
        "987": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's CLICK.","comment":"A click (CLICK)"},
        "991": {"synopsis":"Sets the editor's window up: IX = $F700 for 32 columns ($D73D), $FB00 otherwise; code $0E\nprinted in that window (ROM 0's WIN_PRINT_A); then IX = $D7DD.\nExit: IX = $D7DD.","comment":"A = the width"},
        "994": {"comment":"32 columns?"},
        "996": {"comment":"IX = the 32-column window"},
        "1002": {"comment":"IX = the other window"},
        "1006": {"synopsis":"Code $0E to the window at IX.","comment":"Code $0E to it (WIN_PRINT_A)"},
        "1011": {"comment":"IX = the editor's window block"},
        "1016": {"synopsis":"Handles character A as a key in the editor, from NextZXOS ROM 1's $0A33 and $0A7E (through\nits CALL_ALT_ROM0; $0D, and characters of the Calculator's result): in bank 7 on the\nalternate stack, $D5B7 bit 3 cleared, the cursor shown, stream 2 selected (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT), the key handled (KEY_DISPATCH), bit 3 cleared again, the cursor taken off.\nEntry: A = the code. Keeps DE and HL."},
        "1018": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the alternate stack"},
        "1019": {"comment":"The line not changed"},
        "1024": {"comment":"The code kept"},
        "1025": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1028": {"comment":"Stream 2 (STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "1033": {"comment":"The code back"},
        "1034": {"comment":"Handled as a key"},
        "1037": {"comment":"The line not changed"},
        "1042": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "1045": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "1049": {"synopsis":"Key $07 (EDIT): the cursor off; menu ($D5B8) / 4 + 2 run (ROM 0's RUN_MENU: 2 in mode 0, 3\nin mode 4, 4 in mode 8); the columns applied again; carry; IX = $D7DD; the cursor shown.","comment":"The cursor off"},
        "1052": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "1055": {"comment":"The mode / 4"},
        "1057": {"comment":"Menu 2, 3 or 4"},
        "1062": {"comment":"The columns applied (COLUMNS_APPLY)"},
