        "2327": {"comment":"State 1: the rows above the window"},
        "2328": {"comment":"DE = the stack's first row"},
        "2331": {"comment":"HL = its flags byte"},
        "2336": {"synopsis":"Sets E_PPC to the number of the program line the cursor's row C belongs to: the line's first\nrow (LINE_FIRST_ROW) carries the number after its flags byte, high byte first, when its\nflags\nbit 4 is set (a row from the program); otherwise E_PPC is left. Also pushed as the way out\nby\nROW_UP and ROW_DOWN, and called from KEY_ENTER.\nKeeps AF, BC.\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "2338": {"comment":"The line's first row"},
        "2341": {"comment":"A row from the program?"},
        "2345": {"comment":"D, E = its line number, high byte first"},
        "2349": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "2353": {"synopsis":"BC and AF back."},
        "2356": {"synopsis":"Gives the next character of the line being entered, read from the editor's rows (from\n$16A8). The reader's state at $D5AF (bit 7: count the characters in $D5B5; bits 0-3: 1 the\nrows above the window, 2 the window, 4 the rows below, 8 done), column $D5B0, row $D5B1; the\nstate's routine from ROWS_CHAR_TABLE. Codes 1-$1F come back changed as the row drawing\n($1264) changes them; 0 (the line's end) as $0D.\nExit: A = the character.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "2359": {"comment":"Counting the places?"},
        "2363": {"comment":"One place more"},
        "2370": {"synopsis":"State, column and row; the state's routine.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "2373": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "2375": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "2377": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "2379": {"comment":"The state's number"},
