        "5685": {"comment":"The space into the buffer"},
        "5688": {"comment":"Full"},
        "5690": {"comment":"The buffer holds a space"},
        "5695": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5697": {"synopsis":"Anything else: the buffer written as text (TOK_FLUSH); the character taken again."},
        "5700": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "5702": {"synopsis":"With a space in the word buffer ($D7F4 not 0): the characters before it written as text\n(TOK_OUT) and the rest moved to the buffer's start ($D7F3 = its length); a buffer that ends\nwith its space ($A0) is emptied.\nExit: carry when done; no carry, nothing done, when $D7F4 is 0. Keeps BC.","comment":"A space in the buffer?"},
        "5706": {"comment":"No: no carry"},
        "5708": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5711": {"synopsis":"One character written; the space reached?","comment":"The place kept"},
        "5718": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "5719": {"comment":"The character written"},
        "5721": {"comment":"The end ($A0)?"},
        "5725": {"comment":"The space?"},
        "5727": {"comment":"On to the space"},
        "5729": {"comment":"The rest to the buffer's start"},
        "5732": {"comment":"A counts the characters moved"},
        "5733": {"synopsis":"One character moved, up to the one with bit 7."},
        "5734": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "5736": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "5740": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5741": {"comment":"$D7F3 = the count"},
        "5743": {"synopsis":"BC back; the buffer emptied."},
        "5744": {"synopsis":"State bit 0 cleared; the buffer empty.","comment":"The state"},
        "5747": {"comment":"Not in a word"},
        "5749": {"comment":"Length 0"},
        "5750": {"synopsis":"$D7F3 = A, the length; no space in it ($D7F4 = 0)."},
        "5753": {"comment":"No space in it"},
        "5757": {"synopsis":"$D7F5 bit 4 cleared: no word passed as text.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The state"},
        "5760": {"comment":"Not passing a word"},
        "5764": {"synopsis":"Writes the word buffer as text (TOK_OUT for each character, up to the one with bit 7) and\nempties it (TOK_BUF_RESET). Keeps BC.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "5765": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5768": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"The character"},
        "5776": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "5781": {"comment":"The buffer emptied"},
        "5783": {"synopsis":"The next character in B and its class in C, $D7F7 counted: from the banked buffer\n(TOK_GET_BANK) when $D7FB is 1, from the editor's rows (ROWS_READ_CHAR, $0934) when 0, from\nmemory (TOK_GET_MEM) when $FF. Class 6 a letter, 2 '#' or '$', 3 a space, 1 anything else.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"One more character read"},
        "5790": {"comment":"Where from?"},
        "5793": {"comment":"$FF: memory"},
        "5797": {"comment":"1: the banked buffer"},
        "5800": {"comment":"0: the editor's rows (ROWS_READ_CHAR, $0934)"},
        "5803": {"synopsis":"B = the character; its class."},
        "5804": {"comment":"Class 1 for a start"},
        "5806": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "5810": {"comment":"Lower case for the test"},
        "5812": {"comment":"Not a letter: 1"},
        "5815": {"comment":"Not a letter: 1"},
        "5818": {"comment":"A letter"},
        "5821": {"synopsis":"Below 'A': '#' or '$' 2, a space 3, else 1.","comment":"2"},
        "5822": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "5825": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "5828": {"comment":"3"},
        "5829": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "5832": {"comment":"Else 1"},
        "5835": {"synopsis":"From memory: ($D7FE) characters at ($D7FC), read with bank 0; ENTER when none are left.","comment":"Characters left"},
        "5840": {"comment":"None: ENTER"},
        "5844": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "5848": {"comment":"The place"},
        "5851": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5852": {"comment":"The character"},
        "5854": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5855": {"comment":"The place moved on"},
        "5858": {"comment":"Classed"},
        "5860": {"synopsis":"Adds character B to the word buffer ($D7E5, up to 9 characters, $D7F3 the length), the last\none marked with bit 7.\nExit: carry; no carry (Z) when it is full.","comment":"Full?"},
        "5863": {"comment":"Full: Z, no carry"},
        "5866": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5869": {"comment":"HL = the next place"},
        "5871": {"comment":"The first character?"},
        "5874": {"comment":"Bit 7 off the one before"},
        "5878": {"synopsis":"B stored with bit 7 set; the length + 1."},
        "5879": {"comment":"The last now"},
        "5881": {"comment":"One more"},
        "5887": {"synopsis":"Writes A, joining a '<' or '>' with the character after it: either is held in $D7F9; then <<\ngives $8C, <= $C7, <> $C9, >> $8D, >= $C8, and anything else writes the held one first.\nInside quotes or a comment ($D7F5 bits 1 and 3) A goes straight on (TOK_PUT); THEN ($CB) or\n':' ends a dot command and starts a statement ($D7F6 bit 2 cleared).\nExit: carry, except at the line's end (TOK_PUT).","comment":"The state"},
        "5890": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "5892": {"comment":"Yes: straight on"},
        "5894": {"comment":"In a comment?"},
        "5896": {"comment":"Yes: straight on"},
        "5898": {"comment":"THEN or ':': a new statement"},
        "5900": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "5902": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "5904": {"comment":"No"},
        "5906": {"synopsis":"The dot command over; written; a statement starts.","comment":"Not a dot command now"},
        "5911": {"comment":"At a statement's start"},
        "5917": {"synopsis":"Is a '<' or '>' held?","comment":"B = the character"},
        "5918": {"comment":"One held?"},
        "5923": {"comment":"Yes: a pair?"},
        "5925": {"comment":"None: hold a '>' or '<'"},
        "5926": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5930": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "5932": {"comment":"Neither: written"},
        "5934": {"synopsis":"Held; carry.","comment":"$D7F9 = it"},
        "5937": {"synopsis":"One is held: $D7F9 = 0; was it '<'?","comment":"Nothing held now"},
        "5939": {"comment":"'>' held?"},
        "5941": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5944": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5946": {"comment":"<>"},
        "5950": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "5952": {"comment":"<="},
        "5956": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "5958": {"comment":"<<"},
        "5962": {"comment":"Else '<' first"},
        "5964": {"synopsis":"The held character written first, then A.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "5965": {"comment":"The held one written"},
        "5969": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "5972": {"synopsis":"'>' held: then '=' gives >=, '>' >>.","comment":"'='?"},
        "5974": {"comment":">="},
        "5978": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5980": {"comment":"Else '>' first"},
        "5984": {"comment":">>"},
        "5986": {"synopsis":"The pair's token B written: a held space first (TOK_HELD_SPACE), then the token (TOK_PUT);\n$D7F6 bit 0 cleared.","comment":"The token kept"},
        "5987": {"comment":"A held space written first"},
        "5990": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "5991": {"comment":"Written"},
        "5994": {"comment":"$D7F6 bit 0 cleared"},
        "6000": {"synopsis":"Writes A, keeping the state: ENTER ends the line (in mode 1 a return from TOKENIZE,\nTOK_WRITE_FOUND; in mode 0 a held space written, then no carry); a quote flips $D7F5 bit 1;\nat a statement's start ';' makes $D7F5 8 (a comment), '.' 4 (a dot command; not when $D5B8\nis 4), and REM ($EA) sets $D7F6 bit 4. Everything else through TOK_SPACING.\nExit: carry.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "6004": {"comment":"ENTER: mode 1?"},
        "6007": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "6008": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "6012": {"comment":"Mode 1: out of TOKENIZE"},
        "6015": {"synopsis":"Writes the held space, if $D7F6 bit 1 says one is held (TOK_WRITE); then no carry.","comment":"A space held: written"},
        "6018": {"comment":"A space held?"},
        "6020": {"comment":"A space"},
        "6022": {"comment":"Written when held"},
        "6025": {"comment":"No carry: the line done"},
        "6027": {"synopsis":"B = A; a quote?"},
        "6028": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "6032": {"comment":"Past a statement's start?"},
        "6035": {"comment":"Bit 2: the statement started"},
        "6037": {"comment":"Yes: written"},
        "6039": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "6041": {"comment":"Bit 4 then"},
        "6043": {"comment":"';': a comment"},
        "6045": {"comment":"State 8"},
        "6047": {"comment":"'.': a dot command"},
        "6049": {"comment":"Not '.'"},
        "6051": {"comment":"Unless the state byte is 4"},
        "6054": {"comment":"A = 4: state 4"},
        "6057": {"comment":"Not 4: a dot command"},
        "6059": {"synopsis":"Written (TOK_SPACING); carry."},
        "6065": {"synopsis":"REM: $D7F6 bit 4."},
        "6067": {"comment":"Written"},
        "6069": {"synopsis":"';': state 8."},
        "6071": {"synopsis":"$D7F5 = A."},
        "6074": {"comment":"Written"},
        "6076": {"synopsis":"A quote: $D7F5 bit 1 flipped."},
        "6079": {"comment":"Bit 1 flipped"},
        "6081": {"comment":"Stored, written"},
        "6083": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_WRITE), dropping the spaces around keywords, with the flags in $D7F6 (bit 0 a\nkeyword was the last, bit 1 a space held, bit 2 the statement has started, bit 3 something\nwritten): a space after a keyword is dropped, the line's first space too; otherwise a space\nis held (bit 1) and one more written; a keyword ($81 up, outside quotes, comments and dot\ncommands) drops a held space, and after REM makes the state a comment; any other character\nwrites a held space first. A character other than a digit sets bits 2 and 3.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, B.","comment":"E = the character"},
        "6084": {"comment":"D = the flags"},
        "6089": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6091": {"comment":"Not a space"},
        "6093": {"comment":"After a keyword: dropped"},
        "6095": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared; dropped"},
        "6097": {"comment":"One held: this one written"},
        "6099": {"comment":"Bit 1: this one written"},
        "6101": {"comment":"Something written: held"},
        "6103": {"comment":"Bit 3: hold it"},
        "6105": {"comment":"At the line's start: bit 3 only"},
        "6106": {"comment":"The space dropped"},
        "6110": {"synopsis":"Bit 1: a space held."},
        "6111": {"comment":"Held"},
        "6113": {"synopsis":"$D7F6 = A.","comment":"The flags stored"},
        "6117": {"synopsis":"E written (TOK_WRITE).","comment":"A = the character"},
        "6120": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 cleared."},
        "6121": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "6123": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6125": {"synopsis":"Not a space: a digit?","comment":"A digit?"},
        "6131": {"comment":"Yes: the flags as they are"},
        "6133": {"synopsis":"Not a digit: bits 2 and 3 set."},
        "6135": {"comment":"Something written"},
        "6137": {"synopsis":"A keyword ($81 up)?","comment":"A keyword?"},
        "6139": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6141": {"synopsis":"A held space written first, then the character; bits 0 and 1 cleared.","comment":"A space held?"},
        "6144": {"comment":"Written first"},
        "6150": {"comment":"None held now"},
        "6152": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "6155": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "6157": {"synopsis":"A keyword, outside quotes, comments and dot commands?","comment":"The state"},
        "6161": {"comment":"Quotes, a dot command or a comment?"},
        "6163": {"comment":"Yes: as text"},
        "6165": {"comment":"After REM?"},
        "6170": {"comment":"Then the state a comment"},
        "6172": {"synopsis":"A held space dropped, bit 0 set; written."},
        "6174": {"comment":"A keyword the last"},
        "6176": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6179": {"comment":"Written"},
        "6181": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the place in $D7EE and moves it on. Mode 0 ($D7F2 = 0): one byte of room made\nthere with bank 0 (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE) and A stored. Mode 1: the place moves past the\nline's byte (and a number's hidden form) instead; on reaching X_PTR, BC = the characters\nread less those still in the word buffer, SP = $D7F0 and a return from TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "6182": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "6185": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "6189": {"comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "6191": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "6192": {"comment":"X_PTR reached?"},
        "6197": {"comment":"No"},
        "6199": {"comment":"BC = $D7F7 - $D7F3"},
        "6202": {"comment":"DE = the buffer's length"},
        "6205": {"comment":"Less the characters read"},
        "6210": {"comment":"BC = the place's count"},
        "6213": {"synopsis":"SP back: out of TOKENIZE.","comment":"Out of TOKENIZE"},
        "6218": {"synopsis":"Mode 1: past the byte, with bank 0; past a hidden number's six bytes.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6219": {"comment":"Past the byte"},
        "6221": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "6225": {"comment":"Its marker and five bytes"},
        "6231": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: room for one byte at HL, then A stored there.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6232": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "6233": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE"},
        "6236": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6237": {"comment":"Stored in the new byte"},
        "6238": {"comment":"The next place"},
        "6239": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; $D7EE = the next place.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6240": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6245": {"synopsis":"Looks the word in the buffer at $D7E5 up as a keyword, letters in either case, unless a word\nis being passed as text ($D7F5 bit 4):\n1. In ROM 3's table from RND's entry ($0096), through WORD_FIND at $D7B4 with ROM 3: codes\n$A5 up.\n2. In NEXT_KEYWORDS (codes $D0 up for WORD_FIND): its first 36 words give $81-$A4; the rest\nare other spellings, their tokens from ALIAS_TOKENS; one ending in '$' writes the token\n(TOK_OUT) and gives '$'.\nExit: carry and A = the token (or '$'); no carry when not found or passing.","comment":"The state"},
        "6248": {"comment":"Passing a word?"},
        "6250": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "6251": {"comment":"ROM 3's keywords from RND, code $A5"},
        "6256": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORD_FIND at $D7B4"},
        "6259": {"comment":"Found: carry, A = the token"},
        "6260": {"comment":"This ROM's, from code $D0"},
        "6265": {"comment":"WORD_FIND, this ROM's"},
        "6268": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "6269": {"comment":"$F4 up: another spelling"},
        "6271": {"comment":"$D0-$F3: a token"},
        "6273": {"comment":"BC = its number from $F4"},
        "6276": {"comment":"Its last character"},
        "6278": {"comment":"Its token from ALIAS_TOKENS"},
        "6281": {"comment":"HL = its token"},
        "6282": {"comment":"Ending in '$'?"},
        "6284": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "6285": {"comment":"No '$'"},
        "6287": {"comment":"The token written; then '$'"},
        "6290": {"comment":"Then '$'"},
        "6292": {"synopsis":"Carry: found."},
        "6294": {"synopsis":"$D0-$F3: tokens $81-$A4.","comment":"A = the token"},
        "6298": {"synopsis":"Tokenises BC characters at DE (read with bank 0, TOK_GET_MEM) into a line at E_LINE\n(TOKENIZE_GO with A = $FF, mode 0).\nExit: BC = ($D7EE), the place written, less STKBOT - 1 as it was on entry; bank 0. No\nreference to it was found in this page or in NextZXOS.","comment":"STKBOT - 1 kept"},
        "6301": {"comment":"STKBOT - 1"},
        "6303": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "6304": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6305": {"comment":"The text and its length"},
        "6308": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "6312": {"comment":"From memory, mode 0"},
        "6314": {"comment":"Mode 0"},
        "6319": {"comment":"BC = the end less it"},
        "6322": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6323": {"comment":"DE = STKBOT - 1"},
        "6325": {"comment":"BC = the end less it"},
        "6330": {"synopsis":"IDE_TOKENISER with B = 0: the work space cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_WS), an ENTER put at E_LINE\n(ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE), the text in the banked buffer tokenised before it (TOKENIZE_RUN,\nmode 0), then NextZXOS ROM 1's code at $09F3 (inside LINE_ENTER) run with HL = $09E9 and the\nDivMMC memory's byte at $32FF set to 0 round it (DMMC_BYTE_SWAP). With no report (ERR_NR bit\n7 set) and at most $04FB characters: HL = E_LINE, BC = the line's length (TOKAPI_LENGTH),\nNZ. Otherwise the text is walked again to X_PTR, the report's place (mode 1): Z, DE = the\ncount returned less 1.\nExit: carry; bank 0.","comment":"The buffer's address kept"},
        "6331": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "6334": {"comment":"The workspace's HL kept, below it"},
        "6336": {"comment":"An ENTER at E_LINE"},
        "6339": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE"},
        "6342": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "6345": {"comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "6350": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's address"},
        "6351": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6352": {"comment":"Its address again"},
        "6355": {"comment":"The DivMMC byte $32FF = 0, B = it"},
        "6359": {"comment":"The old byte kept"},
        "6360": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6361": {"comment":"ROM 1's $09F3: the line checked"},
        "6364": {"comment":"ROM 1's $09F3"},
        "6367": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6368": {"comment":"The DivMMC byte back"},
        "6372": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "6376": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6377": {"comment":"DE = the workspace's HL kept"},
        "6378": {"comment":"ERR_NR bit 7: no report?"},
        "6382": {"comment":"No report"},
        "6384": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "6385": {"comment":"Mode 1: to the report's place"},
        "6387": {"comment":"TOKENIZE_RUN in mode 1"},
        "6390": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "6391": {"synopsis":"Z: DE = the characters before the error; the work space cleared.","comment":"The count less 1"},
        "6396": {"comment":"DE = the count less 1"},
        "6397": {"comment":"Z"},
        "6400": {"synopsis":"No report: more than $04FB characters is an error too.","comment":"The limit"},
        "6404": {"comment":"More characters than that?"},
        "6406": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "6408": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS; BC = its HL now less DE (its HL at the start, kept on the stack), the\nline's length; HL = E_LINE; carry."},
        "6411": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6416": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6421": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE with A = 1 (the banked buffer, its work space cleared by CLEAR_WS) and mode D, bank\n7 round it; bank 0 on exit.","comment":"The banked buffer"},
        "6423": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6427": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6429": {"synopsis":"Swaps A with the DivMMC memory's byte at $32FF: DMMC_SWAP_CODE copied to $D7B4 and run there\n(DivMMC memory paged in by port $E3 = $80 while it reads and writes).\nExit: B = the old byte, A = 0. From NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_OWN ($0E1E) too.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6432": {"comment":"To $D7B4"},
        "6435": {"comment":"Run there on the RET"},
        "6441": {"comment":"The byte's address in that memory"},
        "6444": {"comment":"C = the new byte"},
        "6445": {"comment":"A = $80 for port $E3"},
        "6447": {"comment":"DMMC_SWAP_CODE at $D7B4"},
        "6448": {"synopsis":"Run at $D7B4 (DMMC_BYTE_SWAP): port $E3 = A ($80, the DivMMC memory paged in), B = (HL),\n(HL) = C, port $E3 = 0.","comment":"The DivMMC memory paged in"},
        "6450": {"comment":"B = the old byte"},
        "6451": {"comment":"The new one written"},
        "6452": {"comment":"Paged out"},
        "6456": {"synopsis":"The next character from the banked buffer: ($D7FC) with the bank in $D7FA paged into MMU 1,\nthen the ROM back (MMU 1 = $FF); $D7FC moved on.\nExit: NZ.","comment":"The place"},
        "6459": {"comment":"The buffer's bank"},
        "6462": {"comment":"In MMU 1"},
        "6465": {"comment":"The character"},
        "6467": {"comment":"The ROM back"},
        "6471": {"comment":"The place moved on"},
        "6474": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "6476": {"synopsis":"Resets the expansion of a line ($D767, the place in the program, and $D769, the place in a\ntext, both 0), then RAM_ROUTINES.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No text pending"},
        "6479": {"comment":"No line"},
        "6485": {"synopsis":"Copies KEYWORD_TEXT and WORD_FIND ($1961-$19C5, 101 bytes) to $D776-$D7DA, where they run\nwith ROM 3 or this ROM paged in.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT and WORD_FIND"},
        "6488": {"comment":"To $D776"},
        "6491": {"comment":"101 bytes"},
        "6497": {"synopsis":"Run at $D776: puts the text of the A-th string of the table at DE (each ended by bit 7) in\nthe buffer at $D76B for EXPAND_NEXT ($D769 = $D76B): a space first when the word starts with\na letter and $D765 bit 0 is clear, then the string, then a space ($A0, the last) unless it\nends with '<', '=' or '>' (bit 7 then on its last character). $D765 = 0.\nExit: HL past the buffer's text.","comment":"B = the strings to pass over"},
        "6498": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6499": {"synopsis":"Any more to pass over?"},
        "6501": {"synopsis":"Up to the end of this string (bit 7)."},
        "6502": {"comment":"Up to the one with bit 7"},
        "6507": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "6510": {"synopsis":"The string reached: a space first?","comment":"$D765"},
        "6513": {"comment":"Bit 0: no space first"},
        "6515": {"comment":"$D765 = 0"},
        "6517": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "6520": {"comment":"Its text given first"},
        "6523": {"comment":"No space first"},
        "6525": {"comment":"A letter first?"},
        "6530": {"comment":"A space first"},
        "6534": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the one with bit 7.","comment":"A character"},
        "6536": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "6539": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "6543": {"comment":"The last character"},
        "6546": {"comment":"'<', '=' or '>'?"},
        "6552": {"comment":"Yes: no space after"},
        "6553": {"synopsis":"Its last character without bit 7, then $A0.","comment":"Its bit 7 off"},
        "6556": {"comment":"Then a space with bit 7"},
        "6559": {"synopsis":"Run at $D7B4: compares the word at $D7E5 (its last character with bit 7 set) with the\nstrings at HL, each ended by bit 7, B the code of the first: lower-case letters in the word\ncount as capitals.\nExit: carry, A = B = the code of the one that matches, HL past it; no carry when none does\nbefore B passes $FF.","comment":"The word"},
        "6562": {"synopsis":"The word's next character, a letter as a capital.","comment":"The word's character"},
        "6565": {"comment":"Lower case?"},
        "6570": {"comment":"As a capital"},
        "6572": {"synopsis":"The same as the string's?","comment":"The same as the string's?"},
        "6573": {"comment":"No"},
        "6575": {"comment":"Both moved on"},
        "6577": {"comment":"The word's last?"},
        "6581": {"comment":"Matched: carry"},
        "6584": {"synopsis":"No match: the next string's code; past $FF, none found.","comment":"The next code"},
        "6585": {"comment":"Past $FF: none"},
        "6587": {"synopsis":"Past the end of this string.","comment":"To the end of this string"},
        "6593": {"comment":"Compared again"},
        "6595": {"synopsis":"None found: no carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "6596": {"synopsis":"A = B.","comment":"A = the code"},
        "6598": {"synopsis":"NextBASIC's own keywords, each ended by bit 7: tokens $81-$A4, TIME, PRIVATE, IF, ENDIF,\nEXIT, REF, PEEK$, REG, DPOKE, DPEEK, MOD, <<, >>, UNTIL, ERROR, ON, DEFPROC, ENDPROC, PROC,\nLOCAL, DRIVER, WHILE, REPEAT, ELSE, REMOUNT, BANK, TILE, LAYER, PALETTE, SPRITE, PWD, CD,\nMKDIR, RMDIR, SPECTRUM, PLAY; then 12 other spellings for ALIAS_TOKENS: LS, DIR, GOTO,\nGOSUB, DEFFN, OPEN#, CLOSE#, RAND, CONT, ERROR$, TIME$, USR$. Read by EXPAND_NEXT (through\nKEYWORD_TEXT, code - $81) and KEYWORD_LOOKUP (WORD_FIND, B = $D0 for the first)."},
        "6817": {"synopsis":"The tokens of NEXT_KEYWORDS' last 12 words, read by KEYWORD_LOOKUP: LS and DIR $CF (CAT),\nGOTO $EC, GOSUB $ED, DEFFN $CE, OPEN# $D3, CLOSE# $D4, RAND $F9, CONT $E8, ERROR$ $8F, TIME$\n$81 and USR$ $C0 (the last three followed by '$')."},
        "6829": {"synopsis":"Prints program lines through RST $28, from the line at HL in bank ($5B65) on (NextZXOS ROM\n1's LIST_FIND, $362A): for each, BREAK tested (NextZXOS ROM 1's BREAK_STOP), the line copied\nto $5CB6 (ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY), its number and text expanded (LINE_START_NUM,\nEXPAND_NEXT) and printed, a 0 as a space. Ends at a line number from $2800 up (the program's\nend).\nExit: bank 7.","comment":"The line's address kept"},
        "6830": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6831": {"comment":"The expansion reset"},
        "6834": {"synopsis":"One line: BREAK, then a copy of it at $5CB6.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6835": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP"},
        "6838": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "6841": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "6843": {"comment":"ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY: HL = $5CB6"},
        "6846": {"comment":"Past the program's end?"},
        "6847": {"comment":"A number from $2800 up?"},
        "6849": {"comment":"DE = the line's address"},
        "6850": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "6851": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6852": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6856": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "6859": {"comment":"The next line's address kept"},
        "6860": {"comment":"Past its header and text"},
        "6865": {"comment":"The next line kept"},
        "6866": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6867": {"comment":"HL = the copy + 1"},
        "6869": {"comment":"Its number as text first"},
        "6872": {"synopsis":"The next character; none left: the next line."},
        "6875": {"comment":"None left: the next line"},
        "6877": {"comment":"Bank 0 while printing"},
        "6878": {"comment":"0?"},
        "6881": {"comment":"A space"},
        "6883": {"synopsis":"Printed (RST $28); bank 7; the next."},
        "6884": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6885": {"comment":"The next"},
        "6887": {"synopsis":"Counts the characters the line at HL expands to (its number and text; LINE_START_NUM, then\nEXPAND_NEXT until none is left). From NextZXOS ROM 1's $3FE3.\nExit: HL = the count; bank 0.","comment":"The line's address kept"},
        "6888": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6892": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6894": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6897": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6901": {"comment":"The count, one short"},
        "6904": {"synopsis":"One character counted."},
        "6909": {"comment":"One more"},
        "6910": {"comment":"While characters come"},
        "6912": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6914": {"synopsis":"Renumbers program lines: the lines numbered from BC to DE get the numbers HL, HL + IX, ...\n1. BC, DE, HL and IX kept at $5CA4, $5CA6, $5C9E and $5CA0 (in MEMBOT).\n2. The lines counted (RENUM_COUNT); none: no carry.\n3. The last new number (RENUM_NEW_NUM) must fit and be below 9999; no other line may lie\nbetween the first and the last new number (RENUM_CHECK_LOOP): otherwise no carry.\n4. The line numbers in GO TO, GO SUB and the other commands of RENUM_TOKENS changed\n(RENUM_REFS), then the lines' own numbers written (RENUM_NUM_LOOP).\n5. The program put back in order (RENUM_SORT).\nFrom LINE_CMD and NextZXOS ROM 1's $2AEF.\nEntry: BC = the first line, DE = the last, HL = the new first number, IX = the step.\nExit: carry when done.","comment":"$5CA4 = the first line"},
        "6918": {"comment":"$5CA6 = the last line"},
        "6922": {"comment":"$5C9E = the new first number"},
        "6925": {"comment":"$5CA0 = the step"},
        "6929": {"comment":"BC = the lines to renumber"},
        "6934": {"comment":"None: no carry"},
        "6935": {"comment":"HL = the last new number"},
        "6938": {"comment":"Too big: no carry"},
        "6940": {"comment":"9999"},
        "6945": {"comment":"9999 or more: no carry"},
        "6946": {"comment":"HL = the last new number + 1"},
        "6949": {"comment":"HL = the new first number"},
        "6952": {"comment":"The first line at or after it (FIND_LINE)"},
        "6955": {"comment":"BC = its number"},
        "6959": {"comment":"DE = its length word"},
        "6962": {"comment":"Above the new numbers?"},
        "6964": {"comment":"Then no clash"},
        "6968": {"comment":"Before the first line renumbered?"},
        "6975": {"comment":"Then a clash: no carry"},
        "6976": {"synopsis":"One line of the program inside the new numbers' range: must be one of those renumbered\n(not above ($5CA6)); then the next line."},
        "6977": {"comment":"After the last one renumbered?"},
        "6985": {"comment":"Then a clash: no carry"},
        "6986": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "6992": {"comment":"BC = its number"},
        "6998": {"comment":"The program's end?"},
        "7003": {"comment":"Still among the new numbers?"},
        "7009": {"synopsis":"Room checked: the references changed (RENUM_REFS); HL = the first line renumbered, DE = the\nnew first number.","comment":"The references changed"},
        "7012": {"comment":"The first line renumbered"},
        "7018": {"comment":"DE = the new first number"},
        "7022": {"synopsis":"One line: its number BC; above ($5CA6), done; otherwise DE written as its number (high byte\nfirst), DE + the step, the next line."},
        "7026": {"comment":"Above the last one renumbered?"},
        "7033": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "7035": {"comment":"The new number written, high byte first"},
        "7041": {"comment":"DE + the step"},
        "7047": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "7051": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "7054": {"synopsis":"Puts the program back in order: from PROG, each line whose number is not above the one\nbefore it is moved to its place: copied to $3700 in RAM page $0F (MMU 1), taken out (ROM 3's\nRECLAIM), room made where it belongs (FIND_LINE, MAKE_ROOM) and copied back. A line of more\nthan $0900 bytes stops it.\nExit: carry at the program's end; no carry for a line too long.","comment":"No number before the first line"},
        "7057": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7060": {"synopsis":"One line: BC = its number, HL its length word; the program's end ($28 up) returns carry."},
        "7064": {"comment":"The program's end: carry"},
        "7069": {"comment":"Above the one before it?"},
        "7075": {"comment":"Yes: in order"},
        "7077": {"comment":"IX = its number"},
        "7080": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "7083": {"comment":"HL = the line's start"},
        "7086": {"comment":"BC = the whole line"},
        "7091": {"comment":"More than $0900 bytes?"},
        "7098": {"comment":"Then no carry"},
        "7102": {"comment":"RAM page $0F at $2000-$3FFF"},
        "7106": {"comment":"The line copied to $3700"},
        "7111": {"comment":"The ROM back in MMU 1"},
        "7119": {"comment":"The line taken out (RECLAIM)"},
        "7122": {"comment":"HL = its number"},
        "7125": {"comment":"Where it belongs (FIND_LINE)"},
        "7130": {"comment":"Room made (MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "7134": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "7141": {"comment":"Copied back from $3700"},
        "7152": {"comment":"HL = the next line at the old place"},
        "7156": {"synopsis":"In order: DE = its number; on to the next line.","comment":"DE = this number"},
        "7158": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7162": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "7165": {"synopsis":"RENUM_STMT's 8 tokens that take a line number: LINE ($CA), LIST ($F0), LLIST ($E1), GO TO\n($EC), GO SUB ($ED), RESTORE ($E5), RUN ($F7) and $85 (EXIT in this page's keyword table)."},
        "7173": {"synopsis":"Changes the line numbers that statements refer to, all through the program: for each line\n$5C9C = its length word's address, each statement through RENUM_STMT, until VARS.","comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7176": {"synopsis":"The next line: $5C9C = its length word, HL its text."},
        "7178": {"comment":"Kept at $5C9C"},
        "7181": {"comment":"HL = its text"},
        "7183": {"synopsis":"One statement; the line's ENTER ends the line."},
        "7186": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "7191": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "7198": {"comment":"Not yet: the next line"},
        "7201": {"synopsis":"A = the next character at HL that is not a space or a control code, HL past it; ENTER ($0D)\nand the number marker ($0E) are given as they are.\nExit: Z for ENTER or $0E."},
        "7205": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "7208": {"comment":"A number's hidden form"},
        "7211": {"comment":"Spaces and control codes passed"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Looks through one statement for line numbers to change: after the statement's first\ncharacter (ELSE, $98, is passed first), a statement starting with token $9A (BANK), REM\n($EA), INPUT ($EE), $9E (SPRITE), ';' or '.' is only gone through (B bit 0). Text in quotes\n(B bit 1) and numbers' hidden forms are passed. A token of RENUM_TOKENS is looked at by\nRENUM_TOKEN.\nExit: A = the character that ended it (ENTER, ':' or THEN).","comment":"B = 0"},
        "7216": {"comment":"The statement's first character"},
        "7219": {"comment":"ELSE ($98) passed"},
        "7227": {"comment":"BANK"},
        "7231": {"comment":"REM"},
        "7235": {"comment":"INPUT"},
        "7239": {"comment":"SPRITE"},
        "7243": {"comment":"';'"},
        "7247": {"comment":"'.': a dot command"},
        "7251": {"synopsis":"B bit 0: the statement only gone through."},
        "7252": {"synopsis":"The next character."},
        "7255": {"synopsis":"A quote flips B bit 1."},
        "7257": {"comment":"Not a quote"},
        "7259": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "7261": {"comment":"Then out"},
        "7265": {"comment":"Else in"},
        "7267": {"synopsis":"Inside quotes: the next character."},
        "7269": {"comment":"Inside quotes: passed"},
        "7271": {"comment":"A number's hidden form?"},
        "7275": {"comment":"Passed"},
        "7281": {"synopsis":"The statement's end (THEN, ENTER or ':', $273E)?"},
        "7284": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "7285": {"comment":"Only gone through?"},
        "7289": {"comment":"C = the character"},
        "7290": {"comment":"RENUM_TOKENS"},
        "7293": {"comment":"8 tokens"},
        "7295": {"synopsis":"One of RENUM_TOKENS' 8 tokens?"},
        "7302": {"comment":"Not one: the next character"},
        "7304": {"synopsis":"A token that takes a line number: what follows it. AT ($AC), token $93 (PROC), '@' (a label)\nand '#' after GO TO are not line numbers; '%' starts a number written as text\n(RENUM_REF_INT);\nthe statement's end (ENTER, ':') means no number. A number with its hidden form goes to\nRENUM_REF_FP; anything else is an expression (RENUM_REF_EXPR).","comment":"The place after the token kept"},
        "7305": {"comment":"What follows it"},
        "7308": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "7312": {"comment":"PROC?"},
        "7316": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "7320": {"comment":"After GO TO?"},
        "7323": {"comment":"No: an expression"},
        "7325": {"synopsis":"Not a line number: the place dropped."},
        "7326": {"synopsis":"B = 0, on through the statement."},
        "7330": {"synopsis":"Not $AC, $93 or '#': '%' or '@'?"},
        "7332": {"comment":"'%': a number in text"},
        "7334": {"comment":"'@': a label"},
        "7338": {"comment":"The statement's end?"},
        "7343": {"comment":"Nothing follows: done with the statement"},
        "7345": {"synopsis":"The number's text: digits, '.' and 'e' passed up to its hidden form ($0E).","comment":"The hidden form?"},
        "7349": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "7354": {"comment":"'.'?"},
        "7358": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "7360": {"comment":"'e'?"},
        "7364": {"synopsis":"Past this character."},
        "7369": {"synopsis":"An expression, not a number: the 2 bytes '?' and the character after the token are put in\nplace of that character (RENUM_REPLACE with 1 byte replaced by 2), so that the line shows a\nreference that could not be renumbered."},
        "7371": {"comment":"H = the character after the token"},
        "7372": {"comment":"L = '?'"},
        "7374": {"comment":"'?' and it at $5CA8"},
        "7377": {"comment":"Two bytes in place of one"},
        "7385": {"synopsis":"'%': digits must follow (otherwise RENUM_REF_EXPR); their value in DE."},
        "7388": {"comment":"A digit must follow"},
        "7396": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "7399": {"synopsis":"One digit: DE = DE x 10 + it."},
        "7401": {"comment":"Not a digit: the end"},
        "7407": {"comment":"DE x 10 + the digit"},
        "7422": {"synopsis":"BC = the value; HL back on the character after the digits."},
        "7427": {"synopsis":"A number with its hidden form: put on the calculator stack (ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER) and taken\ninto BC (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC; 9999 when it does not fit).","comment":"The number onto the calculator stack"},
        "7431": {"comment":"BC = it (FP_TO_BC)"},
        "7434": {"comment":"It fits"},
        "7436": {"comment":"Otherwise 9999"},
        "7439": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "7440": {"synopsis":"After the number only the statement's end may follow (otherwise RENUM_REF_EXPR); the old\ntext's length; its new text made (RENUM_NEW_TEXT); when the line is not renumbered, the old\ntext is left."},
        "7443": {"comment":"The statement's end next?"},
        "7446": {"comment":"No: an expression"},
        "7448": {"comment":"HL = the end of the old text"},
        "7452": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "7455": {"comment":"The new text at $5CA8"},
        "7459": {"comment":"Renumbered: replaced"},
        "7462": {"comment":"Otherwise past the old text"},
        "7466": {"synopsis":"Replaces DE bytes (the old text) at the place on the stack by HL bytes from $5CA8: the\nline's\nlength word at ($5C9C) changed by the difference, the bytes taken out (ROM 3's RECLAIM) or\nroom made (RENUM_GROW)."},
        "7468": {"comment":"Old less new"},
        "7470": {"comment":"The new one longer"},
        "7472": {"comment":"BC = the bytes fewer"},
        "7474": {"synopsis":"BC = the bytes to take out (none: RENUM_REPL_COPY)."},
        "7480": {"comment":"Those bytes taken out"},
        "7483": {"synopsis":"The line's length word less BC; the new text copied in from $5CA8; on through the\nstatement."},
        "7484": {"comment":"HL = the line's length word"},
        "7492": {"comment":"Less BC"},
        "7495": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7500": {"comment":"The new text"},
        "7503": {"comment":"Copied in"},
        "7509": {"synopsis":"The new text is longer: BC = the extra bytes; with room for them and 100 more below the\nstack, room made (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM) and RENUM_REPL_COPY with BC = minus the extra bytes."},
        "7510": {"comment":"IX = minus the extra bytes"},
        "7518": {"comment":"BC = the extra bytes"},
        "7519": {"comment":"STKEND + them"},
        "7526": {"comment":"And 100 more"},
        "7533": {"comment":"Below the stack?"},
        "7542": {"comment":"Room made (MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "7547": {"synopsis":"No room: only a '?' put in at $5CA8 for the old text.","comment":"Just '?'"},
        "7553": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "7566": {"synopsis":"The new text for a reference to line BC: the line it leads to (the first numbered BC or\nmore,\nROM 3's FIND_LINE); when that line is one of those renumbered (($5CA4) to ($5CA6)), its new\nnumber (its place among them, RENUM_COUNT_TO, then RENUM_NEW_NUM) written at $5CA8 as '%'\nand up to four digits (no leading zeros).\nExit: no carry and HL = the text's length; carry when the line is not renumbered."},
        "7568": {"comment":"The line it leads to (FIND_LINE)"},
        "7571": {"comment":"BC = that line's number"},
        "7574": {"comment":"Before the first renumbered?"},
        "7581": {"comment":"Then not changed: carry"},
        "7582": {"comment":"After the last renumbered?"},
        "7589": {"comment":"BC = its place among them"},
        "7592": {"comment":"HL = its new number"},
        "7595": {"comment":"The text at $5CA8"},
        "7599": {"comment":"'%' first"},
        "7602": {"comment":"Thousands"},
        "7608": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "7614": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "7619": {"comment":"The units"},
        "7624": {"comment":"HL past the text"},
        "7626": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "7629": {"synopsis":"HL = the new number of the BC-th line renumbered: ($5CA0) x (BC - 1) (ROM 3's MUL_HL_DE) +\n($5C9E).\nExit: carry when it does not fit.","comment":"HL = the step"},
        "7632": {"comment":"DE = BC - 1"},
        "7635": {"comment":"HL = their product (MUL_HL_DE)"},
        "7638": {"comment":"Too big: carry"},
        "7639": {"comment":"Plus the new first number"},
        "7645": {"synopsis":"One decimal digit of HL, BC being minus its place's value, written after DE as '0' + the\ndigit; a 0 with nothing but '%' before it is left out."},
        "7646": {"synopsis":"BC added while it fits; A counts."},
        "7652": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "7654": {"comment":"Not 0: written"},
        "7656": {"comment":"Nothing but '%' yet?"},
        "7660": {"synopsis":"The digit C written at DE + 1."},
        "7661": {"comment":"'0' + the digit"},
        "7666": {"synopsis":"RENUM_COUNT_TO up to the last line, ($5CA6).","comment":"BC = the last line"},
        "7670": {"synopsis":"Counts the program lines from line ($5CA4) up to line BC.\nExit: BC = the count, HL = the line after them.","comment":"The limit kept"},
        "7671": {"comment":"The first line renumbered"},
        "7674": {"comment":"The first line at or after it"},
        "7677": {"comment":"None counted yet"},
        "7680": {"synopsis":"One line: DE = its number; above the limit, done.","comment":"DE = its number"},
        "7684": {"comment":"HL = the limit"},
        "7686": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "7690": {"comment":"HL = the line after them"},
        "7692": {"synopsis":"Counted; the next line (ROM 3's NEXT_LINE)."},
        "7694": {"comment":"One more"},
        "7695": {"comment":"The next line (NEXT_LINE)"},
        "7700": {"synopsis":"LINE (renumbering), reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LINE (word $DE14: the\nalternate ROM with ROM select 0). Two numbers, the new first number and the step; with TO\n($CC) after LINE, two more first (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8): the first and last line to\nrenumber, otherwise 1 and 9999. Only as a direct command (ROM 1's NEED_DIRECT). Each number\nmust be 1-9999 (LINE_TAKE_NUM). Then RENUMBER; when that fails, error code $0F through ROM\n1's ERROR_128_A.\nEntry: A = the character after LINE.","comment":"The character after LINE kept"},
        "7703": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "7707": {"comment":"Past TO, two numbers (NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "7710": {"synopsis":"Checking syntax ends here ($2747); running: direct commands only.","comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7713": {"comment":"A direct command only (NEED_DIRECT)"},
        "7716": {"comment":"The step"},
        "7720": {"comment":"The new first number"},
        "7724": {"comment":"TO given?"},
        "7729": {"comment":"Otherwise lines 1"},
        "7732": {"comment":"To 9999"},
        "7737": {"comment":"The last line"},
        "7741": {"comment":"The first line"},
        "7745": {"synopsis":"HL = the new first number, IX = the step; RENUMBER.","comment":"HL = the new first number"},
        "7746": {"comment":"IX = the step"},
        "7748": {"comment":"Renumbered"},
        "7751": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7752": {"comment":"Failed: error code $0F"},
        "7757": {"synopsis":"BC = a number off the calculator stack (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD), which must be 1-9999; otherwise\nerror code $0A through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.","comment":"BC = the number (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "7760": {"comment":"0?"},
        "7764": {"comment":"Not above 9999?"},
        "7770": {"synopsis":"0 or above 9999: error code $0A.","comment":"Error code $0A"},
        "7775": {"synopsis":"LINE NEW, reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry (word $DE5F): up to two numbers, a\nfirst\nline number and a step ('LINE NEW', 'LINE NEW a', 'LINE NEW a,b' or 'LINE NEW ,b'; a missing\none is 0). When running: in bank 7, $D750 = the step (10 for 0) and $D74E = the number\n(E_PPC\nfor 0) with bit 15 set, the next number AUTO_LINE_NUM types in.\nEntry: A = the character after NEW.","comment":"',' first?"},
        "7779": {"comment":"No first number: 0 (when running)"},
        "7782": {"comment":"Past the ','"},
        "7787": {"synopsis":"A first number (ROM 1's NUM_OR_ZERO_A); then the statement's end or ','.","comment":"The first number, or 0"},
        "7790": {"comment":"The character at CH_ADD"},
        "7793": {"comment":"The statement's end?"},
        "7798": {"comment":"Otherwise ',' must follow"},
        "7802": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7805": {"synopsis":"The step (ROM 1's NUM_OR_ZERO_A); checking syntax ends here.","comment":"The step, or 0"},
        "7808": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7811": {"comment":"BC = the step"},
        "7815": {"comment":"BC = the first number"},
        "7818": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "7820": {"comment":"DE = the step"},
        "7821": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7822": {"comment":"A step of 0?"},
        "7826": {"comment":"Then 10"},
        "7829": {"synopsis":"HL = the first number, E_PPC for 0, with bit 15 set.","comment":"A first number of 0?"},
        "7831": {"comment":"Bit 15: the number itself first"},
        "7835": {"comment":"Then E_PPC"},
        "7838": {"synopsis":"$D74E = HL, $D750 = DE; bank 0.","comment":"The next number"},
        "7841": {"comment":"The step"},
        "7845": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7847": {"synopsis":"ERASE, reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry (word $DEA7):\n1. ERASE alone: the whole program removed (PROG to VARS, ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL) after ROM\n   0's\n$0D9A (E_PPC = 0); then error code $FF through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.\n2. A string: ROM 1's $26E6 (which calls the alternate ROM's other page).\n3. Two numbers 'a,b': the lines a to b removed (ERASE_RANGE), as a direct command only.\nEntry: A = the character after ERASE.","comment":"ERASE alone?"},
        "7852": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7855": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0 (ROM 0's $0D9A)"},
        "7858": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "7862": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "7865": {"comment":"The program removed"},
        "7868": {"comment":"Error code $FF"},
        "7873": {"synopsis":"An expression (ROM 1's ROM3_SCAN_EXPR): a number goes to ERASE_LINES; a string to ROM 1's\n$26E6.","comment":"The expression (SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "7876": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "7882": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7885": {"comment":"A string: ROM 1's $26E6"},
        "7889": {"synopsis":"A number: a ',' must follow.","comment":"',' must follow"},
        "7893": {"synopsis":"Error code $0B through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.","comment":"Error code $0B"},
        "7898": {"synopsis":"The second number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6); direct only; E_PPC = 0 (ROM 0's $0D9A); HL = the\nfirst line at or after the first number (FIND_LINE), BC = the second number.","comment":"Past ',', the second number"},
        "7901": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7904": {"comment":"A direct command only"},
        "7907": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "7910": {"comment":"BC = the last line"},
        "7914": {"comment":"BC = the first line"},
        "7917": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "7919": {"comment":"The first line at or after it"},
        "7922": {"synopsis":"One line: at the program's end or numbered above BC, done; otherwise removed (ROM 3's\nNEXT_ITEM and RECLAIM).","comment":"BC = the last line"},
        "7923": {"comment":"The program's end?"},
        "7927": {"comment":"DE = the line's number"},
        "7931": {"comment":"Above the last?"},
        "7938": {"comment":"BC = the line's length (NEXT_ITEM)"},
        "7941": {"comment":"The line removed (RECLAIM)"},
        "7944": {"comment":"HL = the line now there"},
        "7947": {"synopsis":"BANK n LINE, reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for BANK n LINE (word $DF0B): copies\nthe program lines from a to b into bank n as a line cache, for direct commands only. With\nREM ($EA) after LINE, the comment statements (REM or ';') at a line's end are left out.\n1. The bank's cache area made (ROM 1's BANK_AREA_MAKE) and emptied (BANK_CACHE_CLEAR);\nthe screen's colours (ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS); the bank number to $5B65.\n2. Bank n paged at $C000 (ROM 1's $26AD): 'B', 'C' at $C000, then $80 from $C002 to $FFFF;\n$5EB8 = $C002, the place to write.\n3. From the first line at or after a (FIND_LINE), each line up to b: its number printed\n('LINE' and the number, ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN and ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, backspaced over\nafter, $2057), the line copied to $5CB6 (its number high byte first, its length, its\ntext and ENTER) and from there into the bank at ($5EB8).\n4. A line of 253 bytes or more, or a bank that is full: error code $0F ($202C).\nEntry: A = the character after LINE.","comment":"The character after LINE kept"},
        "7950": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "7952": {"comment":"Then past it"},
        "7955": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "7958": {"comment":"A direct command only"},
        "7961": {"comment":"The cache area made (BANK_AREA_MAKE)"},
        "7964": {"comment":"Emptied (BANK_CACHE_CLEAR)"},
        "7967": {"comment":"The screen's colours (SCREEN_COLOURS)"},
        "7970": {"comment":"The last line"},
        "7974": {"comment":"The first line"},
        "7978": {"comment":"A = the bank (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "7981": {"comment":"Kept at $5B65"},
        "7984": {"comment":"Paged at $C000 (ROM 1's $26AD)"},
        "7987": {"comment":"'B'"},
        "7993": {"comment":"'C'"},
        "7996": {"comment":"$5EB8 = $C002: the place to write"},
        "7999": {"comment":"$80 from $C002"},
        "8004": {"comment":"To $FFFF"},
        "8009": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8010": {"comment":"HL = the first line"},
        "8011": {"comment":"The first line at or after it (FIND_LINE)"},
        "8014": {"comment":"Nothing printed yet"},
        "8015": {"synopsis":"One line: DE = its number; above b, the end ($2014); otherwise its number high byte first at\n$5CB6, the previous number backspaced over (A characters, $2057) and the new one printed.","comment":"BC = the last line"},
        "8016": {"comment":"DE = the line's number"},
        "8020": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "8022": {"comment":"Above the last?"},
        "8024": {"comment":"Then the end"},
        "8027": {"comment":"HL = the number again"},
        "8032": {"comment":"Its bytes swapped"},
        "8035": {"comment":"$5CB6 = the number, high byte first"},
        "8039": {"comment":"Backspaces over the last one printed"},
        "8043": {"comment":"The keyword LINE"},
        "8045": {"comment":"No space before it"},
        "8049": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_TOKEN)"},
        "8052": {"comment":"Leading spaces"},
        "8054": {"comment":"The number (NUM_OUT_5)"},
        "8057": {"comment":"HL = the line's length word"},
        "8058": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "8062": {"comment":"REM given after LINE?"},
        "8067": {"comment":"No: the whole text"},
        "8069": {"comment":"HL = just before the text"},
        "8071": {"synopsis":"One statement of the line's text (ROM 1's FIND_STMT_CHAR with D = 2 steps over one)."},
        "8072": {"synopsis":"Its first character other than a space: ENTER, REM or ';' cuts the text there."},
        "8073": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "8074": {"comment":"ENTER: cut"},
        "8078": {"comment":"Spaces passed"},
        "8082": {"comment":"REM: cut"},
        "8086": {"comment":"';': cut"},
        "8090": {"comment":"Back on it"},
        "8091": {"comment":"D = 2: past one statement"},
        "8094": {"comment":"To the next statement (FIND_STMT_CHAR)"},
        "8098": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "8100": {"comment":"No: its first character"},
        "8102": {"comment":"The whole text"},
        "8104": {"synopsis":"Cut before this statement."},
        "8105": {"synopsis":"BC = the length of the text kept, HL = the text."},
        "8107": {"comment":"BC = the length kept"},
        "8111": {"comment":"HL = the text's start"},
        "8113": {"synopsis":"The text's length at $5CB8; empty: BANK_LINE_FREE. Otherwise up to 252 bytes, copied to\n$5CBA, ENTER after it; then the whole line (number, length, text) copied into the bank at\n($5EB8), which moves on."},
        "8114": {"comment":"$5CB8 = the length"},
        "8120": {"comment":"Nothing: the bytes free shown"},
        "8122": {"comment":"Plus its number, length and ENTER"},
        "8125": {"comment":"Too long?"},
        "8127": {"comment":"Then error code $0F"},
        "8130": {"comment":"The text's length"},
        "8134": {"comment":"To $5CBA"},
        "8141": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8143": {"synopsis":"ENTER at the text's end.","comment":"ENTER after it"},
        "8147": {"comment":"BC = the whole line"},
        "8148": {"comment":"DE = the place in the bank"},
        "8153": {"comment":"Past the bank's end?"},
        "8154": {"comment":"Then error code $0F"},
        "8156": {"comment":"The bank paged at $C000"},
        "8162": {"comment":"The line from $5CB6"},
        "8165": {"comment":"Copied into the bank"},
        "8167": {"comment":"The place moved on"},
        "8171": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8172": {"synopsis":"Prints ' --> ' ($2031), the bytes left in the bank (0 - ($5EB8), ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5) and\n' free' ($2036); on at $2007.","comment":"' --> '"},
        "8178": {"comment":"HL = 0 - the place: the bytes free"},
        "8188": {"comment":"Leading spaces"},
        "8190": {"comment":"Printed (NUM_OUT_5)"},
        "8212": {"synopsis":"The end of BANK n LINE (NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax word at $04C3, the command at $1F0B), when\nthe next line's number is past the last one asked for ($1F58): a new line printed; the bank\npaged at $C000 (ROM 1's $26AD, through its BANK_MAP) and its program's index built (ROM 1's\nBUILD_INDEX_BANK); with bit 7 of the program's flags byte at $C001 set (no room left for the\nindex) TXT_NO_CACHE printed.\nExit: bank 0.","comment":"ENTER: a new line"},
        "8214": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8215": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8218": {"comment":"Paged at $C000 (ROM 1's $26AD)"},
        "8221": {"comment":"Its program's index built (ROM 1's BUILD_INDEX_BANK)"},
        "8224": {"comment":"A = the program's flags byte at $C001"},
        "8227": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "8228": {"comment":"Bit 7, no room for the index, into the carry"},
        "8229": {"comment":"DE = TXT_NO_CACHE"},
        "8232": {"comment":"Printed when there was no room"},
        "8236": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0F (report G) through NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A. From BANK n\nLINE ($1FBF, $1FDA) and LINE_MERGE (a joined line too long).","comment":"Error code $0F, report G"},
        "8238": {"comment":"Stops (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A)"},
        "8241": {"synopsis":"\" --> \", its last character with bit 7 set (PRINT_BIT7). Printed by BANK n LINE at $1FEF\nbefore the bytes left in the bank."},
        "8246": {"synopsis":"\" free\", its last character with bit 7 set. Printed by BANK n LINE at $2004 after the bytes\nleft in the bank."},
        "8251": {"synopsis":"\"Insufficient space for cache\", its last character with bit 7 set. Printed by BANK_LINE_DONE\nwhen the bank has no room left for its program's index."},
        "8279": {"synopsis":"Prints character 8 (back one place) A times through RST $28 (RST_PRINT_A). A = 0 prints it\n256 times. From BANK n LINE ($1F67, only when A is not 0).\nEntry: A = the count.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8280": {"comment":"Character 8: back one place"},
        "8282": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8283": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "8284": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "8285": {"comment":"Until none is left"},
        "8288": {"synopsis":"LINE MERGE m,n (token $CA's MERGE: NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax word at $04F7, class 8, two\nnumbers), a direct command only (ROM 1's NEED_DIRECT): joins the program's lines from m to n\ninto the first of them. From the first line numbered m or more (ROM 3's FIND_LINE), each\nnext\nline numbered n or less is added: when the two lines' listed lengths (LINE_TEXT_LEN, through\nNextZXOS ROM 1's $3FE3) come to 1280 ($0500) characters or more, report G (REPORT_G);\notherwise the first line's ENTER becomes ':', the next line's 4-byte header is removed (ROM\n3's RECLAIM_DE_HL) and its length is added to the first line's. No line from m: nothing\nhappens.","comment":"A direct command only (ROM 1's NEED_DIRECT)"},
        "8291": {"comment":"BC = n, the last line (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "8294": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8295": {"comment":"BC = m, the first line"},
        "8298": {"comment":"HL = m"},
        "8300": {"comment":"HL = the first line numbered m or more (ROM 3's FIND_LINE)"},
        "8303": {"comment":"Its number's high byte"},
        "8304": {"comment":"$28 or more: the program's end?"},
        "8306": {"comment":"BC = n"},
        "8307": {"comment":"No line from m: done"},
        "8308": {"comment":"HL = the line's length"},
        "8310": {"synopsis":"One more line: is the line after this one numbered n or less?\nEntry: HL = this line's length, BC = n.","comment":"n kept"},
        "8311": {"comment":"The length's address kept"},
        "8312": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "8315": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "8316": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "8317": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "8320": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE at its second byte"},
        "8322": {"comment":"Carry when it is n or less"},
        "8324": {"comment":"Then it is joined"},
        "8326": {"comment":"Past n: the stack cleared, done"},
        "8329": {"synopsis":"The next line (its second byte at DE) joined to this one when their listed lengths come to\nless than 1280; otherwise report G.","comment":"HL = this line's length address"},
        "8330": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "8331": {"comment":"The next line's second byte kept"},
        "8332": {"comment":"HL = this line"},
        "8334": {"comment":"HL = its listed length (LINE_TEXT_LEN, ROM 1's $3FE3)"},
        "8337": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the next line's second byte"},
        "8338": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "8339": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "8340": {"comment":"HL = its listed length"},
        "8343": {"comment":"DE = the next line's second byte"},
        "8344": {"comment":"BC = this line's listed length"},
        "8345": {"comment":"The two together"},
        "8346": {"comment":"1280 characters"},
        "8349": {"comment":"That many or more?"},
        "8351": {"comment":"Then report G"},
        "8354": {"comment":"The next line's second byte kept"},
        "8355": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "8356": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "8357": {"comment":"BC = the next line's length"},
        "8360": {"comment":"HL = its text"},
        "8361": {"comment":"DE = the next line's second byte"},
        "8362": {"comment":"DE = this line's ENTER"},
        "8364": {"comment":"Made ':'"},
        "8367": {"comment":"DE = the next line's header"},
        "8368": {"comment":"The next line's length kept"},
        "8369": {"comment":"The header removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL)"},
        "8372": {"comment":"BC = the next line's length"},
        "8373": {"comment":"HL = this line's length address"},
        "8374": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "8377": {"comment":"Plus the next line's"},
        "8380": {"comment":"The new length stored"},
        "8383": {"comment":"BC = n"},
        "8384": {"comment":"The line after"},
        "8386": {"synopsis":"BANK n MERGE (token $9A n's MERGE: NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax word at $04C9), a direct command\nonly (ROM 1's NEED_DIRECT): merges the program kept in bank n into the program. The line\ncache area is made (ROM 1's BANK_AREA_MAKE); the bank, kept at $5B65, must hold a program\n(\"BC\" at $C000, ROM 1's BANK_PROG_CHECK, report N otherwise); then each of its lines from\n$C002 is copied to $5CB6 (ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY), a program line of the same number removed\n(ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM and RECLAIM) and the copy put in its place (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM, PROG\nkept),\nup to the bank program's end (a first byte of $28 or more).","comment":"A direct command only (ROM 1's NEED_DIRECT)"},
        "8389": {"comment":"The line cache area made (ROM 1's BANK_AREA_MAKE)"},
        "8392": {"comment":"A = n, the bank (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "8395": {"comment":"Kept at $5B65"},
        "8398": {"comment":"Paged at $C000"},
        "8401": {"comment":"It must hold a program (ROM 1's BANK_PROG_CHECK)"},
        "8404": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "8405": {"comment":"HL = the bank's first line"},
        "8408": {"synopsis":"One line of the bank: copied to $5CB6; at the bank program's end, done; a program line of\nthe same number removed.\nEntry: HL = the line in the bank.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8411": {"comment":"Copied to $5CB6, DE = the bank's next line (ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY)"},
        "8414": {"comment":"L = the number's high byte, H its low"},
        "8418": {"comment":"$28 or more: the bank program's end?"},
        "8420": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "8421": {"comment":"The bank's next line kept"},
        "8422": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "8424": {"comment":"Is that line in the program (ROM 3's FIND_LINE)?"},
        "8427": {"comment":"No"},
        "8429": {"comment":"Yes: its length (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM)"},
        "8432": {"comment":"It is removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM)"},
        "8435": {"synopsis":"The copied line put in the program at HL, PROG kept as it was; then the bank's next line.","comment":"BC = the copy's length"},
        "8439": {"comment":"Plus its 4-byte header"},
        "8443": {"comment":"HL = the byte before the place"},
        "8444": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "8445": {"comment":"PROG kept"},
        "8450": {"comment":"Room made (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "8453": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "8455": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "8456": {"comment":"PROG back as it was"},
        "8460": {"comment":"The copy"},
        "8463": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "8464": {"comment":"Put in the room"},
        "8466": {"comment":"HL = the bank's next line"},
        "8467": {"comment":"Its turn"},
        "8469": {"synopsis":"Runs start-up menu A (from NextZXOS ROM 0's MENU_LOOP_A at $0C78, and this page's $0423):\nthe menu file (MENUS_CFG_NAME, \"c:/nextzxos/enMenus.cfg\") loaded into $F720 by READ_FILE\n(at most $7FF bytes) unless SYMBOL SHIFT is held, and the built-in menu text (MENU_TEXT,\n$3AB\nbytes) copied after it; menu A found (FIND_MENU); then shown again and again (NextZXOS ROM\n0's $0669) and the chosen item's action run (MENU_ACTION), a click for a refused one, until\nthe menu is left or an action finishes.\nEntry: A = the menu number.\nExit: carry, the menu left with EDIT or space; Z, an action finished; no carry, no menu A.","comment":"A = the menu number kept"},
        "8470": {"comment":"The buffer at $F720, up to $0800 bytes"},
        "8476": {"comment":"DE = MENUS_CFG_NAME"},
        "8479": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT held?"},
        "8485": {"comment":"No: the file loaded (READ_FILE)"},
        "8488": {"comment":"DE = $F720, or the end of what was loaded"},
        "8489": {"comment":"The built-in menus after it (MENU_TEXT)"},
        "8495": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8497": {"comment":"A = the menu number"},
        "8498": {"comment":"Found (FIND_MENU)?"},
        "8501": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "8502": {"synopsis":"The current menu shown with item 0 selected, an item chosen and its action run.","comment":"Item 0 selected"},
        "8506": {"comment":"Shown and an item chosen (NextZXOS ROM 0's $0669)"},
        "8509": {"comment":"Carry: the menu left"},
        "8510": {"comment":"The item's action done (MENU_ACTION)"},
        "8513": {"comment":"No carry: refused"},
        "8515": {"comment":"Z: finished"},
        "8516": {"synopsis":"No carry: a click (KEY_REFUSED); the menu again.","comment":"A click for a refused item (KEY_REFUSED)"},
        "8519": {"comment":"The menu again"},
        "8521": {"synopsis":"Finds menu A in the menu text at $F720: a line \"=n\" (CFG_NUMBER) with n = A, its title on\nthe line after (NextZXOS ROM 0's CFG_SKIP_EOL). Also MENU_ACTION's 'm'.\nEntry: A = the menu number.\nExit: carry, found: $D744 = A, $D742 = HL = the title line; no carry, not there.","comment":"The menu text in the buffer"},
        "8524": {"comment":"C = the menu number wanted"},
        "8525": {"synopsis":"One line: does it start '=' and the number wanted?","comment":"A line beginning '='?"},
        "8528": {"comment":"No: the next line"},
        "8530": {"comment":"The number after '=' (CFG_NUMBER)"},
        "8534": {"comment":"None: the next line"},
        "8536": {"comment":"The menu wanted?"},
        "8538": {"comment":"No: the next line"},
        "8540": {"comment":"Past the line end: the title (ROM 0's CFG_SKIP_EOL)"},
        "8543": {"comment":"The end of the text: not found"},
        "8544": {"comment":"$D744 = the menu number"},
        "8548": {"comment":"$D742 = the title's address"},
        "8551": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "8553": {"synopsis":"The next line (NextZXOS ROM 0's CFG_NEXT_LINE), unless the text ends.","comment":"To the next line (ROM 0's CFG_NEXT_LINE)"},
        "8556": {"comment":"The end of the text: not found"},
        "8557": {"comment":"That line"},
        "8559": {"synopsis":"The menu items' functions, 'i' 0 to 12 (MENU_ACT_I): a word each, bit 7 set for an address\nin this ROM (the bit cleared), clear for one in NextZXOS ROM 0 (run through $0072). 0-2\nEDITOR_START (the items NextBASIC, Calculator, Command Line); 3 EDITOR_RESTART; 4\nMODE_TOGGLE (Command Line / NextBASIC in the options); 5 COLUMNS_NEXT (32/64/85); 6\nEDIT_SCREEN_SWAP (Screen); 7 RENUMBER_ALL (Renumber); 8 STACK_BELOW_UDG (Clear); 9 ROM 0's\nMENU_RESTART_CLS (Exit); 10 ROM 0's $2C04 (Browser); 11 KEY_11 (Token keys); 12 KEY_12\n(String tokens)."},
        "8585": {"synopsis":"Runs item A's action, the text after its ':' (at $F70B + 2A): 'i' and a number, a function\nof MENU_FUNCS; 'g' and a name, the guide on that topic; 'b' and a command, run as BASIC; 'm'\nand a number, that menu made current (FIND_MENU).\nEntry: A = the item.\nExit: no carry, refused (no action, or a bad letter or number); carry otherwise, Z when the\nmenu is finished.","comment":"A = 2 x the item"},
        "8586": {"comment":"The items' text addresses"},
        "8591": {"comment":"DE = the item's"},
        "8594": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "8595": {"comment":"An item's action starts with ':'"},
        "8599": {"synopsis":"No carry, NZ: refused.","comment":"Otherwise no carry, NZ: refused"},
        "8602": {"comment":"E = the action's letter"},
        "8603": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8604": {"comment":"A ':' after it skipped"},
        "8608": {"synopsis":"The action's letter, in lower case.","comment":"A = the letter in lower case"},
        "8611": {"comment":"'i': a function (MENU_FUNCS)"},
        "8615": {"comment":"'g': a guide"},
        "8619": {"comment":"'b': a BASIC command"},
        "8623": {"comment":"'m': a menu; other letters refused"},
        "8627": {"comment":"E = the menu number"},
        "8630": {"comment":"None: refused"},
        "8631": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Found and made the current menu"},
        "8634": {"synopsis":"'i': the function in MENU_FUNCS, numbers 0-12: one in this ROM entered by RET, one in\nNextZXOS ROM 0 through $0072 (CALL_ROM0's second half).","comment":"E = the function number"},
        "8637": {"comment":"None: refused"},
        "8638": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "8639": {"comment":"13 functions, 0-12"},
        "8642": {"comment":"The function's word in MENU_FUNCS"},
        "8648": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "8651": {"comment":"Bit 7 set?"},
        "8653": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "8655": {"comment":"Pushed for a RET"},
        "8656": {"comment":"Set: run in this ROM"},
        "8657": {"comment":"Clear:"},
        "8658": {"comment":"run in ROM 0"},
        "8661": {"synopsis":"'g': the guide's name copied to $DA35 with its end, then the command GUIDE_CMD_TEXT\n(layer2,0:layer0:sprite print0:.guide \"|\") run, the '|' standing for the name. Also called\nby NextZXOS ROM 0 ($30AD) with HL = a guide's file name.","comment":"HL kept: the guide's name"},
        "8662": {"comment":"Copied to $DA35"},
        "8665": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "8666": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8668": {"comment":"Up to a control code or $FF, which is copied too"},
        "8673": {"comment":"The command line that shows the guide"},
        "8676": {"comment":"Run"},
        "8678": {"synopsis":"'b': no texts for '|' ($FF at $E090 and $DA35); the command after the 'b' run.","comment":"$FF: no text for a '|'"},
        "8683": {"comment":"In both places"},
        "8686": {"synopsis":"Runs the command text at HL as BASIC: $D5B8 = 5 when it was 4; the text copied to the rows\nat $C000 of bank 7 (C characters each, the width at $D73D, then a flag byte and two more:\nflag\n3 the first row, 2 the others, and the last one's with bit 1 cleared and bit 3 set), its\ncharacters expanded (EXPAND_TEXT); FLAGS2 bit 0 set; the cursor set up (CURSOR_SET_UPPER)\nand\nthe rows entered as a line ($0842 with C = 0). Also called by NextZXOS ROM 0 ($3127).\nEntry: HL = the command, ended by a control code or $FF.\nExit: no carry.","comment":"$D5B8 = 4?"},
        "8692": {"comment":"No"},
        "8694": {"comment":"Yes: made 5"},
        "8698": {"synopsis":"The rows built.","comment":"XL = 3: the first row's flag"},
        "8701": {"comment":"The rows built at $C000 in bank 7"},
        "8704": {"comment":"C = the row width"},
        "8708": {"comment":"The command copied, characters expanded"},
        "8711": {"comment":"The last row's rest filled with 0"},
        "8712": {"synopsis":"The last row's rest made 0.","comment":"A 0 more"},
        "8714": {"comment":"To the row's end"},
        "8717": {"comment":"The row's flag byte"},
        "8719": {"comment":"Bit 1 cleared"},
        "8721": {"comment":"Bit 3 set: the last row"},
        "8724": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 0 set"},
        "8728": {"comment":"The cursor set up (CURSOR_SET_UPPER)"},
        "8731": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "8733": {"comment":"The rows entered as a line ($0842)"},
        "8736": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "8738": {"synopsis":"Copies the text at HL to DE up to a control code or $FF, in rows of C characters (each full\nrow followed by the flag byte in XL, which then becomes 2, and two bytes skipped; C back to\nthe width at $D73D). Characters expanded: '|' the text at $E090, or after a quote the\nguide's\nname at $DA35; '`' \"en\" (LANG_CODE_TEXT); $7F \"c:/nextzxos/\" (SYS_FOLDER_TEXT); each\nexpansion up to its control code or $FF. From RUN_COMMAND and READ_FILE (C = 0).\nExit: HL at the end, DE past the copy, C the room left in the row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, XL.","comment":"The next character"},
        "8739": {"comment":"A control code or $FF ends the text"},
        "8743": {"comment":"A back"},
        "8744": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "8745": {"comment":"B = 1: one character"},
        "8747": {"comment":"'|'?"},
        "8749": {"comment":"No"},
        "8751": {"comment":"The character before it"},
        "8753": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "8755": {"comment":"HL = the text kept at $E090"},
        "8758": {"comment":"No quote before the bar: that text"},
        "8760": {"comment":"After a quote: the guide's name at $DA35"},
        "8765": {"synopsis":"Not '|': '`', $7F or the character itself.","comment":"'`'?"},
        "8767": {"comment":"Then \"en\""},
        "8772": {"comment":"$7F?"},
        "8774": {"comment":"Then \"c:/nextzxos/\""},
        "8777": {"comment":"Neither: the character itself"},
        "8779": {"synopsis":"One character of an expansion, up to its control code or $FF.","comment":"A character of the string"},
        "8781": {"comment":"Its end?"},
        "8786": {"comment":"A back"},
        "8787": {"comment":"B one more, so the string goes on"},
        "8788": {"synopsis":"A character stored; the row closed when full.","comment":"Stored in the row"},
        "8790": {"comment":"The row full?"},
        "8793": {"comment":"The row's flag byte"},
        "8796": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8797": {"comment":"XL = 2 for the rows after"},
        "8800": {"comment":"Past the row's 2 other bytes"},
        "8802": {"comment":"C = the row width again"},
        "8806": {"synopsis":"The rest of the expansion.","comment":"The rest of the string"},
        "8808": {"synopsis":"The text's next character.","comment":"HL back"},
        "8809": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "8810": {"comment":"Its turn"},
        "8812": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number at HL, 0-255, into E: one digit at least, then digits up to $FF, $0D\nor $0A (NextZXOS ROM 0's IS_LINE_END).\nExit: carry, E = the number, HL at the line end; no carry, another character or a number\nabove 255.\nChanges: AF, D, E, HL.","comment":"E = 0"},
        "8814": {"comment":"A digit must come first"},
        "8817": {"synopsis":"The next character: a line end ends the number.","comment":"The next character"},
        "8818": {"comment":"$FF, $0D or $0A: the number ends (ROM 0's IS_LINE_END)"},
        "8821": {"comment":"Carry: a number"},
        "8823": {"synopsis":"A digit: E = E x 10 + it.","comment":"Below '0': no carry"},
        "8827": {"comment":"Above '9': no carry"},
        "8831": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8832": {"comment":"DE = E x 10"},
        "8834": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "8836": {"comment":"Still below 256?"},
        "8838": {"comment":"Yes: the next digit"},
        "8840": {"comment":"No: no carry"},
        "8841": {"synopsis":"READ_TO_C000 with BC = $700 (at most $6FF bytes). Called by NextZXOS ROM 0 ($2EC4, with DE =\nBROWSEXT_CFG).","comment":"At most $6FF bytes"},
        "8844": {"synopsis":"READ_FILE into $C000. Called by NextZXOS ROM 0 ($30FE).\nExit: as READ_FILE; BC and HL kept.","comment":"Into $C000"},
        "8847": {"comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "8849": {"comment":"The file read"},
        "8855": {"synopsis":"Reads the file named at DE into HL, at most BC - 1 bytes: BC + 1 bytes from HL first filled\nwith $FF; the name copied to $D82B by EXPAND_TEXT (which expands $7F to \"c:/nextzxos/\") and\nended by $FF; DOS_OPEN file 0 (BC = DE = 1), DOS_READ (C = bank 7), DOS_CLOSE, each in ROM 2\nthrough RST $30. From RUN_MENU, READ_TO_C000 and NextZXOS ROM 0 ($3B2A, with DE =\nBROWSER_CFG_NAME).\nEntry: HL = the buffer, BC = its size, DE = the name.\nExit: carry and HL = the end of the bytes read; no carry when the file did not open.","comment":"The buffer, size and name kept"},
        "8858": {"comment":"DE = HL + 1"},
        "8861": {"comment":"The buffer filled with $FF"},
        "8865": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8866": {"comment":"The name expanded to $D82B"},
        "8872": {"comment":"EXPAND_TEXT"},
        "8875": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "8878": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8879": {"comment":"DE = BC = 1"},
        "8884": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN (ROM 2): file 0, exclusive read"},
        "8887": {"comment":"DE = the size"},
        "8888": {"comment":"Less one"},
        "8889": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8890": {"comment":"Did not open"},
        "8893": {"comment":"B = file 0, C = bank 7"},
        "8896": {"comment":"DOS_READ (ROM 2): DE bytes to HL"},
        "8899": {"comment":"Not all read: DE = the bytes left"},
        "8901": {"comment":"All read"},
        "8904": {"synopsis":"DE = the bytes not read (0 when all were); DOS_CLOSE."},
        "8905": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "8907": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE (ROM 2)"},
        "8911": {"comment":"HL = the bytes asked for"},
        "8912": {"comment":"Less those not read"},
        "8915": {"comment":"The buffer's start"},
        "8916": {"comment":"HL = the end of what was read"},
        "8917": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8919": {"synopsis":"The built-in start-up menus, $3AB bytes to $2681, copied to $F720 or after the menu file by\nRUN_MENU; read by FIND_MENU, NextZXOS ROM 0's $0669 and MENU_ACTION. Lines end $0A ($0D\nfirst). A line \"=n\" starts menu n, the next line is its title, and each line after is an\nitem: its text ('_' after the hotkey), ':', an action letter and its argument ('i' function,\n'm' menu, 'g' guide, 'b' BASIC command; '<$7F>' stands for \"c:/nextzxos/\"). The text ends\nwith $FF. Menus 0-6: the main menus, the options of three editors, the cartridges and the\ntools."},
        "8920": {"synopsis":"Menu 0: \"NextZXOS\"."},
        "9020": {"synopsis":"Menu 1: \"NextZXOS\"."},
        "9274": {"synopsis":"Menu 2: \"Options\"."},
        "9433": {"synopsis":"Menu 3: \"Options\"."},
        "9485": {"synopsis":"Menu 4: \"Options\"."},
        "9553": {"synopsis":"Menu 5: \"NextZXOS\"."},
        "9725": {"synopsis":"Menu 6: \"Tools\"."},
        "9858": {"synopsis":"A command line, ended by $0D, that MENU_ACT_G hands to RUN_COMMAND:\n\"layer2,0:layer0:sprite print0:.guide \"|\"\". Its \"|\" after a quote becomes the text at $DA35\n(the guide's name copied there by MENU_ACT_G)."},
        "9899": {"synopsis":"The language code \"en\", ended by $FF: what EXPAND_TEXT puts for a \"`\" ($60) in a name."},
        "9902": {"synopsis":"The system folder \"c:/nextzxos/\", ended by $FF: what EXPAND_TEXT puts for a $7F in a name."},
        "9915": {"synopsis":"The menu file's name, ended by $00: $7F, \"enMenus.cfg\" (so \"c:/nextzxos/enMenus.cfg\" once\nexpanded). Passed in DE by RUN_MENU to READ_FILE, which loads it unless SYMBOL SHIFT is\nheld."},
        "9928": {"synopsis":"A file name ended by $00: $7F, \"browser.cfg\" (the system folder, see SYS_FOLDER_TEXT).\nPassed to READ_FILE by NextZXOS ROM 0 ($3B27)."},
        "9941": {"synopsis":"A file name ended by $00: $7F, \"enBrowsext.cfg\". Passed to READ_TO_C000_7 by NextZXOS ROM 0\n($2EC1)."},
        "9957": {"synopsis":"\"c:/docs/guides/browser.gde\", ended by $FF: the Browser's own guide, which NextZXOS ROM 0\nhands to MENU_ACT_G ($30A8)."},
        "9984": {"synopsis":"A command line: \"CLS:LOAD\"RUN.BAS\"\", $0D (NextZXOS ROM 0 at $30E7). RUN_GDE_TXT follows."},
        "10002": {"synopsis":"\"run\", which runs on into GDE_EXT_TXT: \"run.gde\", ended by $FF (NextZXOS ROM 0 at $3053,\nfor MENU_ACT_G)."},
        "10005": {"synopsis":"\".gde\", ended by $FF. Nothing in the ROMs points at it apart from RUN_GDE_TXT running on\ninto it."},
        "10010": {"synopsis":"HL = CH_ADD, then SKIP_CHAR. From $1E6E.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "10013": {"comment":"On with SKIP_CHAR"},
        "10016": {"synopsis":"HL = CH_ADD, then SKIP_ONE: the character after CH_ADD's. From $1E66, $1E7A, $1F10.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "10019": {"synopsis":"HL + 1, CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"Past this character"},
        "10020": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"A = the character at HL; $21 and up and ENTER ($0D) are kept (return). Anything else moves\non: $00-$0F (a number's mark $0E too) and $18-$20 past themselves, the colour codes $10-$15\nwith their one operand, AT and TAB ($16, $17) with their two; CH_ADD follows each time.\nExit: A = the character, HL = CH_ADD at it.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "10024": {"comment":"Printable or a token: keep it"},
        "10027": {"comment":"ENTER: keep it"},
        "10030": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10031": {"comment":"$18-$20: skip it"},
        "10035": {"comment":"$00-$0F: skip it"},
        "10039": {"comment":"$10-$15: skip it and its operand"},
        "10043": {"comment":"AT, TAB: skip it and both operands"},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"Z if A is THEN ($CB), ENTER or ':' (IS_STMT_END). From $1C71.\nChanges: F.","comment":"THEN?"},
        "10049": {"synopsis":"Z if A is ENTER or ':'. From $1CAA, $1D13, $1E71, $1EA7.\nChanges: F.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "10052": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "10055": {"synopsis":"The end of a command's operands, as NextZXOS ROM 1's STATEMENT_END. Running (FLAGS bit 7\nset): returns, and the command goes on. Checking: the command is left: its return is taken\noff, the two entries below it are kept and the one under them is replaced by ROM 1's\nSTMT_NEXT ($0944), so the way back out of this ROM ends there. From $1E1E, $1E80, $1EAC,\n$1ECA, $1EDD, $1F13.","comment":"Running?"},
        "10060": {"comment":"Checking: the command's return dropped"},
        "10061": {"comment":"BC = the entry below it"},
        "10062": {"comment":"DE = the one below that"},
        "10063": {"comment":"The entry under them becomes ROM 1's STMT_NEXT"},
        "10067": {"comment":"The two put back"},
        "10069": {"comment":"On through them"},
        "10070": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE, whose last character has bit 7 set, one character at a time through\nRST $28 (RST_PRINT_A), bit 7 taken off. From BANK n LINE ($1FEF, $2004) and BANK_LINE_DONE.\nExit: DE past the text.\nChanges: AF, DE, and what ROM 3's printing changes.","comment":"The character without bit 7"},
        "10073": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10074": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: that was the last"}
      }
    },
