      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"Address $0000 (RST $00): 16 NOPs, then RST $10's JP. Code reaching $0000 while this ROM is\npaged in runs on into CALL_ROM1, which takes the word after the RST $00 as a ROM 1 address:\nRST $00 acts as RST $10 here.","comment":"RST $00 falls through 16 NOPs into RST $10"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: CALL_ROM1, a call of the ROM 1 routine whose address is the word after the RST.","comment":"CALL_ROM1: the word after the RST is a ROM 1 address"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: CALL_ROM2, a call of the ROM 2 routine whose address is the word after the RST.","comment":"CALL_ROM2: the word after the RST is a ROM 2 address"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: CALL_ROM3, a call of the ROM 3 routine whose address is the word after the RST.","comment":"CALL_ROM3: the word after the RST is a ROM 3 address"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: A = the character at CH_ADD, CH_ADD moved past what SKIP_CHAR skips (spaces, most\ncontrol codes and their operands), through GET_CHAR_RUN. The job of ROM 3's RST $18.","comment":"GET_CHAR: the character at CH_ADD"},
        "48": {"synopsis":"RST $30: CH_ADD + 1, then on past what SKIP_CHAR skips (NEXT_SKIP_RUN); A = the character.\nThe job of ROM 3's RST $20.","comment":"NEXT_SKIP: the next character after CH_ADD"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"The maskable interrupt (IM 1) while this ROM is paged in: AF pushed, 23 NOPs, AF back, EI\nand RET. Nothing else is done: no frame count and no keyboard scan while this page replaces\nROM 1.","comment":"Keep AF; nothing else is done here"},
        "80": {"comment":"AF back; interrupts on again"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI address: PUSH AF and a NOP, then on into CALL_ROM1, which would take the pushed AF\nas the address of its word. This page has no working NMI handler.","comment":"NMI: AF pushed, then on into CALL_ROM1"},
        "104": {"synopsis":"Calls the ROM 1 routine whose address is the word after the CALL (or RST $10), then comes\nback past the word with this ROM paged in again.\n1. BC kept at $5B54; the word read through the return address, which moves past it.\n2. $007B pushed as the way back: ROM 1's own $007B sets NextReg $8C = $80 (this ROM on) and\n   returns.\n3. The routine pushed, BC restored, then ALT_ROM_OFF, whose RET enters the routine in ROM 1.\nEntry: AF, BC, DE, HL as the routine wants them.\nExit: as the routine leaves them.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "108": {"comment":"HL = the return address, the word there into BC"},
        "113": {"comment":"Return address moved past the word"},
        "114": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1's $007B turns this ROM on again"},
        "118": {"comment":"The ROM 1 routine to RET to"},
        "119": {"synopsis":"The common end of CALL_ROM1 and CALL_DIVMMC: BC back from $5B54, then ALT_ROM_OFF.","comment":"BC back"},
        "123": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8C = 0: this ROM is switched off and NextZXOS ROM 1 is read in its place; the RET\nthen goes into ROM 1 at the address on the stack. Every call out of this page ends here:\nCALL_ROM1-CALL_ROM0 and the inline 'PUSH return / PUSH $007B / PUSH routine / JP $007B'\ncalls used all over the page.","comment":"This ROM off: ROM 1 is read from here on"},
        "127": {"comment":"Into ROM 1 at the stacked address"},
        "128": {"synopsis":"Calls the ROM 2 routine whose address is the word after the CALL (or RST $18): BC kept at\n$5B54, the word read; stacked are $007B (back into this ROM), $5B3E (the RAM routine that\nselects ROM 1 again), the routine and $5B43 (the RAM routine that selects ROM 2); then\nALT_ROM_OFF. Its RET goes to $5B43, which pages ROM 2 in and returns into the routine.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "132": {"comment":"HL = the return address, the word there into BC"},
        "138": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1's $007B turns this ROM on"},
        "142": {"comment":"Then $5B3E selects ROM 1 again"},
        "146": {"comment":"The ROM 2 routine"},
        "147": {"comment":"First $5B43 selects ROM 2"},
        "151": {"comment":"BC back; this ROM off"},
        "157": {"synopsis":"Calls the ROM 3 routine whose address is the word after the CALL (or RST $20), as CALL_ROM2\ndoes, with $5B48 (the RAM routine that selects ROM 3) as the first stop.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "161": {"comment":"HL = the return address, the word there into BC"},
        "167": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1's $007B turns this ROM on","synopsis":"RST $20's stub past its inline word: calls the ROM 3 routine at BC (from $1A0E, which sets\nBC itself)."},
        "171": {"comment":"Then $5B3E selects ROM 1 again"},
        "175": {"comment":"The ROM 3 routine"},
        "176": {"comment":"First $5B48 selects ROM 3"},
        "180": {"comment":"BC back; this ROM off"},
        "186": {"synopsis":"Calls the ROM 0 routine whose address is the word after the CALL, as CALL_ROM2 does, with\n$5B4D (the RAM routine that selects ROM 0) as the first stop.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "190": {"comment":"HL = the return address, the word there into BC"},
        "196": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1's $007B turns this ROM on"},
        "200": {"comment":"Then $5B3E selects ROM 1 again"},
        "204": {"comment":"The ROM 0 routine"},
        "205": {"comment":"First $5B4D selects ROM 0"},
        "209": {"comment":"BC back; this ROM off"},
        "215": {"synopsis":"Calls the DivMMC memory's routine whose address is the word after the CALL: BC kept at\n$5B54, the routine and ROM 1's CALL_DIVMMC_ALT ($3EA0) pushed, then CALL_ROM_GO. No $007B is\npushed here: $3EA0 leaves its own way back ($2705 in the DivMMC memory, then $007B).","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "219": {"comment":"HL = the return address, the word there into BC"},
        "225": {"comment":"The DivMMC routine, entered by ROM 1's $3EA0"},
        "232": {"synopsis":"RAM bank 0 at $C000 with ROM 1 selected (NextReg $8E = $09), then SWAP_SP. The same bytes as\nROM 1's SWAP_SP_BANK0 ($2AF5).","comment":"RAM bank 0 at $C000, ROM 1 selected"},
        "236": {"synopsis":"Swaps SP with the stack pointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved over to the other\nstack (carried in AF); HL kept through $5B52.\nExit: AF, BC, DE, HL as on entry; AF' = the return address.\nChanges: SP, AF', $5B52, $5B6A.","comment":"Keep AF; AF = the return address"},
        "238": {"comment":"Keep HL"},
        "241": {"comment":"SP swapped with the one kept at $5B6A"},
        "249": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "252": {"comment":"The return address onto the new stack; AF back"},
        "255": {"synopsis":"SWAP_SP, then RAM bank 7 at $C000 with ROM 1 selected (NextReg $8E = $79). The same work as\nROM 1's SWAP_SP_BANK7 ($2B0C).","comment":"Keep AF; AF = the return address"},
        "257": {"comment":"Keep HL"},
        "260": {"comment":"SP swapped with the one kept at $5B6A"},
        "268": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "271": {"comment":"The return address onto the new stack; AF back"},
        "273": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, ROM 1 selected"},
        "278": {"synopsis":"GET_CHAR's work (RST $28 jumps here): HL = CH_ADD, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "284": {"synopsis":"NEXT_SKIP's work (RST $30 jumps here): HL = CH_ADD, then SKIP_ONE.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "287": {"synopsis":"HL + 1, CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR. The same bytes as ROM 1's SKIP_ONE ($3ECF).","comment":"Past this character"},
        "288": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "291": {"synopsis":"A = the character at HL; $21 and up, ENTER ($0D) and $0E (a number's mark) are kept\n(return). Anything else moves on: $00-$0F and $18-$20 past themselves, the colour codes\n$10-$15 with their one operand, AT and TAB ($16, $17) with their two; CH_ADD follows each\ntime.\nExit: A = the character, HL = CH_ADD.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "292": {"comment":"Printable or a token: keep it"},
        "295": {"comment":"ENTER: keep it"},
        "298": {"comment":"A number's mark: keep it"},
        "301": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "302": {"comment":"$18-$20: skip it"},
        "306": {"comment":"$00-$0F: skip it"},
        "310": {"comment":"$10-$15: skip it and its operand"},
        "314": {"comment":"AT, TAB: skip it and both operands"},
        "317": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE, whose last character has bit 7 set, one character at a time through\nROM 3's $0010 (its print restart), bit 7 taken off.\nExit: DE past the text.\nChanges: AF, DE, and what ROM 3's printing changes.","comment":"The character without bit 7"},
        "320": {"comment":"Print it through ROM 3's $0010"},
        "323": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: that was the last"},
        "329": {"synopsis":"The end of a command's operands, as ROM 1's STATEMENT_END. Running (FLAGS bit 7 set):\nreturns, and the command goes on. Checking: the command is left: its return and the $007B\nbelow it taken off, the entry under them replaced by ROM 1's STMT_NEXT ($0944), and $007B\nput back, so ALT_ROM_OFF goes to STMT_NEXT for what follows the statement. Must be called at\nthe command's own stack level (SPR_RANGE and the TILE helper at $0FC5 take their own return\noff first). Changes (checking): BC, HL.","comment":"Running?"},
        "334": {"comment":"Checking: drop the command's return and the $007B below it"},
        "336": {"comment":"The entry below becomes ROM 1's STMT_NEXT"},
        "340": {"comment":"$007B back on top; on to STMT_NEXT"},
        "965": {"synopsis":"The rest of ROM 3's TONE_OUT, which pages this ROM in (NextReg $8C = $80 at its $03C1) and\nruns on here with the alternate ROM in its place: the same tone loop as ROM 3's, with the\nCPU at 3.5 MHz when the DivMMC memory's $2993 (called with ROM 1 selected, NextReg $8E =\n$01, then ROM 3 again) gives E bit 3 set; the speed from NextReg 7 is kept on the stack and\nput back after. IX = TONE_ALT_NOPS + BC, the entry into the NOPs. Leaves through ALT_ROM_OFF\nwith A = 0, into ROM 3 at TONE_OUT's return address.\nEntry: as in ROM 3's TONE_OUT after its $03C1: interrupts off, DE = the cycles, H the outer\ncount, L the inner count (already / 4), BC = 3 - L's low two bits.\nExit: A = 0; interrupts on.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Keep DE"},
        "966": {"comment":"ROM 1 selected for the DivMMC call"},
        "970": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2993: E"},
        "975": {"comment":"ROM 3 selected again"},
        "979": {"comment":"A = NextReg 7, the CPU speed"},
        "990": {"comment":"E bit 3: 3.5 MHz for the tone?"},
        "994": {"comment":"The speed kept"},
        "997": {"comment":"Yes: 3.5 MHz"},
        "1001": {"synopsis":"IX = the entry into TONE_ALT_NOPS; A = the border colour from BORDCR with bit 3 set.","comment":"IX = the entry into the NOPs"},
        "1007": {"comment":"The border colour from BORDCR"},
        "1012": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "1015": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "1017": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay loop."},
        "1020": {"comment":"B and C one more for the loops' first DEC"},
        "1022": {"synopsis":"The delay: C counts down, then B (from H) with C reloaded."},
        "1025": {"comment":"C = $3F for the outer rounds"},
        "1031": {"comment":"The speaker bit flipped"},
        "1033": {"comment":"The edge"},
        "1035": {"comment":"B = H again"},
        "1036": {"comment":"C = the byte sent"},
        "1037": {"comment":"A rising edge?"},
        "1039": {"comment":"Yes: the second half"},
        "1041": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "1043": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "1045": {"comment":"A back, C = L"},
        "1047": {"comment":"One cycle less"},
        "1048": {"comment":"The next half-cycle"},
        "1050": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer."},
        "1051": {"comment":"One count longer"},
        "1054": {"synopsis":"DE ran out: interrupts on, the CPU speed back (NextReg 7), A = 0, out through ALT_ROM_OFF.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1055": {"comment":"The speed back"},
        "1059": {"comment":"A = 0; back into ROM 3"},
        "1387": {"synopsis":"SPRITE (token $9E): NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for it ($038B) is class $0E with the word\n$856B, this ROM's $056B. The character after SPRITE chooses the form: MOVE (SPR_MOVE),\nCONTINUE (SPR_CONTINUE), PAUSE (SPR_PAUSE), RUN (SPR_RUN), STOP (SPR_STOP), PRINT and BORDER\n(SPR_PRINT_BORDR), PALETTE (token $9D, $39B5), CLEAR (SPR_CLEAR), DIM (SPR_DIM), BANK (token\n$9A, SPR_BANK), OVER (token $DE, SPR_OVER); anything else is SPRITE n,... (SPR_SET). Reached\nwhen checking and when running; each form stops checking at STATEMENT_END.\nEntry: A = the character after SPRITE, at CH_ADD.","comment":"Below $81 (not a token): SPRITE n and its numbers"},
        "1392": {"comment":"MOVE?"},
        "1397": {"comment":"CONTINUE?"},
        "1402": {"comment":"PAUSE?"},
        "1407": {"comment":"RUN?"},
        "1411": {"comment":"STOP?"},
        "1415": {"comment":"PRINT?"},
        "1419": {"comment":"BORDER?"},
        "1423": {"comment":"PALETTE (token $9D)? Handled at $39B5"},
        "1428": {"comment":"CLEAR?"},
        "1432": {"comment":"DIM?"},
        "1436": {"comment":"BANK (token $9A)?"},
        "1441": {"comment":"OVER (token $DE)?"},
        "1445": {"comment":"Any other token: SPRITE n and its numbers"},
        "1448": {"synopsis":"SPRITE PRINT n and SPRITE BORDER n: n (0 or 1, otherwise report B) into NextReg $15 through\nROM 1's NEXTREG_15_MASK: PRINT its bit 0 (sprites shown), BORDER its bit 1 (sprites over the\nborder).\nEntry: A = the token.","comment":"Keep the token"},
        "1449": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: the number after the token"},
        "1452": {"comment":"The token back"},
        "1453": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1456": {"comment":"Keep the token"},
        "1457": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: A = n"},
        "1460": {"comment":"Only 0 or 1 allowed"},
        "1465": {"comment":"E = n"},
        "1467": {"comment":"PRINT: NextReg $15 bit 0, sprites shown"},
        "1474": {"comment":"BORDER: bit 1, sprites over the border"},
        "1477": {"synopsis":"NextReg $15 changed: D = the mask of the bits kept, E = the new bit.","comment":"E = the bit"},
        "1478": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXTREG_15_MASK: NextReg $15 changed"},
        "1482": {"synopsis":"SPRITE RUN: running, the sprites are shown and moved once first (SPRITE_UPDATE); then\nSPR_SET_MODE with E = 0: from now on a SPRITE n,... goes to the hardware at once.","comment":"Running: show and move the sprites once"},
        "1489": {"comment":"E = 0: changes shown at once"},
        "1493": {"synopsis":"SPRITE STOP: SPR_SET_MODE with E = $FF: from now on a SPRITE n,... only marks the sprite,\nand SPRITE MOVE shows it.","comment":"E = $FF: changes wait for SPRITE MOVE"},
        "1495": {"synopsis":"Past the token, the statement's end (STATEMENT_END); then $2CFF in 8K page $10 = E (page $10\nat $2000 for the write, MMU 1 = $FF after).","comment":"Past the token"},
        "1496": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1499": {"comment":"Page $10 at $2000"},
        "1503": {"comment":"$2CFF = the mode"},
        "1507": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "1512": {"synopsis":"SPRITE CLEAR: past CLEAR, the statement's end, then ROM 1's SPRITES_RESET (sprites off, all\nhidden, the records at $24DF-$2CFF of page $10 cleared, the clip window reset); then, when\nbit 4 of E from the DivMMC memory's $2993 is set (SPRITE OVER set it), NextReg $4B (the\nsprites' transparency index) = $E3 again.","comment":"Past CLEAR"},
        "1513": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1516": {"comment":"ROM 1's SPRITES_RESET"},
        "1519": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2993: E"},
        "1524": {"comment":"Bit 4: SPRITE OVER used?"},
        "1527": {"comment":"Yes: the transparency index back to $E3"},
        "1532": {"synopsis":"SPRITE DIM x1,x2,y1,y2: two pairs (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8 each; report C without the ','\nbetween them), the statement's end, then LAYER_DIM_GO ($10FC) with L = $19, the sprites'\nclip window register (NextReg $19).","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8: x1,x2"},
        "1535": {"comment":"A ',' must follow"},
        "1540": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8: y1,y2"},
        "1543": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1546": {"comment":"L = $19, the sprites' clip window register"},
        "1548": {"comment":"Set it from the four numbers"},
        "1551": {"synopsis":"SPRITE OVER n: n (NEXT_CLASS_6, then TAKE_BYTE when running) into NextReg $4B, the sprites'\ntransparency index; then the word the DivMMC memory's $2993 gives in DE is written back by\nits $2A00 with bit 4 of the low byte set (SPR_CLEAR resets NextReg $4B to $E3 while that bit\nis set). Checking stops at STATEMENT_END.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: n"},
        "1554": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1557": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: A = n"},
        "1560": {"comment":"The sprites' transparency index"},
        "1563": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2993: DE"},
        "1568": {"comment":"HL = it with bit 4 set"},
        "1571": {"comment":"Written back by the DivMMC memory's $2A00"},
        "1577": {"synopsis":"SPRITE n,x,y,p,f,s,h,v (SPRITE followed by a number): n and up to 7 more numbers, any of\nthem left out by an empty place (',,') or by ending early.\n1. n (ROM 1's CLASS_6).\n2. C collects a bit for each place, 1 for a number given, n's ending in bit 7; each place\n   after a ',' is a number (CLASS_6) or empty; anything but ',' or the statement's end is\n   report C.\n3. With 8 places, SPR_SET_DONE.","comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: n"},
        "1580": {"comment":"No places yet"},
        "1583": {"synopsis":"A number was given: a 1 for its place.","comment":"A number given"},
        "1584": {"synopsis":"The place's bit into C; C full (8 places) ends the list.","comment":"Its bit into C; 8 places done?"},
        "1589": {"comment":"ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST: the end?"},
        "1592": {"comment":"At the end: an empty place"},
        "1594": {"comment":"Otherwise a ',' must follow"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Past the ','"},
        "1599": {"synopsis":"After a ',': another ',' or the end leaves the place empty; otherwise a number.","comment":"ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST again"},
        "1602": {"comment":"End: an empty place"},
        "1604": {"comment":"Another ',': an empty place"},
        "1608": {"comment":"Keep the flags"},
        "1609": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the number"},
        "1612": {"comment":"The flags back; a number given"},
        "1615": {"synopsis":"SPRITE n,... at its end: checking stops here (STATEMENT_END).\n1. The 8 places' values taken (TAKE_VALUES).\n2. A negative n is a relative sprite: REL_SPRITE_FLDS; otherwise SPRITE_FIELDS; the values\n   put into sprite |n|'s record (SET_FIELDS).\n3. A hidden sprite stops moving (its bit in the moving map cleared).\n4. With $2CFF zero (SPRITE RUN) the record goes to the hardware now (UPLOAD_ATTRS);\n   otherwise the sprite is marked changed for SPRITE MOVE.","comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1618": {"comment":"8 places off the calculator stack"},
        "1623": {"comment":"SPRITE_FIELDS for n not negative"},
        "1626": {"comment":"Is n negative?"},
        "1628": {"comment":"Its sign dropped"},
        "1630": {"comment":"Negative: a relative sprite, REL_SPRITE_FLDS"},
        "1635": {"synopsis":"HL = the fields table: the values into the record.","comment":"The values into the record"},
        "1638": {"comment":"Keep the record"},
        "1639": {"comment":"Visible?"},
        "1646": {"comment":"Hidden: its moving bit cleared"},
        "1656": {"synopsis":"HL = the record: uploaded now, or marked for later.","comment":"The record back"},
        "1657": {"comment":"SPRITE STOP mode?"},
        "1660": {"comment":"Yes: mark the sprite changed"},
        "1664": {"comment":"SPRITE RUN mode: send it now"},
        "1667": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "1672": {"synopsis":"Report C (error code $0B, Nonsense in BASIC) through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.","comment":"Error code $0B, report C"},
        "1674": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "1677": {"synopsis":"SPRITE BANK b [,o,p,n]: copies sprite patterns from RAM bank b to the sprites' pattern\nmemory (port $5B): n patterns (1-64) of 256 bytes from offset o in the bank (0-65535, the\nbytes must lie in the bank), into pattern slots p (0-63) on (p + n at most 64); anything out\nof range is report B. With only b: all 64 patterns from the bank's start. Checking stops at\nSTATEMENT_END.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: the bank"},
        "1680": {"comment":"Only the bank?"},
        "1684": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8: offset and first slot"},
        "1687": {"comment":"A ',' must follow"},
        "1691": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: the count"},
        "1694": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1697": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: the count"},
        "1700": {"comment":"0 patterns: report B"},
        "1704": {"comment":"More than 64: report B"},
        "1709": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "1710": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "1711": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: the first slot"},
        "1714": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "1715": {"comment":"64 or more: report B"},
        "1720": {"comment":"C = the first slot"},
        "1721": {"comment":"First + count past 64: report B"},
        "1730": {"comment":"Keep them"},
        "1731": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_WORD: the offset"},
        "1734": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "1736": {"comment":"Count and first slot back"},
        "1739": {"synopsis":"Only the bank: B = 64 patterns, C = slot 0, HL = offset 0.","comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "1742": {"comment":"64 patterns, slot 0, offset 0"},
        "1747": {"synopsis":"B = the count, C = the first slot, HL = the offset: the bank taken (ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3\nchecks it and gives its upper 8K page), paged in at $C000 (MMU 6 and 7) on the other stack\n(SWAP_SP); report B when the patterns would run past the bank's end; slot C selected (port\n$303B); B blocks of 256 bytes out to port $5B; then bank 0 and the stack back\n(SWAP_SP_BANK0).","comment":"Keep them"},
        "1749": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: the bank"},
        "1752": {"comment":"Offset, count and slot back"},
        "1754": {"comment":"ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3: A = the bank's upper page"},
        "1757": {"comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "1760": {"comment":"HL = $C000 + the offset"},
        "1764": {"comment":"The bank at $C000-$FFFF"},
        "1771": {"comment":"Keep count and offset"},
        "1773": {"comment":"BC = 256 x the count - 1"},
        "1776": {"comment":"Would the last byte be past the bank's end?"},
        "1779": {"comment":"Yes: report B, the stack back first"},
        "1782": {"comment":"Select the first pattern slot"},
        "1788": {"synopsis":"One pattern: 256 bytes by OTIR.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "1789": {"comment":"256 bytes to port $5B"},
        "1794": {"comment":"Count back; next pattern"},
        "1797": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "1801": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the stack back"},
        "1805": {"synopsis":"Sends a sprite's record to the sprite slot selected by port $303B: its attribute bytes\nthrough port $57, rebuilt.\n1. Bytes 0 and 1 (X, Y) as they are.\n2. Byte 2; for a relative sprite (record byte 3 bit 6) its bit 0 is record byte 4's bit 7.\n3. Byte 3 with bit 6 set, so byte 4 always follows.\n4. Byte 4: for an anchor the record's bits 5-1 (bits 7-6 and 0 clear: an 8-bit pattern, Y\n   below 256); for a relative $40 with the record's bits 4-1 and bit 0 from its bit 6.\nEntry: HL = the record.\nExit: HL = the record + 4.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"BC = port $57, sprite attributes"},
        "1808": {"comment":"Byte 0: x"},
        "1812": {"comment":"Byte 1: y"},
        "1816": {"comment":"A = byte 2"},
        "1818": {"comment":"E = byte 3, D = byte 4"},
        "1821": {"comment":"A relative sprite?"},
        "1825": {"comment":"Yes: bit 0 from byte 4 bit 7"},
        "1833": {"synopsis":"Byte 2 out; then byte 3 with bit 6 set.","comment":"Byte 2 out"},
        "1835": {"comment":"Byte 3 with bit 6 set: byte 4 follows"},
        "1840": {"comment":"A = byte 4"},
        "1841": {"comment":"A relative sprite?"},
        "1845": {"comment":"Relative: bits 4-1 and $40"},
        "1849": {"comment":"Bit 0 from byte 4 bit 6"},
        "1855": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1857": {"synopsis":"An anchor's byte 4: bits 5-1 only.","comment":"Anchor: bits 5-1 only"},
        "1859": {"synopsis":"Byte 4 out.","comment":"Byte 4 out"},
        "1862": {"synopsis":"SET_FIELDS' table for SPRITE n,... with n not negative (an anchor or a plain sprite),\n$0746-$0756. First a byte ORed into record byte 3 after its bit 6 is cleared ($00: not\nrelative; with bit 7 set the byte would be left alone). Then two bytes for each of the 8\nplaces: the size in bits (bits 5-0; bit 7 set: the value may be negative); then where it\ngoes: the record's byte (high nibble) and the shift (low nibble), 1 for nothing stored,\n$FD-$FF for PUT_SPECIAL. Here: n 7 bits (not stored); x 9 bits to byte 0 (bit 8 to byte 2\nbit 0; at most 319); y 8 bits to byte 1; the pattern 6 bits to byte 3; the flags 8 bits\n($FF: bits 7-1 to byte 2, bit 0 to byte 3 bit 7, visible); 3 bits to byte 4 bits 7-5 ($FE);\n2 bits to byte 4 bits 4-3 (X scale); 2 bits to byte 4 bits 2-1 (Y scale). Read by\nSPR_SET_DONE ($0657)."},
        "1879": {"synopsis":"SET_FIELDS' table for SPRITE -n,... (a relative sprite), $0757-$0767, laid out as\nSPRITE_FIELDS: $40 sets record byte 3 bit 6 (relative); x and y are 7 bits with a sign ($87:\noffsets from the anchor) into bytes 0 and 1; the other places as in SPRITE_FIELDS. Read by\nSPR_SET_DONE ($0660)."},
        "1896": {"synopsis":"SET_FIELDS' table for SPRITE CONTINUE's 12 places, $0768-$0780, laid out as SPRITE_FIELDS:\n$80 leaves record byte 3 alone. n; x1 and x2, 9 bits each, to bytes 6 and 7 (their bits 8 to\nbit 0 of bytes 8 and 9); the x step, 7 bits and a sign, to byte $0A; y1 and y2 to bytes $0B\nand $0C; the y step, signed, to byte $0D; the first and last pattern, 6 bits each, to bits\n6-1 of bytes 8 and 9; the flags ($FD, PUT_SPECIAL); the delay to byte $0E and the count to\nbyte $0F. Read by SPR_CONTINUE ($0B1E)."},
        "1921": {"synopsis":"Takes A numbers off the calculator stack into the words at $5C9A + 2 x place (place 0\nfirst), last place first: BC's low A bits say which places were given (the last place in bit\n0); a given value through ROM 1's FP_TO_BC (past 65535: SPR_ERR_B). The signs are shifted\ninto DE, so the first place's ends in D bit 7 and the next ones below it. An empty place's\nword and sign bit are left meaningless.\nEntry: A = the places, BC = the flags.\nExit: DE = the signs.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "1922": {"comment":"HL = $5C9A + 4 x the count, then down"},
        "1929": {"synopsis":"One place, from the last: its flag to carry, BC rotated for the next.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "1930": {"comment":"Rotate the flags: this place's to carry"},
        "1936": {"comment":"Keep flags, signs and pointer"},
        "1939": {"comment":"Not given: skip it"},
        "1941": {"comment":"ROM 1's FP_TO_BC: BC = |value|"},
        "1944": {"synopsis":"The value's word stored; its sign into DE.","comment":"Pointer and signs back"},
        "1946": {"comment":"Past 65535: report B"},
        "1948": {"comment":"Positive: a 0 sign"},
        "1950": {"comment":"Negative: a 1 sign"},
        "1951": {"synopsis":"The sign bit (carry) into D and E.","comment":"The sign into DE"},
        "1955": {"comment":"The word stored"},
        "1959": {"comment":"Flags and count back"},
        "1961": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "1964": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "1966": {"synopsis":"Puts the values at $5C9A into sprite ($5C9A)'s record by the table at HL (SPRITE_FIELDS'\nlayout):\n1. The sprite selected and its record found (SELECT_SPRITE: port $303B, page $10 at $2000);\n   the table's first byte into record byte 3, as SPRITE_FIELDS says.\n2. For each place given (BC's flags, the first place in the top bit) PUT_FIELD with its\n   value and its sign (D bit 7).\nEntry: HL = the table, BC = the flags, DE = the signs.\nExit: HL = the record; page $10 still at $2000.\nChanges: all, and the second register set.","comment":"A = the sprite number, place 0's value"},
        "1970": {"comment":"Select it; DE = its record"},
        "1973": {"comment":"HL' = the record"},
        "1978": {"comment":"Byte 3 with bit 6 cleared"},
        "1982": {"comment":"Merge the table's first byte"},
        "1983": {"comment":"Bit 7: leave byte 3 alone?"},
        "1988": {"comment":"Store byte 3"},
        "1991": {"synopsis":"A' = 0, the offset of place 0's word.","comment":"A' = place 0's offset"},
        "1993": {"synopsis":"One place: its flag to carry, its word into BC, PUT_FIELD when given.","comment":"This place's flag to carry"},
        "1997": {"comment":"Keep flags and the table pointer"},
        "1999": {"comment":"BC = the place's word"},
        "2011": {"comment":"Table pointer back"},
        "2012": {"comment":"Given: store the value"},
        "2015": {"comment":"Next table entry"},
        "2017": {"comment":"Next sign bit to D bit 7"},
        "2021": {"comment":"Flags back; places left?"},
        "2026": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "2028": {"synopsis":"Puts one value into the record (the second set's HL) by its table entry at HL.\n1. The value must fit the entry's size in bits; -128 passes for a 7-bit entry when negative\n   (the second set's DE is the mask of the bits above the size).\n2. A negative value only for a signed entry (bit 7), stored as its two's complement;\n   otherwise report B (SPR_ERR_B).\n3. Stored by PF_STORE.\nEntry: HL = the entry, BC = the value, D bit 7 = its sign.","comment":"A = the entry's size in bits"},
        "2031": {"comment":"Keep the value"},
        "2033": {"comment":"DE' = the mask of the bits above the size"},
        "2039": {"comment":"The value back"},
        "2040": {"comment":"High byte past the size: report B"},
        "2044": {"comment":"Low byte past the size?"},
        "2048": {"comment":"Only -128 may pass"},
        "2053": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "2057": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "2059": {"synopsis":"The value fits; is it negative where that is not allowed?","comment":"A signed entry?"},
        "2064": {"comment":"Negative where not allowed?"},
        "2068": {"synopsis":"Report B (error code $0A, Integer out of range) through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A, after\nPAGE_ROM_IY (MMU 1 and IY back).","comment":"MMU 1 and IY back"},
        "2071": {"comment":"Error code $0A, report B"},
        "2073": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "2076": {"synopsis":"A signed entry: a negative value made two's complement.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "2081": {"comment":"Yes: two's complement"},
        "2085": {"synopsis":"The mask widened by one bit (the sign's).","comment":"Mask one bit wider"},
        "2089": {"synopsis":"Where it goes: the entry's second byte. 1: nothing; $FD-$FF: PUT_SPECIAL; otherwise the byte\nat the record + the high nibble, the value and mask shifted left by the low nibble and\nmerged in; a 9-bit value's bit 8 into bit 0 of the byte two further on, the value at most\n319.","comment":"A = where it goes"},
        "2092": {"comment":"1: nothing stored (the sprite number)"},
        "2095": {"comment":"Keep the record pointer"},
        "2097": {"comment":"$FD-$FF: the special entries"},
        "2101": {"comment":"HL' = the record + the high nibble"},
        "2108": {"comment":"The low nibble: the shift"},
        "2113": {"synopsis":"Value and mask rotated into place.","comment":"Mask and value rotated"},
        "2120": {"synopsis":"The value merged into the byte, the other bits kept.","comment":"Merge the value in, other bits kept"},
        "2124": {"comment":"9 bits?"},
        "2127": {"comment":"Byte two on: bit 0 = bit 8"},
        "2134": {"comment":"X past 319: report B"},
        "2141": {"synopsis":"Done: the record pointer back, the first register set again.","comment":"Record pointer back"},
        "2144": {"synopsis":"SPRITE OVER (a,b [TO c] [,d [,e]]) for ROM 3's SPRITE_OVER_FN ($39AF), which calls here\nthrough its $1EF2: checks whether sprite a overlaps any of the sprites b to c (OVER_SEARCH),\na's box made d pixels narrower on each side and e pixels shorter at top and bottom. Checking\nsyntax it returns at once. Any number from 128, or c below b, is report B.\nEntry: L = a, A = b, H = c, D = d, E = e.\nExit: A = the first sprite found ($80 for sprite 0), 0 for none; MMU 1 = $FF, IY = $5C3A.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "2149": {"comment":"C = b"},
        "2150": {"comment":"Any number 128 or more?"},
        "2155": {"synopsis":"Report B (SPR_ERR_B) when a number is 128 or more."},
        "2157": {"comment":"Is c below b?"},
        "2161": {"comment":"B = the count, c - b + 1"},
        "2163": {"comment":"A = a; the search"},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"MMU 1 = $FF (the ROM back at $2000-$3FFF) and IY = $5C3A, the system variables.","comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "2171": {"comment":"IY = the system variables"},
        "2176": {"synopsis":"The special entries, on the record + 2 (the second set's HL): $FF, the flags: bits 7-1 into\nbyte 2 (palette offset, mirrors, turn), bit 0 into byte 3 bit 7 (visible).","comment":"HL' = the record + 2"},
        "2178": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "2181": {"comment":"Keep byte 2's bit 0"},
        "2185": {"comment":"Bits 7-1 from the flags"},
        "2190": {"comment":"Byte 3: bit 7 = the flags' bit 0"},
        "2199": {"synopsis":"$FE: 3 bits into byte 4 bits 7-5, its bits 4-0 kept.","comment":"HL' = the record + 4"},
        "2201": {"comment":"$FE?"},
        "2204": {"comment":"Keep bits 4-0"},
        "2208": {"comment":"The 3 bits to bits 7-5"},
        "2216": {"synopsis":"$FD, SPRITE CONTINUE's flags: bit 7 into byte 4 bit 0 (mirror and turn follow the\ndirection), bits 5-0 into byte 5 (bits 7-6 kept), bit 6 into byte 8 bit 7 (animate even when\nnot moving).","comment":"$FD: byte 4 bit 0 = flags bit 7"},
        "2224": {"synopsis":"Bits 5-0 into byte 5; then bit 6 into byte 8 bit 7.","comment":"Byte 5: keep bits 7-6"},
        "2229": {"comment":"Bits 5-0 from the flags"},
        "2234": {"comment":"Byte 8: bit 7 = flags bit 6"},
        "2247": {"synopsis":"SPRITE AT (n,i) for ROM 3's SPRITE_CALL ($39A4, with L = AT), called through its $1EF2: a\nvalue of sprite n, in DE. L = AT ($AC): i = 0 its x, 1 its y (SPRITE_BOX), 2 its pattern (a\nrelative sprite with relative patterns adds its anchor's), 3 its x step, 4 its y step (both\nsigned), 5 its delay count; 0 for each when it is hidden. L = CONTINUE ($E8): 0 when it is\nnot moving, else 1, + 2 when y moves, + 4 when x moves. Any other L: 1 when the sprite and\nits anchor are both visible, else 0. Checking syntax: returns at once.\nEntry: E = n (report B from 128), D = i, L = the token.\nExit: DE; MMU 1 = $FF, IY = $5C3A.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "2252": {"comment":"C = the token"},
        "2253": {"comment":"Sprite 128 or more: report B"},
        "2255": {"synopsis":"n must be below 128 (also the way back for i from 6: B counted down again)."},
        "2257": {"comment":"IY = the record, IX = the anchor"},
        "2263": {"comment":"CONTINUE?"},
        "2268": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "2272": {"comment":"Anchor visible?"},
        "2278": {"comment":"And the sprite itself?"},
        "2282": {"synopsis":"DE = 1 with NZ, 0 with Z; then PAGE_ROM_IY.","comment":"DE = 1 when visible"},
        "2287": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "2288": {"synopsis":"Return with DE (PAGE_ROM_IY).","comment":"Return DE"},
        "2290": {"synopsis":"CONTINUE: is the sprite in the moving map?","comment":"Is it in the moving map?"},
        "2295": {"comment":"No: DE = 0"},
        "2298": {"comment":"Bits 7-6 of byte 5: x and y moving"},
        "2303": {"comment":"1 + 2 for y + 4 for x"},
        "2312": {"synopsis":"AT: the sprite's box (0 when hidden), then the item chosen by B.","comment":"Keep the item number"},
        "2313": {"comment":"The sprite's box; hidden?"},
        "2316": {"comment":"B = the item"},
        "2317": {"comment":"Hidden: DE = 0"},
        "2319": {"comment":"DE = x"},
        "2320": {"comment":"Item 0?"},
        "2324": {"comment":"DE = y"},
        "2325": {"comment":"Item 1?"},
        "2328": {"comment":"Item 2?"},
        "2330": {"comment":"Item 2: the pattern"},
        "2333": {"comment":"A relative sprite?"},
        "2337": {"comment":"With a relative pattern?"},
        "2343": {"comment":"Add the anchor's pattern"},
        "2346": {"synopsis":"The pattern number, 0-63.","comment":"DE = the pattern number"},
        "2353": {"synopsis":"Items 3 and up: the x step, the y step or the delay count.","comment":"The x step"},
        "2356": {"comment":"Item 3?"},
        "2359": {"comment":"The y step"},
        "2362": {"comment":"Item 4?"},
        "2364": {"synopsis":"DE = A sign-extended.","comment":"DE = A sign-extended"},
        "2370": {"synopsis":"Item 5: byte $0F, the delay count; higher items go round again.","comment":"Item 5?"},
        "2372": {"comment":"DE = byte $0F, the count"},
        "2379": {"synopsis":"SPRITE_OVER's search: sprite A's box (SPRITE_ANCHOR, SPRITE_BOX; none when hidden), moved in\nby D across and E down and shrunk to match (report B when nothing is left), kept in the\nsecond register set. Then the B sprites from C on, and any relatives after the last: each\nvisible one tested by SPAN_APART on both axes.\nExit: A = the first sprite that overlaps ($80 for sprite 0) or 0, Z for none.","comment":"Sprite a: IY its record, IX its anchor"},
        "2383": {"comment":"Its box; hidden?"},
        "2386": {"comment":"Hidden: nothing overlaps"},
        "2388": {"comment":"X + $4000"},
        "2392": {"comment":"Y + $4000"},
        "2396": {"comment":"X moved in by d"},
        "2401": {"comment":"Width less 2 x d: nothing left?"},
        "2403": {"synopsis":"The span left after taking 2 x the margin off: none is report B."},
        "2406": {"comment":"B = the new width"},
        "2409": {"comment":"Y moved in by e"},
        "2414": {"comment":"Height less 2 x e"},
        "2418": {"comment":"C = the new height"},
        "2421": {"comment":"The first of b..c"},
        "2426": {"synopsis":"One sprite: its box; carry from SPAN_APART on either axis means no overlap.","comment":"Keep count and number"},
        "2427": {"comment":"Its box; hidden?"},
        "2432": {"comment":"X + $4000, as sprite a's"},
        "2436": {"comment":"Y + $4000"},
        "2440": {"comment":"Apart in y?"},
        "2445": {"comment":"Swap axes"},
        "2448": {"comment":"Apart in x?"},
        "2451": {"comment":"Swap axes back"},
        "2456": {"comment":"Apart: next"},
        "2458": {"comment":"Overlap: A = the sprite number"},
        "2461": {"comment":"0 would read as none: $80"},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"Not overlapping: an anchor becomes IX for the relatives after it.","comment":"A relative sprite?"},
        "2471": {"comment":"No: the new anchor"},
        "2475": {"synopsis":"The next record, the next sprite number.","comment":"IY on to the next record"},
        "2480": {"comment":"Count and number back"},
        "2481": {"comment":"Next number; more?"},
        "2484": {"comment":"Past sprite 127?"},
        "2488": {"comment":"One more if the next is a relative"},
        "2496": {"synopsis":"No overlap: A = 0, Z.","comment":"None: A = 0"},
        "2498": {"synopsis":"Selects sprite slot (or pattern slot) A through port $303B, pages 8K page $10 in at $2000\n(MMU 1) and points DE at sprite A's 16-byte record there ($24DF + 16 x A). The record: bytes\n0-4 the attributes; 5 the movement flags; 6-9 the x limits and pattern range; $0A the x\nstep; $0B-$0C the y limits; $0D the y step; $0E the delay; $0F the count.\nChanges: BC, DE.","comment":"Select slot A"},
        "2503": {"synopsis":"SELECT_SPRITE without the port: page $10 at $2000, DE = sprite A's record.","comment":"Page $10 at $2000"},
        "2507": {"synopsis":"DE = $24DF + 16 x A, sprite A's record (page $10 already at $2000).","comment":"DE = $24DF + 16 x A"},
        "2517": {"synopsis":"A = NextReg $14, the global transparency colour (READ_NEXTREG).","comment":"NextReg $14: the transparency colour"},
        "2519": {"synopsis":"A = NextReg A, through ports $243B and $253B.\nExit: BC = $253B, so an OUT (C) writes the same register.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Select NextReg A"},
        "2524": {"comment":"Read it through port $253B"},
        "2528": {"synopsis":"Carry when two spans on one axis do not overlap: [DE, DE + C - 1] of this register set and\nof the other. The set whose span starts first is made current (EXX), and carry says whether\nits span ends before the other starts.\nChanges: AF, AF', the current register set.","comment":"This set's y against the other's"},
        "2535": {"comment":"This set's y lower: stay"},
        "2537": {"comment":"Otherwise the other set"},
        "2538": {"synopsis":"The set with the lower start is current: its end against the other's start.","comment":"Keep the result"},
        "2539": {"comment":"HL = this set's end, y + C - 1"},
        "2549": {"comment":"Against the other set's start"},
        "2556": {"comment":"Back to the set the test began in"},
        "2559": {"synopsis":"Carry from the test; back to the right register set."},
        "2561": {"synopsis":"Swaps the axes in both register sets: HL with DE, B with C.","comment":"HL with DE, B with C"},
        "2565": {"comment":"The same in the other set"},
        "2572": {"synopsis":"IY = sprite A's record, IX = its anchor's: the nearest record at or before it whose byte 3\nbit 6 is clear (not relative). Page $10 at $2000 (SPRITE_REC_PAGE).\nChanges: DE.","comment":"Page $10; DE = the record"},
        "2575": {"comment":"IY and IX = the record"},
        "2581": {"comment":"DE = -16"},
        "2584": {"synopsis":"Back a record while IX is a relative sprite.","comment":"IX relative? Back one record"},
        "2593": {"synopsis":"Sprite IY's box on the sprite screen: Z when it is hidden (byte 3 bit 7 clear, or for a\nrelative sprite its anchor IX hidden). Otherwise HL = x, DE = y, B = the width, C = the\nheight (16 pixels times the scale), NZ. A relative sprite's offsets (bytes 0 and 1, signed)\nare added to its anchor's place: for a unified one (anchor byte 4 bit 5) turned, mirrored\nand scaled as the anchor is, its size by the anchor's scale; for a composite one unscaled,\nits size by its own scale.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Visible?"},
        "2598": {"comment":"A relative sprite?"},
        "2604": {"comment":"HL = x, 9 bits"},
        "2613": {"comment":"DE = y"},
        "2618": {"comment":"A = byte 4, shifted: the scales"},
        "2622": {"synopsis":"C = 16 << the Y scale (bits 1-0 of A), B = 16 << the X scale (bits 3-2); NZ.","comment":"Keep it"},
        "2623": {"comment":"Y scale"},
        "2625": {"comment":"C = 16 << the Y scale"},
        "2629": {"synopsis":"C doubled once for each step of the Y scale."},
        "2634": {"synopsis":"The X scale next.","comment":"The X scale"},
        "2639": {"comment":"B = 16 << the X scale"},
        "2643": {"synopsis":"B doubled once for each step of the X scale."},
        "2648": {"synopsis":"A = 1 after the loops: NZ.","comment":"NZ: visible"},
        "2650": {"synopsis":"A relative sprite: its anchor must be visible; HL, DE = the anchor's x and y; C, B = its own\nx and y offsets.","comment":"Anchor visible?"},
        "2655": {"comment":"HL = the anchor's x"},
        "2664": {"comment":"DE = the anchor's y"},
        "2669": {"comment":"Own scale bits into A's high nibble"},
        "2677": {"comment":"C = the x offset, B = the y offset"},
        "2683": {"comment":"Unified with the anchor?"},
        "2689": {"comment":"Anchor turned?"},
        "2695": {"comment":"Turned: offsets swapped"},
        "2698": {"comment":"Turned: x negated unless X mirror"},
        "2706": {"synopsis":"Anchor not turned: X mirror negates the x offset.","comment":"X mirror?"},
        "2712": {"synopsis":"x offset negated.","comment":"The x offset negated"},
        "2716": {"synopsis":"Anchor's Y mirror negates the y offset.","comment":"Y mirror?"},
        "2722": {"comment":"The y offset negated"},
        "2726": {"synopsis":"A unified sprite takes the anchor's scale, in both nibbles of A.","comment":"The anchor's scale, both nibbles"},
        "2738": {"synopsis":"The offsets added: y scaled by A's bits 1-0, x by bits 3-2.","comment":"Keep the offsets and the scales"},
        "2740": {"comment":"BC = the y offset sign-extended"},
        "2746": {"comment":"The Y scale"},
        "2751": {"synopsis":"BC doubled once for each step of the scale.","comment":"BC doubled"},
        "2758": {"synopsis":"DE = the anchor's y + the y offset.","comment":"DE = the anchor's y + the offset"},
        "2761": {"comment":"Scales and offsets back"},
        "2763": {"comment":"BC = the x offset sign-extended"},
        "2768": {"comment":"The X scale"},
        "2776": {"synopsis":"BC doubled once for each step of the scale.","comment":"BC doubled"},
        "2783": {"synopsis":"HL = the anchor's x + the x offset; then the size from A's high nibble.","comment":"HL = the anchor's x + the offset"},
        "2784": {"comment":"The size scales into bits 3-0"},
        "2787": {"comment":"Width and height from them"},
        "2790": {"synopsis":"SPRITE CONTINUE n [,x1 [TO x2]] [STEP s] [RUN|STOP] [,y1 [TO y2] [STEP t] [RUN|STOP]] [,p1\n[TO p2]] [,f] [,d] [,c]: sets sprite n moving. Without a ',' after n it is SPRITE CONTINUE n\n[TO m] (SPR_RESUME): those sprites move again as they were.\n1. n (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6).\n2. The x and y parts by ROM 1's OPT_RANGE_STEP (each a given bit per number into HL; RUN or\n   STOP into D, RUN's 1 into E), the pattern range by OPT_RANGE, the last three by\n   OPT_NUMBER.\n3. Checking stops at STATEMENT_END.\n4. The 12 places taken (TAKE_VALUES) and put in by MOTION_FIELDS (SET_FIELDS); a pattern\n   range given starts the animation forward (byte 9 bit 7 cleared); RUN sets and STOP clears\n   byte 5 bit 7 (x) or bit 6 (y).\n5. The sprite's bit set in the moving map; MMU 1 = $FF.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: n"},
        "2793": {"comment":"A ',' after n?"},
        "2795": {"comment":"No: SPRITE CONTINUE n [TO m] (SPR_RESUME)"},
        "2798": {"comment":"HL = 1 (n given), DE = 0"},
        "2803": {"comment":"ROM 1's OPT_RANGE_STEP: the x part"},
        "2806": {"comment":"ROM 1's OPT_RANGE_STEP: the y part"},
        "2809": {"comment":"RUN/STOP bits up to bits 7-6"},
        "2813": {"comment":"Keep them"},
        "2814": {"comment":"ROM 1's OPT_RANGE: the pattern range"},
        "2817": {"comment":"Three more places"},
        "2819": {"synopsis":"Three optional numbers: a given bit each into HL (ROM 1's SHIFT_CARRY_HL)."},
        "2820": {"comment":"An optional number"},
        "2824": {"comment":"Flags back"},
        "2825": {"comment":"Its bit into HL: ROM 1's SHIFT_CARRY_HL"},
        "2830": {"comment":"Next of the three"},
        "2833": {"comment":"RUN/STOP bits back"},
        "2834": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "2837": {"comment":"Keep them, and the flags"},
        "2839": {"comment":"12 places off the calculator stack"},
        "2846": {"comment":"Put in by MOTION_FIELDS"},
        "2852": {"comment":"IX = the record"},
        "2855": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "2856": {"comment":"Pattern range given?"},
        "2860": {"comment":"Yes: the animation goes forward"},
        "2864": {"comment":"The RUN/STOP bits","synopsis":"The RUN/STOP bits taken back from the stack into byte 5 of the sprite's record."},
        "2868": {"comment":"Byte 5 bits 7-6 for RUN or STOP given"},
        "2877": {"comment":"Set the sprite's moving bit"},
        "2878": {"synopsis":"With carry: the sprite's moving bit set ($0B65), then the ROM back at $2000 (from $067D)."},
        "2881": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "2886": {"synopsis":"An optional ',n' at CH_ADD: no ',' gives NZ, no carry; a ',' and another ',' (left empty) Z,\nno carry, CH_ADD at the second ','; otherwise the number (ROM 1's CLASS_6) and carry.","comment":"A ','?"},
        "2891": {"comment":"No: NZ, no carry"},
        "2892": {"comment":"Past it; another ','?"},
        "2896": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: the number"},
        "2899": {"comment":"Given: carry"},
        "2901": {"synopsis":"HL = sprite A's byte in the two maps at $2CDF (page $10), one pair of bytes for each 8\nsprites: with no carry the changed map ($2CDF + 2 x (A / 8)), with carry the moving map (the\nbyte after); A = the sprite's bit ($80 for A mod 8 = 0).\nChanges: E (= the sprite), F.","comment":"The changed map"},
        "2904": {"comment":"Carry: the moving map"},
        "2907": {"synopsis":"E = the sprite; HL on to its pair of bytes.","comment":"E = the sprite"},
        "2908": {"comment":"2 x (A / 8): its pair of bytes"},
        "2914": {"comment":"A = the sprite's bit"},
        "2917": {"synopsis":"Sets sprite ($5C9A)'s bit in a map: no carry, changed (shown at the next SPRITE MOVE);\ncarry, moving.","comment":"A = the sprite number"},
        "2920": {"synopsis":"MARK_SPRITE for sprite A.","comment":"The bit set"},
        "2926": {"synopsis":"SPRITE CONTINUE n [TO m] (SPR_CONTINUE when no ',' follows n): sets the moving bit of\nsprites n to m (C to B), taken by SPR_RANGE (n [TO m] at CH_ADD); MMU 1 = $FF after.","comment":"C = n, B = m"},
        "2929": {"synopsis":"One sprite of the range.","comment":"Keep them"},
        "2930": {"comment":"Set this sprite's moving bit"},
        "2935": {"comment":"Next; past m?"},
        "2941": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "2946": {"synopsis":"SPRITE PAUSE n [TO m]: sprites n to m stop moving (their bits in the moving map cleared). n\nby ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6, the rest by SPR_RANGE.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: n"},
        "2949": {"comment":"C = n, B = m"},
        "2952": {"synopsis":"One sprite of the range: its moving bit cleared.","comment":"Keep them"},
        "2953": {"comment":"Clear this sprite's moving bit"},
        "2961": {"comment":"Next; past m?"},
        "2967": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "2972": {"synopsis":"n [TO m] (A = the character after n): TO m (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6); the statement's end with\nthis routine's return taken off, so checking stops here; then C = n and B = m (both below\n128, m not below n, else report B); page $10 at $2000. Without TO, B = C = n.","comment":"TO?"},
        "2976": {"comment":"Off the stack: checking stops here"},
        "2981": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: n"},
        "2984": {"comment":"B = C = n"},
        "2988": {"synopsis":"TO m: the number, the statement's end, both bytes taken.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: m"},
        "2991": {"comment":"Off the stack: checking stops here"},
        "2996": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: m"},
        "2999": {"comment":"B = m"},
        "3001": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: n"},
        "3004": {"comment":"C = n"},
        "3006": {"synopsis":"Both below 128, B not below C; page $10 at $2000.","comment":"Either 128 or more: report B"},
        "3013": {"comment":"Report B when m is below n"},
        "3018": {"comment":"Page $10 at $2000"},
        "3023": {"synopsis":"SPRITE MOVE [INT [n]]: shows the changes and moves the moving sprites one step\n(SPRITE_UPDATE). With INT alone a HALT first (the next frame); with INT n the CPU at 28 MHz\n(NextReg 7 = 3) until the active video line (NextRegs $1E, $1F) is n - 32 (0 for n below\n32), then the speed back. Checking stops at STATEMENT_END.","comment":"Past MOVE; INT?"},
        "3028": {"comment":"Past INT"},
        "3029": {"comment":"ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST: a number?"},
        "3032": {"comment":"None: a HALT"},
        "3034": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_6: n"},
        "3037": {"comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "3040": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: n"},
        "3043": {"comment":"L = n - 32, or 0"},
        "3050": {"synopsis":"L = the line; the speed kept in H, 28 MHz meanwhile.","comment":"H = the CPU speed (NextReg 7)"},
        "3056": {"comment":"28 MHz meanwhile"},
        "3060": {"synopsis":"Wait for line L: the line's MSB must be 0, its LSB L.","comment":"Line MSB (NextReg $1E) still 1?"},
        "3069": {"comment":"Line LSB (NextReg $1F) = L?"},
        "3077": {"comment":"Speed back"},
        "3083": {"synopsis":"INT alone: one frame.","comment":"Wait for the next frame"},
        "3084": {"synopsis":"The statement's end; then SPRITE_UPDATE.","comment":"Checking stops here"},
        "3087": {"synopsis":"Goes through the 128 sprites' maps at $2CDF (page $10), 8 sprites a pair of bytes: each\nchanged byte cleared as it is read. A moving sprite gets one step (SPRITE_STEP) and, with\nrecord byte 4 bit 0 set, mirror and turn bits from its direction (DIR_BITS); every sprite\nmoved or changed has its record sent to the hardware (UPLOAD_ATTRS). Also from SPR_RUN.\nExit: MMU 1 = $FF.","comment":"Page $10 at $2000"},
        "3091": {"comment":"HL before the first pair; B = -1"},
        "3096": {"synopsis":"Next pair: E = the changed byte (cleared), D = the moving byte.","comment":"E = the changed byte, then cleared"},
        "3100": {"comment":"D = the moving byte"},
        "3102": {"comment":"Any bit in either?"},
        "3106": {"comment":"E = both maps' bits"},
        "3107": {"comment":"A = the next sprite number"},
        "3108": {"synopsis":"Next sprite of the 8: moving, changed, or neither."},
        "3109": {"comment":"Moving?"},
        "3113": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "3117": {"synopsis":"More changed bits in this byte?","comment":"More bits left?"},
        "3119": {"synopsis":"B on by 8; all 16 pairs done?","comment":"B on by 8"},
        "3123": {"comment":"All 128 done?"},
        "3127": {"comment":"The ROM back at $2000"},
        "3132": {"synopsis":"A moving sprite: its record in IX, one step.","comment":"IX = the record"},
        "3139": {"comment":"Keep the sprite number"},
        "3140": {"comment":"One step"},
        "3143": {"comment":"Look follows the direction?"},
        "3149": {"comment":"The x step's sign"},
        "3153": {"comment":"And the y step's"},
        "3159": {"comment":"Each against its moving bit"},
        "3162": {"comment":"A = 0-3"},
        "3166": {"comment":"Byte 2's mirror and turn bits from DIR_BITS"},
        "3180": {"synopsis":"Its changed bit dropped too: it is uploaded now anyway.","comment":"The number back"},
        "3182": {"comment":"Changed bit dropped too"},
        "3184": {"synopsis":"Sprite A selected and its record sent (UPLOAD_ATTRS)."},
        "3185": {"comment":"Select the sprite; DE = its record"},
        "3188": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "3189": {"comment":"Keep the number"},
        "3190": {"comment":"Send the record"},
        "3193": {"comment":"Number back; the next sprite"},
        "3197": {"synopsis":"Byte 2's mirror and turn bits (3-1) for a sprite whose look follows its direction, by\nSPRITE_UPDATE ($0C5E): $06, $08, $00, $02, indexed by the signs of the x and y steps (each\ninverted when that axis moves)."},
        "3201": {"synopsis":"One step of moving sprite IX (the other register set's HL at its byte of the moving map, A'\n= its number).\n1. The count, byte $0F, counted down; at 0 reloaded from byte $0E and the step taken.\n2. When byte 8 bit 7 is set or the sprite moves, the pattern (byte 3 bits 5-0) goes on\n   between the first and last pattern (bits 6-1 of bytes 8 and 9): forward, or back while\n   byte 9 bit 7 is set; at the last it wraps to the first, or with byte 5 bit 4 turns back;\n   with byte 5 bit 5 the sprite stops (STOP_SPRITE) at the end instead.\n3. With byte 5 bit 6, y moves by byte $0D between bytes $0B and $0C.\n4. With byte 5 bit 7, x moves by byte $0A between the 9-bit limits in bytes 6 and 7 (bit 8\n   in bit 0 of bytes 8 and 9). At a limit the step changes sign, the Y or X mirror flips\n   when byte 5 bit 2 or 3 is set, and byte 5 bits 1-0 say: 0 go on, 1 this axis stops and\n   the other starts, 2 this axis stops, 3 STOP_SPRITE.","comment":"Count still running?"},
        "3207": {"comment":"Yes: one less, no step"},
        "3211": {"synopsis":"Count reloaded from the delay; the pattern next.","comment":"Count = the delay"},
        "3217": {"comment":"C = visible and byte-4 bits"},
        "3224": {"comment":"A = the pattern"},
        "3227": {"comment":"Animate always?"},
        "3234": {"comment":"Or when moving?"},
        "3243": {"synopsis":"Animate: E = the first pattern, D = the last, B bit 7 = backwards.","comment":"E = the first pattern"},
        "3247": {"comment":"D = the last pattern"},
        "3255": {"comment":"Backwards?"},
        "3259": {"comment":"One back; still from the first on?"},
        "3266": {"synopsis":"Back at the first pattern: forward again.","comment":"Before the first: forward again"},
        "3273": {"synopsis":"Forward: before the last, the next pattern.","comment":"Before the last?"},
        "3276": {"comment":"At the last: turn back?"},
        "3280": {"comment":"No: wrap to the first"},
        "3283": {"comment":"Yes: backwards from the last"},
        "3288": {"synopsis":"At an end: with byte 5 bit 5 the sprite stops, hidden.","comment":"Stop at the end?"},
        "3295": {"comment":"Yes: the sprite stops"},
        "3298": {"comment":"And stays hidden"},
        "3300": {"synopsis":"The next pattern."},
        "3301": {"synopsis":"Byte 3 = the pattern with the visible and byte-4 bits.","comment":"Byte 3 = the pattern and flags"},
        "3305": {"synopsis":"Movement: C = byte 5's flags; y first, x after.","comment":"HL = the record"},
        "3308": {"comment":"C = byte 5's flags"},
        "3312": {"comment":"A = y"},
        "3314": {"comment":"Is y moving?"},
        "3318": {"comment":"Add the y step"},
        "3322": {"comment":"Moving up?"},
        "3326": {"comment":"D = the lower limit"},
        "3329": {"comment":"Past 0?"},
        "3331": {"comment":"Below the limit?"},
        "3334": {"comment":"Above it: keep it"},
        "3336": {"synopsis":"Below the lower limit or on it: bounce."},
        "3338": {"synopsis":"Moving down: past the upper limit?","comment":"D = the upper limit"},
        "3341": {"comment":"Past 255?"},
        "3343": {"comment":"Below the limit: keep it"},
        "3346": {"synopsis":"Bounce: y step negated, Y mirror flipped when byte 5 bit 2 is set.","comment":"The y step negated"},
        "3352": {"comment":"Y mirror flipped if byte 5 bit 2"},
        "3361": {"comment":"Byte 5 bits 1-0: what next"},
        "3366": {"comment":"3: stop the sprite"},
        "3370": {"comment":"1, 2: y stops"},
        "3374": {"comment":"1: x starts"},
        "3383": {"synopsis":"Mode 3: the sprite stops."},
        "3386": {"synopsis":"Y = the limit reached.","comment":"Y = the limit reached"},
        "3387": {"synopsis":"Byte 1 = the new y.","comment":"Store y"},
        "3388": {"synopsis":"X, when byte 5 bit 7 is set.","comment":"HL = the record"},
        "3389": {"comment":"Is x moving?"},
        "3393": {"comment":"BC = x, 9 bits"},
        "3400": {"comment":"HL = the record + 6"},
        "3404": {"comment":"DE = the lower x limit"},
        "3411": {"comment":"HL = the upper x limit"},
        "3421": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "3422": {"comment":"HL = the x step sign-extended"},
        "3429": {"comment":"BC = the new x"},
        "3432": {"comment":"Upper limit back"},
        "3433": {"comment":"Moving left?"},
        "3437": {"comment":"Below 0?"},
        "3439": {"comment":"Against the lower limit"},
        "3443": {"comment":"Below it: bounce"},
        "3445": {"comment":"HL = the lower limit again"},
        "3446": {"synopsis":"X went below 0: bounce with HL as it is, the upper limit."},
        "3448": {"synopsis":"Moving right: past the upper limit?","comment":"Carry (never, for a positive step)?"},
        "3450": {"comment":"Against the upper limit"},
        "3454": {"comment":"Below it: keep the new x"},
        "3456": {"synopsis":"On or past the upper limit: bounce at it.","comment":"HL = the limit"},
        "3457": {"synopsis":"Bounce: x step negated, X mirror flipped when byte 5 bit 3 is set.","comment":"The x step negated"},
        "3465": {"comment":"X mirror flipped if byte 5 bit 3"},
        "3477": {"comment":"Byte 5 bits 1-0: what next"},
        "3482": {"comment":"3: stop the sprite"},
        "3486": {"comment":"1, 2: x stops"},
        "3490": {"comment":"1: y starts"},
        "3499": {"synopsis":"Mode 3: the sprite stops."},
        "3502": {"synopsis":"X = the limit reached.","comment":"X = the limit reached"},
        "3504": {"synopsis":"Byte 0 and byte 2 bit 0 = the new x.","comment":"Store x: byte 0"},
        "3507": {"comment":"And bit 8 in byte 2 bit 0"},
        "3517": {"synopsis":"Stops sprite IX: hidden (byte 3 bit 7 cleared) and its bit cleared in the moving map (the\nother register set's HL); A' = the sprite's number.\nChanges: E.","comment":"Hidden"},
        "3521": {"comment":"A = the sprite number"},
        "3523": {"comment":"Its bit"},
        "3526": {"comment":"Cleared in the moving map"},
        "3531": {"comment":"A' back"},
        "3534": {"synopsis":"TILE [w,h] [AT x,y] [TO a,b] (token $9B with no sub-keyword: NextZXOS ROM 1's SUBKEY_ENTRIES\nentry at $04FC is class $0E with the word $8DCE, this ROM's $0DCE). Draws tiles from a tile\nmap onto the Layer 2 or LoRes screen.\n1. The tile size from $5C7F (bit 6, or bit 7 when bit 1 is set): 8 pixels on a 32 x 24 tile\n   screen, or 16 on 16 x 12; kept at $5BBE (size), $5BBF (columns), $5BC0 (rows).\n2. The operands: none (the whole screen from the map's start, TL_WHOLE); AT x,y alone\n   (TL_AT_ONLY); or w,h (CLASS_8), then AT x,y ($5B66 bit 7: where in the map to start) and\n   TO a,b ($5B66 bit 6: the screen tile to draw at). Checking stops at $0FC5 (the\n   statement's end and a test of the screen mode, error $5E otherwise).\n3. Running, on the other stack (SWAP_SP): w and h at least 1 and within the tile screen,\n   else report B; the screen address set up by $3616 (C bit 7 set: Layer 2); the banks from\n   $5B73 (LoRes) or $5B75 (Layer 2) into $5BBC and paged at $8000 (tiles) and $C000 (map) by\n   $0FDD, interrupts off; the map's place from the row length at $5B7C/$5B7E and the start\n   at $5B80/$5B82.\n4. The transparent colour: the mode's own one ($5C3F LoRes, $5C40 Layer 2) when TILE BANK\n   ... OVER set the mode's bit in $5B68 (bit 2 LoRes, bit 3 Layer 2), otherwise NextReg\n   $14's. Each tile: its 8 or 16 rows copied by LDIX, which skips bytes of that colour;\n   8-pixel tiles are 64 bytes at $8000 + 64 x n, 16-pixel tiles 256 bytes, 64 to a bank from\n   $5BBC's bank on.\n5. MMU 4-7 back to banks 2 and 0, interrupts on, the stack back ($1177).","comment":"A = the screen mode byte, $5C7F"},
        "3537": {"comment":"Layer 2: the size bit is bit 7"},
        "3542": {"comment":"16-pixel tiles?","synopsis":"The size bit tested (bit 6, or bit 7 for Layer 2 after the RRCA): 8 or 16-pixel tiles."},
        "3544": {"comment":"8 pixels, 32 columns, 24 rows"},
        "3551": {"comment":"16 pixels, 16 columns, 12 rows"},
        "3555": {"comment":"$5BBE = the tile size","synopsis":"Stores the tile size at $5BBE and the columns and rows at $5BBF/$5BC0."},
        "3558": {"comment":"$5BBF = columns, $5BC0 = rows"},
        "3562": {"comment":"AT next?"},
        "3568": {"comment":"ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST: TILE alone?"},
        "3571": {"comment":"Yes: the whole screen"},
        "3574": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_8: w,h"},
        "3577": {"comment":"No AT, no TO yet"},
        "3584": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "3586": {"comment":"TO next?"},
        "3588": {"comment":"AT given"},
        "3590": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8: x,y"},
        "3593": {"comment":"HL back at the flags"},
        "3596": {"synopsis":"TO a,b: $5B66 bit 6, two numbers.","comment":"TO?"},
        "3598": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "3600": {"comment":"TO given"},
        "3602": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8: a,b"},
        "3605": {"synopsis":"TILE when running (from $0E0E): the screen mode tested, then the AT and TO options.","comment":"Checking stops here; the screen mode tested"},
        "3608": {"comment":"TO given?"},
