        "4034": {"synopsis":"On with the drawing.","comment":"On with the drawing"},
        "4037": {"synopsis":"Ends the statement when checking syntax (through $0149: the caller does not come back);\nrunning, the screen mode must be one with tiles ($36B0 gives carry), otherwise error code\n$5E (ERROR_128_A).\nExit: A = the mode from $36B0, 1 for LoRes (also used to choose LoRes's or Layer 2's\nvariables).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "4038": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "4041": {"comment":"The screen mode's tile kind ($36B0): carry when it has one"},
        "4044": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "4045": {"comment":"A mode with tiles: return"},
        "4046": {"comment":"Otherwise error code $5E (NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A)"},
        "4051": {"synopsis":"A = A x 8, or A x 16 when the tiles are 16 x 16 ($5BBE bit 4).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"X 8"},
        "4054": {"comment":"16 x 16 tiles?"},
        "4058": {"comment":"No: x 8 is all"},
        "4059": {"comment":"X 16"},
        "4061": {"synopsis":"Pages 16K bank L at $8000-$BFFF (MMU slots 4-5) and bank H at $C000-$FFFF (MMU slots 6-7):\nHL doubled gives their first 8K pages.\nEntry: L, H = the banks.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"H and L: the banks as 8K page numbers"},
        "4062": {"comment":"Bank L's two pages"},
        "4063": {"comment":"At $8000-$BFFF"},
        "4070": {"comment":"Bank H's two pages"},
        "4071": {"comment":"At $C000-$FFFF"},
        "4079": {"synopsis":"TILE BANK n [OVER t] (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for TILE BANK, the word at its\n$0500; n is on the calculator stack and A is the character after it): with OVER, t too\n(NEXT_CLASS_6). Checking stops at TILE_MODE_TEST. Running, in the current mode (1 LoRes, 2\nLayer 2): the mode's bit in $5B68 (bit 2 LoRes, bit 3 Layer 2) is cleared, and with OVER set\nagain and t (TAKE_BYTE) stored at $5C3F (LoRes) or $5C40 (Layer 2): TILE then skips that\ncolour instead of NextReg $14's. Then bank n is checked through NextZXOS ROM 1's\nBANK_PAGE_ROM3 (past its HL test, at $330B) and becomes the tile bank of the mode: $5B73 for\nLoRes, $5B75 for Layer 2.\nEntry: A = the character after n.","comment":"OVER?"},
        "4081": {"comment":"The flags kept (Z: OVER)"},
        "4082": {"comment":"No OVER: on"},
        "4084": {"comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6: t"},
        "4087": {"synopsis":"B, C = the character after n and its flags (C bit 6: OVER); the mode tested\n(TILE_MODE_TEST); the mode's bit in $5B68 cleared.","comment":"B, C = the character and its flags"},
        "4088": {"comment":"Checking: done; running: A = the mode (1 LoRes)"},
        "4091": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4092": {"comment":"E = the mode's bit (mode x 4)"},
        "4095": {"comment":"D = the mask without it"},
        "4097": {"comment":"The bit cleared in $5B68"},
        "4103": {"comment":"OVER given?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"No: the bank"},
        "4107": {"comment":"Yes: the bit set"},
        "4109": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE: A = t"},
        "4112": {"comment":"B = the mode"},
        "4114": {"comment":"$5C40 for Layer 2"},
        "4117": {"comment":"LoRes?"},
        "4119": {"comment":"Yes: $5C3F"},
        "4120": {"synopsis":"The transparent colour stored for the mode.","comment":"The mode's transparent colour"},
        "4121": {"synopsis":"E = the bank (TAKE_BYTE), checked by NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3 past its HL test.","comment":"A = the bank (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4124": {"comment":"E = the bank"},
        "4125": {"comment":"Is it a bank? (NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3 past its HL test)"},
        "4128": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "4129": {"comment":"LoRes?"},
        "4130": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "4131": {"comment":"Yes"},
