        "7132": {"comment":"PLAY_NEXT ended"},
        "7134": {"synopsis":"One more length in the list: 11 is report o.","comment":"A = the lengths so far + 1"},
        "7138": {"comment":"An eleventh?"},
        "7140": {"comment":"Report o"},
        "7143": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7147": {"synopsis":"No length given: the current one, once.","comment":"Back to the note's name"},
        "7150": {"comment":"One length"},
        "7154": {"comment":"HL = the block's length list"},
        "7157": {"comment":"The string's pointer to it"},
        "7160": {"comment":"C = the current length"},
        "7164": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "7168": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7171": {"synopsis":"Returns two bytes past the call's return: past PLAY_NEXT's JR, which ends it.","comment":"The return address"},
        "7172": {"comment":"Moved past PLAY_NEXT's JR"},
        "7176": {"synopsis":"The string's end: the return address dropped (PLAY_NEXT left), its bit set in $5CAE.","comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "7177": {"synopsis":"The current string's bit ($5CAC) set in $5CAE.","comment":"HL = the ended bits"},
        "7180": {"comment":"The current string's bit added"},
        "7190": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7194": {"synopsis":"HL = the block's list of lengths (IX + 34).","comment":"HL = IX + 34"},
        "7202": {"synopsis":"The string's pointer to its current length (in IY's list at +18) = HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7203": {"comment":"HL = IY + 18"},
        "7210": {"comment":"+ 2 x the string's number"},
        "7218": {"comment":"DE = the list"},
        "7219": {"comment":"The pointer stored"},
        "7222": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "7224": {"synopsis":"The routines of PLAY's commands, from the index PLAY_FIND_LETTER gives (0 for none): a note\n(PLAY_NOTE), '!', O, N, '(', ')', T, M, V, U, W, X, Y, Z, H, L, R, S."},
        "7260": {"synopsis":"W's envelope shapes for 0-7: 0, 4, 11, 13, 8, 12, 14, 10."},
        "7268": {"synopsis":"Looks A up in PLAY_LETTERS (CPIR, BC = 18).\nExit: Z when found; C = its index from the end ('!' is 1, S is 17), 0 when not found.","comment":"18: 17 letters and one"},
        "7271": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_LETTERS"},
        "7274": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "7277": {"synopsis":"The notes A-G within an octave from C: 9, 11, 0, 2, 4, 5, 7."},
        "7284": {"synopsis":"DE = length C's units, from PLAY_LENGTHS. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7285": {"comment":"BC = the length's number"},
        "7287": {"comment":"HL = its entry in PLAY_LENGTHS"},
        "7291": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "7294": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7296": {"synopsis":"The lengths' units for 0-12: $80, then 1-9: 6, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 72, 96; 10-12\n(triplets): 4, 8, 16."},
        "7309": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "7311": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "7312": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "7314": {"comment":"No carry for a digit only"},
        "7316": {"synopsis":"Sounds note A (within the octave) on the string's chip and channel: the octave's base added\n(128 or more is report m); channel A of each chip also sets the chip's noise period (AY\nregister 6) from it; the tone period from PLAY_PERIODS (notes below 21 take $0FBF) into\nregisters 2n and 2n + 1, and with the envelope in use, register 13 = the chip's shape. Kept\nat IX + 0.","comment":"C = the note in the octave"},
        "7317": {"comment":"Plus the octave's base"},
        "7321": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "7323": {"comment":"Report m"},
        "7326": {"comment":"C = the note"},
        "7327": {"comment":"A = the AY channel"},
        "7330": {"comment":"Channel A of its chip?"},
        "7331": {"comment":"No"},
        "7333": {"comment":"Channel A: the noise period from the note"},
        "7337": {"comment":"A quarter"},
        "7341": {"comment":"Register 6"},
        "7344": {"comment":"Written"},
        "7347": {"synopsis":"The note kept; the tone.","comment":"The note kept"},
        "7350": {"comment":"A = the string's number"},
        "7353": {"comment":"9 or more?"},
        "7355": {"comment":"Never: there is no other string"},
        "7356": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_PERIODS"},
        "7361": {"comment":"A = the note"},
        "7362": {"comment":"Less 21"},
        "7364": {"comment":"21 or more"},
