        "7891": {"comment":"Again"},
        "7893": {"synopsis":"The AY tone periods for notes 21 up, one word each: 108 of them (notes 21-128); note 21's\n($0FBF) is also every lower note's; note 60's is $01A8. The 128K ROM 0's table unchanged."},
        "8130": {"synopsis":"The rest of ROM 3's $1FB6, which takes two bytes for PLOT, POINT and DRAW: in screen mode 0\n(the low four bits of $5C7F) ROM 3 goes on itself at its $2307; in any other mode it pages\nthis ROM in (NextReg $8C = $80) and runs on here. ROM 1 is selected (NextReg $8E = $01), and\nthe return address into ROM 3 is taken off and its low byte picks the command: bit 0 set\n(PLOT_CMD, $22DF) PLOT_MODE_1_15 ($2A0D); bit 2 clear (DRAW_LINE, $24BA) DRAW_MODE_1_15\n($2B46); otherwise (POINT_SUB, $22CE) POINT_MODE_1_15 ($2A26). Those carry out the whole\ncommand for the other screen modes.","comment":"ROM 1 selected (the alternate ROM stays in)"},
        "8134": {"comment":"C = the low byte of the return address into ROM 3"},
        "8136": {"comment":"Bit 0: from PLOT_CMD?"},
        "8140": {"comment":"Bit 2 clear: from DRAW_LINE?"},
        "8145": {"comment":"Otherwise from POINT_SUB"},
        "8148": {"synopsis":"CAT [-] [#n] [name] [EXP] (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for CAT, the word at its\n$0371): catalogues a drive's directory:\n1. '-': 8.3 names instead of long ones ($5B66 bit 7). An optional '#' stream, else stream 2\n   (NextZXOS ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2). ASN goes to $21B4 (the drives), TAB to $21F0.\n2. An optional name (a string) and EXP (the details: $5B66 bit 6); checking syntax ends\n   here. A letter before a ':' in the name is the drive ($5B65; 0 for the default one). \"T:\"\n   (either case) is the tape, at $2308.\n3. The name to $E090 in bank 7; with bank 7 paged, DOS_CATALOG (ROM 2) fills the 64-entry\n   buffer at $F700, sorted by long name, with directories (and system files with EXP).\n4. Each entry: its long name from IDE_GET_LFN (ROM 2) or, with '-', its 8.3 name; TAB 25;\n   with EXP its attributes, date and time and size in bytes, otherwise its size in K or\n   \"<DIR>\"; BREAK stops it (NextZXOS ROM 1's BREAK_STOP). A full buffer goes on from its\n   last entry.\n5. \"No files found\" when nothing matched; then the drive's free space (DOS_FREE_SPACE) and \"\n   free\". Errors from ROM 2 stop it through NextZXOS ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0.","comment":"$5B66 bits 7 and 6 cleared: no '-', no EXP"},
        "8155": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "8157": {"comment":"No"},
        "8159": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 7: 8.3 names"},
        "8161": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8162": {"synopsis":"The stream, then what follows.","comment":"An optional '#' stream, else stream 2 (NextZXOS ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2)"},
        "8165": {"comment":"A = the character there"},
        "8166": {"comment":"Z at ENTER or ':' (NextZXOS ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)"},
        "8169": {"comment":"No name: everything"},
        "8171": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "8173": {"comment":"Yes: everything, with the details"},
        "8175": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "8177": {"comment":"Yes: the drives ($21B4)"},
        "8180": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "8182": {"comment":"Yes: the cards ($21F0)"},
        "8185": {"comment":"A string: the name (NextZXOS ROM 1's CLASS_A)"},
        "8188": {"comment":"A = the character after it"},
        "8189": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "8191": {"comment":"No"},
        "8193": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 6: the details"},
        "8198": {"comment":"Past EXP"},
        "8199": {"synopsis":"Checking ends here; running, a drive letter A-Z before a ':' in the name kept at $5B65.","comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "8202": {"comment":"DE = the name, BC = its length (NextZXOS ROM 1's STK_FETCH)"},
        "8205": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "8206": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8208": {"comment":"A ':' in it?"},
        "8212": {"comment":"No: no drive letter"},
        "8214": {"comment":"HL = the character before the ':'"},
        "8216": {"comment":"Capitals"},
        "8219": {"comment":"Below A?"},
        "8221": {"comment":"Not a letter"},
        "8223": {"comment":"Past Z?"},
        "8225": {"comment":"Not a letter"},
        "8227": {"comment":"$5B65 = the drive letter"},
        "8230": {"comment":"On"},
        "8232": {"synopsis":"No drive letter in the name: $5B65 = 0, the default drive.","comment":"$5B65 = 0: the default drive"},
        "8236": {"synopsis":"BC = the length again.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "8237": {"comment":"On"},
        "8239": {"synopsis":"EXP with no name: the details.","comment":"$5B66 bit 6: the details"},
        "8244": {"comment":"Past EXP"},
        "8245": {"synopsis":"Checking ends here; an empty name, the default drive.","comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "8248": {"comment":"$5B65 = 0: the default drive"},
        "8252": {"comment":"BC = 0: no name"},
        "8254": {"synopsis":"A name of two characters, T and ':' (either case): the tape, at $2308.","comment":"Two characters?"},
        "8258": {"comment":"No: the disk"},
        "8260": {"comment":"The second"},
        "8263": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "8265": {"comment":"No: the disk"},
        "8267": {"comment":"The first"},
        "8268": {"comment":"T or t?"},
        "8270": {"comment":"Yes: the tape ($2308)"},
        "8275": {"synopsis":"The name to $E090 in bank 7; bank 7 paged in; the buffer's first entry at $F700 cleared (13\nbytes).","comment":"The name to $E090 in bank 7, $FF after it ($357D)"},
        "8278": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, the other stack"},
        "8281": {"comment":"Entry 0 of the buffer at $F700 cleared: from the start"},
        "8293": {"synopsis":"One part of the catalogue: B = 64 entries, C = $26 (long-name flags, directories, sorting by\nA), $27 with EXP (system files too); then CAT_CALL.","comment":"B = 64 entries, C = $26: long names, directories, sorting"},
        "8296": {"comment":"With EXP?"},
        "8301": {"comment":"No"},
        "8303": {"comment":"C = $27: system files too"},
        "8305": {"synopsis":"DOS_CATALOG (ROM 2) with DE = the buffer at $F700, HL = the name at $E090, A = 8 (sorted by\nlong name).","comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "8308": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8311": {"comment":"A = 8: sorted by long name"},
        "8313": {"comment":"DOS_CATALOG (ROM 2)"},
        "8316": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8318": {"synopsis":"Waits while SPACE is down.","comment":"Keyboard row SPACE-B"},
        "8323": {"comment":"Wait while SPACE is down"},
        "8325": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key yet"},
        "8329": {"comment":"$D803 = the directory handle"},
        "8332": {"comment":"HL = entry 1, the first new one"},
        "8335": {"comment":"B = the new entries"},
        "8337": {"comment":"Any?"},
        "8338": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8340": {"comment":"None: the end"},
        "8343": {"synopsis":"An error from ROM 2: $17 (nothing matched) is CAT_NONE; the others stop it through NextZXOS\nROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0.","comment":"$17: nothing matched?"},
        "8345": {"comment":"Yes: the end"},
        "8348": {"synopsis":"RAM bank 0, then the error in A stops it (NextZXOS ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0). Also reached\nfrom $20B0, $21C9 and $2301.","comment":"Bank 0, the error stops it (NextZXOS ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0)"},
        "8351": {"synopsis":"BC kept, then CAT_ENTRY (from $2092).","comment":"The entries kept"},
        "8352": {"synopsis":"One file: A = the names left, HL = its entry; its long name, date, time and size from\nIDE_GET_LFN (ROM 2), kept by ROM 0's STORE_LFN_INFO.","comment":"The names left kept"},
        "8353": {"comment":"The entry's address kept"},
        "8354": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "8355": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8358": {"comment":"BC = $D82B: the long name's buffer"},
        "8361": {"comment":"IX = the directory handle"},
        "8365": {"comment":"IDE_GET_LFN (ROM 2)"},
        "8368": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8370": {"comment":"The date, time and size kept (ROM 0's STORE_LFN_INFO)"},
        "8375": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8378": {"comment":"BREAK stops it (NextZXOS ROM 1's BREAK_STOP)"},
        "8381": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8384": {"comment":"'-' given ($5B66 bit 7)?"},
        "8388": {"comment":"No: the long name"},
        "8390": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8392": {"comment":"8 name letters"},
        "8394": {"synopsis":"One name letter, without its attribute bit.","comment":"A letter, its attribute bit off"},
        "8398": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8401": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8403": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "8408": {"comment":"3 type letters"},
        "8410": {"synopsis":"One type letter, without its attribute bit.","comment":"A letter, its attribute bit off"},
        "8414": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8417": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8419": {"comment":"On"},
        "8421": {"synopsis":"The long name from $D82B (NextZXOS ROM 1's PRINT_MSG).","comment":"HL = the long name"},
        "8424": {"comment":"Printed (NextZXOS ROM 1's PRINT_MSG)"},
        "8427": {"synopsis":"TAB 25, then the attributes as text (ROM 0's MAKE_ATTR_TEXT); with EXP: they, the date and\ntime, and the size in bytes (or nothing for a directory).","comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8430": {"comment":"TAB 25 and a space ($2409)"},
        "8436": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8439": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8440": {"comment":"+ 7: its attribute letters"},
        "8444": {"comment":"The attributes as text at $5B9D; B bit 0: a directory (ROM 0)"},
        "8449": {"comment":"HL = the size's address, kept"},
        "8450": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8453": {"comment":"EXP given ($5B66 bit 6)?"},
        "8458": {"comment":"No: the size only"},
        "8460": {"comment":"The attributes kept"},
        "8461": {"comment":"8 characters"},
        "8464": {"comment":"The attributes at DE printed (ROM 3's PRINT_STRING)"},
        "8467": {"comment":"DE = the time"},
        "8471": {"comment":"BC = the date"},
        "8475": {"comment":"Printed (NextZXOS ROM 1's PRINT_DATE_TIME)"},
        "8478": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8483": {"comment":"A = the attributes"},
        "8484": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "8485": {"comment":"Yes: no size"},
        "8487": {"comment":"The size in bytes (ROM 0's PRINT_FILE_SIZE)"},
        "8492": {"comment":"On"},
        "8494": {"synopsis":"Without EXP: \"<DIR>\" for a directory, otherwise its size in K.","comment":"A directory?"},
        "8496": {"comment":"No: its size"},
        "8498": {"comment":"\"<DIR>\""},
        "8504": {"comment":"On"},
        "8506": {"synopsis":"The size in K (NextZXOS ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, spaces before) and \"K\".","comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8509": {"comment":"HL = the size in K"},
        "8513": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8516": {"comment":"Spaces for leading zeros"},
        "8518": {"comment":"Printed (NextZXOS ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5)"},
        "8521": {"comment":"\"K\""},
        "8526": {"synopsis":"ENTER; the next entry.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8531": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8534": {"comment":"HL = the size's address"},
        "8535": {"comment":"+ 2: the next entry"},
        "8537": {"comment":"A = the names left"},
        "8538": {"comment":"One less"},
        "8539": {"comment":"More?"},
        "8542": {"comment":"B = the entries DOS_CATALOG gave"},
        "8543": {"comment":"63: the buffer was full, more may follow"},
        "8546": {"comment":"No: the end"},
        "8548": {"comment":"The last entry (63, at $FA33)"},
        "8551": {"comment":"To entry 0: the next call goes on from it"},
        "8559": {"comment":"HL = $F70B, its size"},
        "8560": {"comment":"$FA there: not 0, more were found"},
        "8561": {"comment":"The next part"},
        "8564": {"synopsis":"ENTER after the last entry.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8567": {"synopsis":"The sort's memory freed ($2653: DOS_CATALOG with B = 2, C = $20, A = 0); the free space on\nthe drive given, or on the default one (DOS_SET_DRIVE), printed with \" free\" ($23C4, $241C).","comment":"The sort's memory freed ($2653)"},
        "8570": {"comment":"A drive letter given?"},
        "8574": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8576": {"comment":"A = $FF: ask"},
        "8578": {"comment":"The default drive (DOS_SET_DRIVE, ROM 2)"},
        "8581": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8584": {"synopsis":"DOS_FREE_SPACE (ROM 2) for drive A.","comment":"The free space on drive A (DOS_FREE_SPACE, ROM 2)"},
        "8587": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8590": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8593": {"comment":"Printed in K, M or G ($23C4)"},
        "8596": {"comment":"\" free\" and ENTER"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"Nothing matched: \"No files found\" ($2422) unless an earlier part of the catalogue was\nprinted (entry 0's size byte, $F70B, not 0); then CAT_FREE.","comment":"Did any part come before (entry 0's size byte not 0)?"},
        "8606": {"comment":"\"No files found\""},
        "8609": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8612": {"comment":"Only when nothing came before"},
        "8615": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8618": {"comment":"The free space"},
        "8620": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A of ROM 3's keyword table (ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN, 0 = RND) with FLAGS bit 0\nset first, so no space goes before it. Called with $25 (LINE), $3F (DATA) and $0A (CODE) by\nTAPE_CAT.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL (what PRINT_TOKEN changes).","comment":"FLAGS bit 0: no space before the keyword"},
        "8624": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN"},
        "8628": {"synopsis":"CAT ASN (CAT followed by the token ASN, from $1FF1): past ASN; checking ends at the\nstatement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each drive letter A-P ROM 2's\nIDE_DOS_MAPPING ($00F7) with L = $80 + the letter (the 256-byte form, BC = $D82B): a mapped\ndrive prints as the letter, \": \" and the description ROM 2 left at $D82B ($FF-ended, ROM 1's\nPRINT_MSG), then ENTER. An error from ROM 2 goes to $209C (CAT_DOS_ERROR). Ends in bank 0.","comment":"Past ASN"},
        "8629": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8635": {"comment":"16 drive letters"},
        "8637": {"comment":"From 'A'"},
        "8639": {"synopsis":"One letter: L = 'A'-'P', B the letters left.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8640": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "8641": {"comment":"BC = the 256-byte buffer for the description"},
        "8644": {"comment":"L = $80 + the letter: the long form"},
        "8646": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAPPING"},
        "8649": {"comment":"An error: $209C"},
        "8652": {"comment":"Not mapped: the next letter"},
        "8654": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "8656": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8660": {"comment":"':'"},
        "8665": {"comment":"' '"},
        "8670": {"comment":"The description, $FF-ended"},
        "8673": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG"},
        "8676": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8679": {"synopsis":"The next letter; after P, bank 0.","comment":"The letter back"},
        "8680": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "8681": {"comment":"The next letter"},
        "8682": {"comment":"For 16 letters"},
        "8684": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8688": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB (CAT followed by the token TAB, from $1FF6): lists the cards' partitions. Past TAB;\nchecking ends at the statement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each of 16 units:\n1. ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY ($01B4, C = the unit): a unit that fails is skipped (CAT_TAB_FREE).\n2. In bank 0: ENTER, \"Unit \", its number, \": \"; 16 bytes copied from IX (left by\n   IDE_CAPACITY) into 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) by ROM 2's $05CC and\n   printed; \", \" and the capacity (PRINT_SECTORS_A, no padding), ENTER.\n3. Every partition entry from 0 (CAT_TAB_ENTRY); unused ones counted; then the count and \"\n   free partition entries\" (CAT_TAB_FREE). Ends in bank 0.","comment":"Past TAB"},
        "8689": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8692": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8695": {"comment":"16 units"},
        "8697": {"synopsis":"One unit: A = 16 - B, the unit number; the free-entry count 0 kept on the stack under it.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8698": {"comment":"A = 16 - B, the unit number"},
        "8701": {"comment":"The free-entry count, 0"},
        "8705": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8706": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "8707": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY: DEHL = its sectors"},
        "8710": {"comment":"No such unit: on to the next"},
        "8713": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8715": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8718": {"comment":"The capacity kept (DEHL)"},
        "8720": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8721": {"comment":"ENTER, \"Unit \""},
        "8727": {"comment":"The unit number"},
        "8728": {"comment":"HL = the unit"},
        "8731": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8733": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "8736": {"comment":"\": \""},
        "8742": {"comment":"17 bytes of workspace"},
        "8745": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8748": {"comment":"HL = IX, as IDE_CAPACITY left it"},
        "8751": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "8752": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "8755": {"comment":"ROM 2's $05CC (the DivMMC memory's copy routine)"},
        "8758": {"comment":"A = $A0 (PRINT_TEXT_DE does not read it)"},
        "8760": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "8761": {"comment":"Its text printed, up to a byte with bit 7 set"},
        "8764": {"comment":"\", \""},
        "8770": {"comment":"DEHL = the capacity again"},
        "8772": {"comment":"No padding"},
        "8774": {"comment":"The capacity, with its unit letter"},
        "8777": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8782": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8785": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "8788": {"synopsis":"Entry BC of the unit's partition table read into $F752 (ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, $00C4, A\n= the unit); an error goes to CAT_TAB_ERROR. Type 0 (the byte at $F762) is counted as free.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "8790": {"comment":"The entry's buffer"},
        "8793": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, entry BC"},
        "8796": {"comment":"An error: CAT_TAB_ERROR"},
        "8799": {"comment":"The entry's type"},
        "8802": {"comment":"0: an unused entry?"},
        "8804": {"comment":"No: a partition"},
        "8806": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8807": {"comment":"The free-entry count"},
        "8808": {"comment":"One more"},
        "8810": {"comment":"The unit kept again"},
        "8811": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "8813": {"synopsis":"A partition: \"u>\" (the unit's number, '>'), its 16-character name from $F752 with $00 shown\nas '~'; a space, its size (the 32-bit word at $F769 + 1, in 512-byte sectors,\nPRINT_SECTORS), a space and its type's name from PART_TYPE_NAMES; ENTER.","comment":"The unit"},
        "8815": {"comment":"The entry number kept"},
        "8816": {"comment":"HL = the unit"},
        "8819": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8821": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8824": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "8827": {"comment":"'>' after the unit"},
        "8832": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8835": {"comment":"The name"},
        "8838": {"comment":"16 characters"},
        "8840": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"One character"},
        "8842": {"comment":"$00?"},
        "8845": {"comment":"Shown as '~'"},
        "8847": {"synopsis":"Printed; E counts the 16.","comment":"Printed in bank 0"},
        "8850": {"comment":"The next of the 16"},
        "8853": {"comment":"The type"},
        "8856": {"comment":"Plus 3: its name's number in the table"},
        "8859": {"comment":"DEHL = the 32-bit word at $F769"},
        "8866": {"comment":"plus 1: the size in sectors"},
        "8872": {"synopsis":"The size and the spaces round it, in bank 0; C = the type + 3, the type name's number in\nPART_TYPE_NAMES.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8875": {"comment":"The name's number kept"},
        "8876": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8881": {"comment":"The size, blanks before it"},
        "8884": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8889": {"comment":"C back"},
        "8890": {"comment":"The table of type names"},
        "8893": {"comment":"20 names at most"},
        "8895": {"synopsis":"Names skipped until C reaches 1 (20 at most).","comment":"Down to this name?"},
        "8898": {"synopsis":"One name's bytes, up to the one with bit 7 set.","comment":"The bytes of a name"},
        "8900": {"comment":"Bit 7 into the carry: the last?"},
        "8903": {"comment":"The next name"},
        "8905": {"synopsis":"The type's name printed (PRINT_TEXT_DE at $013D), ENTER; bank 7 again.","comment":"The type's name printed"},
        "8908": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8913": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8916": {"comment":"The entry number back"},
        "8917": {"synopsis":"The next entry, until BC wraps round to 0.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Until BC wraps round to 0"},
        "8923": {"synopsis":"The end of the unit's table: a free-entry count that is not 0 is printed with \" free\npartition entries\" and two ENTERs (MSG_FREE_ENTRIES).","comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8924": {"comment":"HL = the free-entry count"},
        "8925": {"comment":"None?"},
