        "8937": {"comment":"\" free partition entries\", two ENTERs"},
        "8943": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8946": {"synopsis":"The next unit; after the 16th, bank 0.","comment":"The unit count back"},
        "8947": {"comment":"The next unit"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8955": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ failed: error $38 is the table's end (CAT_TAB_FREE); $16 ends the unit\nwith no count; any other is reported ($209C).","comment":"Error $38: the end of the table"},
        "8957": {"comment":"Then the free-entry count"},
        "8959": {"comment":"Error $16: the unit has no table"},
        "8961": {"comment":"Others are reported"},
        "8964": {"comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8965": {"comment":"Drop the count"},
        "8966": {"comment":"The next unit, with no count"},
        "8968": {"synopsis":"CAT of the tape (from $2050, for a name of two characters starting 'T:'): lists the headers\non the tape until BREAK. 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) hold each header, IX at\nthem. The same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT.","comment":"17 bytes for a header"},
        "8971": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8974": {"comment":"IX = the room"},
        "8977": {"synopsis":"A new line, then the next header (the same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8982": {"synopsis":"BREAK (SPACE, port $7FFE bit 0, and CAPS SHIFT, port $FEFE bit 0, both down) ends the list.","comment":"Port $7FFE: SPACE"},
        "8986": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "8987": {"comment":"SPACE not pressed: go on"},
        "8989": {"comment":"Port $FEFE: CAPS SHIFT"},
        "8993": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "8994": {"comment":"Not pressed: go on"},
        "8996": {"comment":"BREAK: done"},
        "8997": {"synopsis":"A header from the tape: flag 0, 17 bytes, loading (ROM 3's LD_BYTES); a failure tries again.\nThen the name in quotes and a space, and by the type: 0 \"BASIC \" and LINE n when it has a\nstart line; 1 and 2 TAPE_CAT_ARRAY; 3 TAPE_CAT_CODE; higher TAPE_CAT_LAYER.","comment":"The flag byte: a header"},
        "8999": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "9002": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "9003": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9005": {"comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "9008": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9010": {"comment":"Failed: try again"},
        "9012": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9014": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9019": {"comment":"10 characters of name"},
        "9021": {"synopsis":"One character of the name (header bytes 1-10).","comment":"One character"},
        "9027": {"comment":"On to the next"},
        "9029": {"comment":"For 10"},
        "9031": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9033": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9038": {"comment":"A space"},
        "9043": {"comment":"The type, header byte 0"},
        "9046": {"comment":"0, a program?"},
        "9048": {"comment":"No: other types"},
        "9050": {"comment":"\"BASIC \""},
        "9056": {"comment":"Header byte 14 bit 7: no start line?"},
        "9060": {"comment":"None: the next header"},
        "9062": {"comment":"LINE"},
        "9067": {"comment":"HL = the start line, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9073": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9075": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9078": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9080": {"synopsis":"Types 1 and 2, arrays: DATA, the array's letter (header byte 14, bit 7 off and bit 6 on),\nthen \"$() \" for type 2 or \"() \" for type 1 (MSG_ARRAY or one byte on).","comment":"Below 3: an array?"},
        "9082": {"comment":"No: CODE or higher"},
        "9084": {"comment":"The type kept"},
        "9085": {"comment":"DATA"},
        "9090": {"comment":"The array's name, header byte 14"},
        "9093": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "9095": {"comment":"Bit 6 on: a letter"},
        "9097": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9100": {"comment":"\"$() \""},
        "9103": {"comment":"The type back"},
        "9104": {"comment":"2, a string array?"},
        "9106": {"comment":"Yes: \"$() \""},
        "9108": {"comment":"No: \"() \""},
        "9109": {"synopsis":"The suffix printed.","comment":"Printed"},
        "9112": {"synopsis":"The next header (TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"The next header"},
        "9115": {"synopsis":"Type 3: CODE, the start (header bytes 13-14), ',' and the length (bytes 11-12).","comment":"Above 3: TAPE_CAT_LAYER"},
        "9117": {"comment":"CODE"},
        "9122": {"comment":"HL = the start, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9128": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9130": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9133": {"comment":"','"},
        "9138": {"comment":"HL = the length, header bytes 11-12"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9146": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9149": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9151": {"synopsis":"Types 4 and up: SHOW_LAYER_KIND ($3512) with A = the type (\"Layer \" and the character A +\n$2D); then the next header.","comment":"\"Layer \" and the kind"},
        "9154": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9156": {"synopsis":"Prints a count of K: the size from ROM 2 in BCDE (K) doubled into DEHL, 512-byte sectors;\nthen PRINT_SECTORS. Called after DOS_FREE_SPACE (CAT_FREE_DRIVE) and by COPY_DATA with the K\ncopied so far.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = DE, the low word of BCDE"},
        "9157": {"comment":"Doubled: K into 512-byte sectors"},
        "9158": {"comment":"The carry into C and B"},
        "9162": {"comment":"DEHL = the sectors"},
        "9164": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL (in 512-byte sectors) with blanks before it (A = $20), as\nPRINT_SECTORS_A.","comment":"Blanks before the number"},
        "9166": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL, in 512-byte sectors, as a number and a unit letter: DE = 0 gives K\n(DEHL / 2), D = 0 M (DEHL / 2048), otherwise G (DEHL / 2^21), the quotient rounded up when\nbits are lost. The number goes through ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5 with E = A ($20 blanks before it,\n$FF none), the letter through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nEntry: A = the padding character for NUM_OUT_5.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The padding kept"},
        "9167": {"comment":"1 shift, 'K'"},
        "9170": {"comment":"DE = 0?"},
        "9172": {"comment":"Yes: K"},
        "9174": {"comment":"11 shifts, 'M'"},
        "9177": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "9179": {"comment":"Yes: M"},
        "9181": {"comment":"21 shifts, 'G'"},
        "9184": {"synopsis":"B = the shift count, C = the letter: the bits shifted out are ORed into A.","comment":"A collects the bits shifted out"},
        "9185": {"synopsis":"One shift of DEHL to the right.","comment":"DEHL one bit right"},
        "9193": {"comment":"The bit out into A"},
        "9195": {"comment":"B times"},
        "9197": {"comment":"Any bits lost?"},
        "9198": {"comment":"No"},
        "9200": {"comment":"Yes: rounded up"},
        "9201": {"synopsis":"E = the padding; the number printed, then the letter.","comment":"The padding back"},
        "9202": {"comment":"E = the padding for NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9203": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "9204": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9207": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "9208": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9213": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER (PRINT_A_BANK0).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9215": {"synopsis":"Prints A through ROM 3's PRINT_A with RAM bank 0 paged in ($00E8), then bank 7 again\n($00FF).\nChanges: AF (what PRINT_A changes).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9218": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9221": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9225": {"synopsis":"CAT's column move, bit 7 on its last byte: TAB ($17) to column 25 ($19, $00), then a space.\nPrinted by PRINT_TEXT_DE ($013D) from CAT_ENTRY_ATTRS."},
        "9229": {"synopsis":"\"BASIC \", bit 7 on the last byte (TAPE_CAT)."},
        "9235": {"synopsis":"\"$() \", bit 7 on the last byte; TAPE_CAT prints it for a string array and from $2414, \"() \",\nfor a number array."},
        "9239": {"synopsis":"\"<DIR>\", bit 7 on the last byte (CAT_NO_EXP)."},
        "9244": {"synopsis":"\" free\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_FREE_DRIVE)."},
        "9250": {"synopsis":"\"No files found\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_NO_FILES)."},
        "9265": {"synopsis":"ENTER and \"Unit \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9271": {"synopsis":"\": \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9273": {"synopsis":"\", \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9275": {"synopsis":"The partition types' names for CAT_TAB_TYPE, each ended by bit 7, number n for type n - 3:\n\"*BAD*\" ($FE), \"FREE\" ($FF), none (0), \"sys\" (1), \"swap\" (2), \"data\" (3), none (4-15, twelve\n$80s), \"FAT16\" ($10), \"FAT32\" ($11), none ($12)."},
        "9319": {"synopsis":"\" free partition entries\" and two ENTERs, bit 7 on the last (CAT_TAB_FREE)."},
        "9344": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO \"name\" (the syntax table's word at $048E, NextZXOS ROM 1, after classes $0A\nand $0C): ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS (checking ends there); the destination's name (on top of\nthe calculator stack) to $D82B in bank 7, $FF-ended (NAME_TO_HL); A = $10, a file, then\nCOPY_FILES.","comment":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS"},
        "9347": {"comment":"The destination's name goes to $D82B"},
        "9350": {"comment":"From the calculator stack, $FF-ended"},
        "9353": {"comment":"$10: the destination is a file"},
        "9355": {"comment":"Kept for COPY_FILES"},
        "9358": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO SCREEN$ or TO LPRINT (the syntax table's word at $0491): stream 3 when the\nsub-keyword kept at $5B5E is LPRINT ($E0), stream 2 otherwise; then COPY_STRM_SET.","comment":"The sub-keyword taken"},
        "9361": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "9363": {"comment":"Stream 3, the printer"},
        "9365": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9367": {"comment":"No: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "9368": {"synopsis":"A = the stream."},
        "9370": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO #n (the syntax table's word at $0495, after '#' and class 0): A = the stream\n(ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE); 16 or more is error code $0A (report B, ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE"},
        "9373": {"comment":"Stream 0-15?"},
        "9375": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9377": {"comment":"Error code $0A (report B)"},
        "9379": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9382": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS (checking ends there); stream A made current (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).","comment":"The stream kept"},
        "9383": {"comment":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS"},
        "9386": {"comment":"The stream"},
        "9388": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "9391": {"synopsis":"Runs a COPY with the destination chosen (A on the stack: a stream 0-15, or $10 for a file\nnamed at $D82B): the source's name to $E090 in bank 7, $FF-ended (NAME_TO_E090); bank 7;\n$D801 = A. A file is COPY_TO_FILE. A stream lists the file: it is opened as file 0 (ROM 2's\nDOS_OPEN, $0106: B = 0, C = 1 read, D = 0, E = 1) and read a byte at a time (DOS_BYTE_READ,\n$0118); printable bytes and ENTER are printed in bank 0, BREAK tested after each (ROM 1's\nBREAK_STOP); other control codes are skipped, LF prints as ENTER unless it follows one, $1A\nor the file's end (error $19) closes it (DOS_CLOSE, $0109). Other errors go to DOS_FAIL.\nEnds in bank 0.","comment":"The source's name to $E090"},
        "9394": {"comment":"The stream, or $10 for a file"},
        "9395": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9398": {"comment":"Kept at $D801"},
        "9401": {"comment":"$10: a file?"},
        "9403": {"comment":"Yes: COPY_TO_FILE"},
        "9405": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9408": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9411": {"comment":"Open action 1, create action 0: it must exist"},
        "9414": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9417": {"comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9419": {"comment":"No byte before the first"},
        "9421": {"synopsis":"The next byte: D = the last one.","comment":"D = the last byte"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Kept over the call"},
        "9423": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9425": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_BYTE_READ: C = the byte"},
        "9428": {"comment":"D back"},
        "9429": {"comment":"A byte read?"},
        "9431": {"comment":"No: $19, the file's end?"},
        "9433": {"comment":"Another error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9436": {"comment":"The end: close it"},
        "9438": {"synopsis":"A byte read (C): $1A ends the file; ENTER is printed; LF goes to COPY_TYPE_LF; other codes\nbelow $20 are skipped.","comment":"The byte: $1A (soft EOF) also ends the file"},
        "9443": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "9445": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9447": {"comment":"LF?"},
        "9451": {"comment":"Another control code?"},
        "9453": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "9455": {"synopsis":"Printed in bank 0; BREAK tested (ROM 1's BREAK_STOP); bank 7.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9458": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9461": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP"},
        "9464": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9467": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "9469": {"synopsis":"The end: file 0 closed; bank 0.","comment":"File 0"},
        "9471": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9474": {"synopsis":"A failed open or close goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9476": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9480": {"synopsis":"LF: skipped after an ENTER, printed as ENTER otherwise.","comment":"ENTER: the byte before an ENTER?"},
        "9482": {"comment":"Then the LF is skipped"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Otherwise printed as ENTER"},
        "9487": {"synopsis":"COPY to a file: ENTER printed first. Also entered at COPY_TO_FILE_GO.","comment":"ENTER first"},
        "9492": {"synopsis":"COPY to a file, with the source's name at $E090 and the destination's at $D82B (bank 7,\n$FF-ended) and $D801 set (bit 7: no messages, BREAK not tested). Also reached from NextZXOS\nROM 1's CALL_ALT_2514 (the browser's copy, $D801 = $80).\n1. $D5D6 = SP (DOS_FAIL comes back to it); $D802, the count of files copied, = 0.\n2. Both names parsed (PARSE_FILESPEC): the destination's results at $D826 (flags),\n   $D827-$D828 (user, drive) and $D829 (where its file name starts); the source's at $D821,\n   $D822-$D823 and $D824. A wildcard in the destination is error code $49.\n3. A wildcard in the source is COPY_WILD; a source with no file name is error code $2C.\n4. A destination with no file name is COPY_WILD too; otherwise COPY_ONE copies the file and\n   COPY_FILES_DONE reports.","comment":"SP kept for DOS_FAIL"},
        "9496": {"comment":"No files copied yet"},
        "9500": {"comment":"The destination's name"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "9506": {"comment":"Where its file name starts"},
        "9509": {"comment":"Its user area and drive"},
        "9513": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "9516": {"comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "9518": {"comment":"No"},
        "9520": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9523": {"comment":"Error code $49"},
        "9525": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9528": {"synopsis":"The source's name parsed.","comment":"The source's name"},
        "9531": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "9534": {"comment":"Where its file name starts"},
        "9537": {"comment":"Its user area and drive"},
        "9541": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "9546": {"comment":"Yes: COPY_WILD"},
        "9548": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name?"},
        "9550": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9552": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9555": {"comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "9557": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9560": {"synopsis":"Neither has a wildcard and the source has a name: a destination with a name is one file\n(COPY_ONE, COPY_FILES_DONE).","comment":"The destination's flags"},
        "9563": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name?"},
        "9565": {"comment":"No: COPY_WILD copies into the place"},
        "9567": {"comment":"One file copied"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Then the count"},
        "9573": {"synopsis":"A ROM 2 call failed, or COPY found an error, error code in A: files 2, 1 and 0 closed (ROM\n2's DOS_CLOSE, $0109), each one that will not close abandoned (DOS_ABANDON, $010C); ENTER.\nWith $D801 bit 7 set (DOS_FAIL_QUIET) SP goes back to $D5D6's value and NC returns the error\nto COPY_TO_FILE_GO's caller; otherwise ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0 reports it. The same job as\nthe +3E's DOS_FAIL.","comment":"The error kept"},
        "9574": {"comment":"Files 2, 1 and 0"},
        "9576": {"synopsis":"One file: B = 2, 1, 0.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9577": {"comment":"B = the file"},
        "9579": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9582": {"comment":"B back"},
        "9583": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "9585": {"comment":"No: ROM 2's DOS_ABANDON"},
        "9588": {"synopsis":"The next file.","comment":"The count back"},
        "9589": {"comment":"The next file"},
        "9591": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "9596": {"comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9600": {"comment":"Yes: back to the caller"},
        "9602": {"comment":"The error"},
        "9603": {"comment":"ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0, which reports it"},
        "9606": {"synopsis":"Quiet: the error code back in A, the stack as COPY_TO_FILE_GO found it, NC.","comment":"The error back"},
        "9607": {"comment":"The stack as COPY_TO_FILE_GO found it"},
        "9611": {"comment":"NC: failed"},
        "9613": {"synopsis":"A wildcard in the source, or a destination with no file name: the destination must be a\ndrive, user area or path alone (error code $4A otherwise). Then each file that matches is\ncopied:\n1. The source's name copied to $DA35; the catalogue slot at $D814 cleared.\n2. COPY_CAT_NEXT: the last name found ($D814) preloaded at $D807 and the next matching file\n   asked for (ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG, $011E: B = 2, C = 2, LFN flags).\n3. Its long name (IDE_GET_LFN, $01B7, IX = the directory handle) written over the source's\n   file name ($D824 points into $E090).\n4. The destination's file name ($D829 on) made from it: the long name as it is when the\n   destination's drive has no XDPB (ROM 2's DOS_REF_XDPB, $0151, fails), otherwise the 8.3\n   name from the catalogue entry.\n5. BREAK tested unless $D801 bit 7 is set; COPY_ONE; again. No more matches: none copied is\n   error $17; otherwise COPY_FILES_DONE.","comment":"The destination's flags"},
        "9616": {"comment":"A file name in the destination?"},
        "9618": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "9620": {"comment":"A drive, user area or path?"},
        "9622": {"comment":"Yes: go on"},
        "9624": {"synopsis":"Error code $4A (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9627": {"comment":"Error code $4A"},
        "9629": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9632": {"synopsis":"The source's name to $DA35, up to and including its $FF.","comment":"The source's name"},
        "9635": {"comment":"copied to $DA35"},
        "9638": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "9639": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9642": {"comment":"Up to its $FF"},
        "9645": {"comment":"The catalogue slot"},
        "9648": {"comment":"cleared"},
        "9649": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "9651": {"synopsis":"One byte of the 13 cleared.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9655": {"synopsis":"The next matching file (see COPY_WILD).","comment":"The last name found"},
        "9658": {"comment":"is the next search's start"},
        "9661": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "9666": {"comment":"The source's name, wildcards and all"},
        "9669": {"comment":"B = 2 slots, C = 2 (LFN flags)"},
        "9672": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "9675": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG"},
        "9678": {"comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9680": {"comment":"B = the names found: none?"},
        "9681": {"comment":"IX = the directory handle"},
        "9684": {"comment":"None: COPY_WILD_END"},
        "9686": {"comment":"The name to look up"},
        "9689": {"comment":"The entry found"},
        "9692": {"comment":"BC = the source's file name: the long one goes there"},
        "9696": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_GET_LFN"},
        "9699": {"synopsis":"IDE_GET_LFN's result: a failure (or error $17 from COPY_WILD_END) goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9701": {"comment":"The destination's drive"},
        "9704": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_REF_XDPB: does it have one?"},
        "9707": {"comment":"DE = the destination's file name"},
        "9711": {"comment":"Yes: an 8.3 name"},
        "9713": {"comment":"No: the long name"},
        "9716": {"synopsis":"One byte of the long name, up to and including its $FF.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9717": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "9719": {"comment":"Up to its $FF"},
        "9722": {"comment":"On"},
        "9724": {"synopsis":"An XDPB drive: the 8 name characters up to a space, '.', the 3 type characters up to a space\n(COPY_TO_SPACE, bit 7 off); a '.' with nothing after it removed.","comment":"The name's 8 characters"},
        "9727": {"comment":"up to a space"},
        "9732": {"comment":"Then '.'"},
        "9739": {"comment":"and the type's 3 characters"},
        "9744": {"comment":"The last character"},
        "9745": {"comment":"A '.' (no type)?"},
        "9748": {"comment":"Yes: overwritten"},
        "9750": {"comment":"No: kept"},
        "9751": {"synopsis":"The $FF after the name.","comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "9754": {"synopsis":"The names ready: BREAK tested in bank 0 (ROM 1's BREAK_STOP) unless $D801 bit 7 is set.","comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9758": {"comment":"Yes: no BREAK test"},
        "9760": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9763": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP"},
        "9766": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9769": {"synopsis":"The file copied (COPY_ONE); the next match.","comment":"The file copied"},
        "9772": {"comment":"The next match"},
        "9774": {"synopsis":"No more matches: none copied is error $17 (through COPY_GOT_LFN's JR NC).","comment":"Files copied"},
        "9777": {"comment":"None?"},
        "9778": {"comment":"Error $17"},
        "9780": {"comment":"Through COPY_GOT_LFN's JP NC"},
        "9782": {"synopsis":"Every file copied: unless $D801 bit 7 is set, the count from $D802 (NUM_OUT_5, blanks before\nit) and \" files copied\" with ENTER (MSG_N_COPIED); SCR_CT = $17; then CAT_SORT_FREE.","comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9786": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "9787": {"comment":"HL = the count of files"},
        "9792": {"comment":"Blanks before it"},
        "9794": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9797": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9800": {"comment":"\" files copied\", two ENTERs"},
        "9806": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $17"},
        "9811": {"synopsis":"Releases the memory a sorted DOS_CATALOG took: ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG ($011E) with B = 2, C =\n$20 and A = 0 (an unsorted call, as the API document advises), DE = $F700, HL = $E090.\nExit: what DOS_CATALOG returns.","comment":"B = 2 slots, C = $20 (A's filter)"},
        "9814": {"comment":"A = 0: no sorting"},
        "9815": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "9818": {"comment":"The name"},
        "9821": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG"},
        "9825": {"synopsis":"Copies one file, the source named at $E090 and the destination at $D82B (bank 7, $FF-ended):\nSCR_CT = $FF. Unless $D801 bit 7 is set the source's name and \" --> \" are printed, and the\ndestination's name and ENTER after it.\n1. The source opened as file 0 for reading (ROM 2's DOS_OPEN: BC = $0001, DE = $0002), the\n   destination as file 1 for writing (BC = $0102, DE = $0204); COPY_DATA copies the bytes;\n   file 1 closed; $D802 + 1.\n2. Unless ROM 2's $292E gives NZ, when the source has a metadata file (ROM 2's META_NAME\n   builds its name at $F700), it is copied too: opened as file 0, the destination's metadata\n   name built, its directories made (ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS), opened as file 1, COPY_DATA,\n   file 1 closed. A failure goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"$FF"},
        "9827": {"comment":"SCR_CT: no 'scroll?'"},
        "9830": {"comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9834": {"comment":"Yes: no names shown"},
        "9836": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9839": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG"},
        "9842": {"comment":"\" --> \""},
        "9848": {"synopsis":"The source opened as file 0.","comment":"The source"},
        "9851": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9854": {"comment":"Open action 2 (no header), create action 0"},
        "9857": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9860": {"synopsis":"A failed open or close goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9863": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "9866": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9867": {"comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9871": {"comment":"Yes: not shown"},
        "9873": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG"},
        "9876": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "9879": {"synopsis":"The destination opened as file 1, then the copy.","comment":"The destination"},
        "9880": {"comment":"File 1, exclusive-write"},
        "9883": {"comment":"Open action 4 (erase it), create action 2"},
        "9886": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9889": {"comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9891": {"comment":"The bytes copied"},
        "9894": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "9896": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9899": {"synopsis":"File 1 closed? Then the metadata file.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9901": {"comment":"One more file copied"},
        "9905": {"comment":"ROM 2's $292E: metadata files off (NZ)?"},
        "9908": {"comment":"Yes: none copied"},
        "9910": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9913": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME: its metadata file's name"},
        "9916": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "9918": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Open action 2, create action 0"},
        "9924": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9927": {"comment":"Not there: done"},
        "9929": {"comment":"The destination's name"},
        "9932": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME"},
        "9935": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9937": {"comment":"None: file 0 closed"},
        "9939": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS: its directories"},
        "9942": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9944": {"comment":"Failed: file 0 closed"},
        "9946": {"comment":"File 1, exclusive-write"},
        "9949": {"comment":"Open action 4, create action 2"},
        "9952": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9955": {"comment":"Opened: the bytes copied"},
        "9958": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "9960": {"synopsis":"File B closed.","comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9963": {"synopsis":"ENTER unless $D801 bit 7 is set.","comment":"$D801 bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Yes: no ENTER"},
        "9968": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER through ROM 3's PRINT_A in bank 0, then pages bank 7 back in.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9973": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9976": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"Copies file 0 into file 1 in 2K pieces through $F700 (bank 7), showing the K copied so far:\na space, then for each piece the count (PRINT_K_SIZE, six characters), read by ROM 2's\nDOS_READ ($0112: B = 0, C = 7, DE = $0800) and written by DOS_WRITE ($0115: B = 1, C = 7);\nthe count is backspaced over before the next. The file's end (error $19) closes file 0 and\nwrites what was read; a piece shorter than 2K ends the copy.\nExit: carry when done; NC with A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A space before the count"},
        "9982": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9985": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9991": {"comment":"The count of K, 0"},
        "9996": {"synopsis":"One piece: the count (HL high word, DE low word, in K) printed.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9998": {"comment":"BCDE = the count"},
        "10000": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10003": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10006": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10009": {"comment":"File 0, into bank 7"},
        "10012": {"comment":"2K"},
        "10015": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10016": {"comment":"At $F700"},
        "10019": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_READ"},
        "10022": {"comment":"All read"},
        "10024": {"comment":"Error $19, the file's end?"},
        "10026": {"comment":"No: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10029": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "10030": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "10032": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "10035": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "10036": {"comment":"HL = 2K"},
        "10037": {"synopsis":"An error leaves through COPY_CLOSE_TEST (DOS_FAIL); otherwise DE = the bytes read.","comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10040": {"comment":"HL = the bytes read"},
        "10043": {"comment":"into DE"},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"All 2K read.","comment":"DE = 2K"},
        "10047": {"synopsis":"DE bytes written (none when DE is 0).","comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "10051": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "10052": {"comment":"From $F700"},
        "10055": {"comment":"File 1, from bank 7"},
        "10058": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_WRITE"},
        "10061": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "10062": {"comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10064": {"comment":"Exactly 2K?"},
        "10068": {"comment":"(the high byte 8)"},
        "10071": {"comment":"No: the last piece"},
        "10073": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "10075": {"comment":"Backspaced over"},
        "10078": {"comment":"2K more"},
        "10083": {"comment":"HL = HL x 2 + the carry, the high word"},
        "10087": {"comment":"The next piece"},
        "10089": {"synopsis":"The last piece: the count backspaced over, the result kept in AF.","comment":"The count"},
        "10091": {"comment":"The result kept"},
        "10092": {"comment":"Backspaced over"},
        "10095": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10097": {"synopsis":"Prints six backspaces (code 8) through ROM 3's PRINT_A in bank 0, back to bank 7 after each.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"Six backspaces"},
        "10099": {"synopsis":"One backspace.","comment":"Code 8"},
        "10101": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10104": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "10107": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10110": {"comment":"The next"},
        "10113": {"synopsis":"\" files copied\" and two ENTERs, bit 7 on the last (COPY_FILES_DONE)."},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"\" --> \", bit 7 on the last space (COPY_ONE, between the names)."},
        "10598": {"synopsis":"LOOK_VARS's search of a DEF FN's parameters: ROM 3's LV_RUN_TEST, running with the high byte\nof DEFADD ($5C0C) not 0, goes on here through its NEXTREG $8C,$80 at $2962. The list at\nDEFADD is scanned: each parameter a letter, a '$' for a string, then $0E and 5 bytes; ','\nbetween them and ')' at the end. A parameter whose form (B: $60 + the letter for a number,\n$40 + the letter for a string) is C, the form LOOK_VARS made, is found:\n1. A number: HL is left at its $0E.\n2. A string: its 5 bytes are copied onto the calculator stack (ROM 3's MOVE_FP, STKEND past\n   them) and ROM 3 is selected again ($5B48).\nFound, A = 1 and NZ, out through ALT_ROM_OFF: the RET returns from LOOK_VARS. Not found, A =\n0 and Z, on at ROM 3's $28F8 (the rest of LV_RUN_TEST).\nEntry: C = the name's form.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = DEFADD, the parameter list"},
        "10601": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "10602": {"comment":"')': no parameters?"},
        "10604": {"comment":"Then not found"},
        "10606": {"synopsis":"One parameter: B = its form.","comment":"A parameter's letter"},
        "10607": {"comment":"$60 + the letter: a number's form"},
        "10609": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "10610": {"comment":"The character after the letter"},
        "10612": {"comment":"$0E, a number's mark?"},
        "10614": {"comment":"Yes: a number"},
        "10616": {"comment":"Back to the letter"},
        "10617": {"comment":"On to the '$'"},
        "10620": {"comment":"Past it, to the $0E"},
        "10621": {"comment":"$40 + the letter: a string's form"},
        "10623": {"synopsis":"The parameter's form (B) compared with C; not the one: past its 5 bytes and the ',' to the\nnext, or not found at ')'.","comment":"The parameter's form"},
        "10624": {"comment":"The one looked for?"},
        "10625": {"comment":"Yes: found"},
        "10627": {"comment":"HL on to the value's last byte"},
        "10632": {"comment":"On to the ',' or ')'"},
        "10635": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "10637": {"comment":"The end: not found"},
        "10639": {"comment":"Past the ',' to the next letter"},
        "10642": {"comment":"The next parameter"},
        "10644": {"synopsis":"Found: a number (C bit 5) leaves HL at its $0E; a string's 5 bytes are stacked.","comment":"A number?"},
        "10646": {"comment":"Yes: HL at its $0E"},
        "10648": {"comment":"Past the $0E: the string's 5 bytes"},
        "10649": {"comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "10653": {"comment":"Copied to the calculator stack (ROM 3's MOVE_FP)"},
        "10656": {"comment":"ROM 3 selected again"},
        "10659": {"comment":"HL = past the copy"},
        "10660": {"comment":"STKEND = it"},
        "10663": {"synopsis":"A = 1 and NZ: found.","comment":"A = 1"},
        "10664": {"comment":"NZ: found"},
        "10665": {"comment":"Out"},
        "10667": {"synopsis":"Not found: A = 0 and Z; ROM 3's LV_RUN_TEST goes on at $28F8.","comment":"A = 0, Z: not found"},
        "10668": {"comment":"Then ROM 3's $28F8"},
        "10672": {"synopsis":"Out through ALT_ROM_OFF, into ROM 3.","comment":"This ROM off; RET into ROM 3"},
        "10675": {"synopsis":"Moves HL on to the next character that is $21 or more (past spaces and control codes).\nExit: A = that character.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The next character"},
        "10677": {"comment":"Below $21?"},
        "10679": {"comment":"Then on"},
        "10681": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "10682": {"synopsis":"An $FF put at DE (after a name copied to $F700), then ROM 2's IDE_PATH ($01B1) with A = the\nreason code and HL = $F700.\nExit: HL = $F700; carry when done, NC with A = the error.","comment":"HL = the end of the name"},
        "10683": {"comment":"$FF there"},
        "10685": {"comment":"The name"},
        "10688": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10689": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH, reason A"},
        "10692": {"comment":"HL = $F700"},
        "10694": {"synopsis":"CD \"path\" (token $A0; the syntax table's word at $03B0, after classes $0A and $0C): the path\n(NAME_TO_F700) $FF-ended in bank 7, then ROM 2's CD_NAME ($0506), which changes the drive\nand directory; done, ROM 2's $1BF9 with A = $FF makes the default drive the LOAD and SAVE\ndrive ($5B79, $5B7A). Then PATH_RESULT.","comment":"The path to $F700"},
        "10697": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10700": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "10703": {"comment":"ROM 2's CD_NAME"},
        "10706": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10708": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "10710": {"comment":"ROM 2's $1BF9: LOAD and SAVE drives = the default"},
        "10713": {"synopsis":"DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The result"},
        "10716": {"synopsis":"MKDIR \"path\" (token $A1; the syntax table's word at $03B4): IDE_PATH with A = 2\n(rc_path_make) on the name; then PATH_RESULT.","comment":"The name to $F700"},
        "10719": {"comment":"2: rc_path_make"},
        "10721": {"synopsis":"IDE_PATH (PATH_CALL) with reason A, in bank 7.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10724": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH"},
        "10727": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10729": {"synopsis":"RMDIR \"path\" (token $A2; the syntax table's word at $03B8): IDE_PATH with A = 3\n(rc_path_delete).","comment":"The name to $F700"},
        "10732": {"comment":"3: rc_path_delete"},
        "10736": {"synopsis":"PWD (token $9F; the syntax table's word at $038F, class $0E): ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2 (stream\n2, an optional #n); checking ends at the statement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7:\nIDE_PATH with A = 1 (rc_path_get) and an empty location ($FF at $F700), so the current path\nis written at $F700; it is printed (ROM 1's PRINT_MSG) with ENTER after it (PRINT_ENTER_B7);\nthen PATH_RESULT with carry.","comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2"},
        "10739": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "10740": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "10743": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10746": {"comment":"1: rc_path_get"},
        "10748": {"comment":"An empty location: the default drive"},
        "10751": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH"},
        "10754": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10756": {"comment":"The path, $FF-ended: ROM 1's PRINT_MSG"},
        "10759": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "10762": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "10763": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10765": {"synopsis":"PLOT in screen modes 1-15: ROM 3's PLOT_CMD calls its $1FB6, which comes here through this\npage's $1FC2 when $5C7F's low four bits are not 0 ($1FC2 drops that call's return). y and x\ncome off the calculator stack as signed numbers (FP_TO_SIGNED_BC) and the pixel is plotted\non the other stack (SWAP_SP, PLOT_XY); then GFX_EXIT. A point off the screen is not plotted\nand is no error.","comment":"BC = y"},
        "10768": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10769": {"comment":"BC = x"},
        "10772": {"comment":"HL = y"},
        "10773": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "10776": {"comment":"The pixel plotted"},
        "10779": {"synopsis":"Back to the first stack (SWAP_SP), then GFX_EXIT. The end of DRAW_MODE_1_15 and\nCIRCLE_MODE_1_15 too.","comment":"The first stack again"},
        "10782": {"synopsis":"ROM 3 selected again (NextReg $8E = $03), carry cleared, and out through ALT_ROM_OFF: the\nRET returns to the caller of the ROM 3 routine that came here.","comment":"ROM 3 selected again"},
        "10786": {"comment":"NC"},
        "10787": {"comment":"Out: RET into ROM 3"},
        "10790": {"synopsis":"POINT in screen modes 1-15 (from ROM 3's POINT_SUB, through $1FC2 as PLOT_MODE_1_15): y and\nx (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD, 0-65535 or report B), the pixel tested on the other stack\n(POINT_TEST_XY). On the screen its value (E: 0 or 1, or the pixel's byte in modes 1 and 2)\nis stacked (ROM 1's STACK_A), then GFX_EXIT; off the screen, POINT_OFF_SCREEN.","comment":"BC = y (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "10793": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10794": {"comment":"BC = x"},
        "10797": {"comment":"HL = y"},
        "10798": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "10801": {"comment":"The pixel tested: E"},
        "10804": {"comment":"The first stack again"},
        "10807": {"comment":"Off the screen: an error"},
        "10809": {"comment":"A = the pixel's value"},
        "10810": {"comment":"Stacked (ROM 1's STACK_A)"},
        "10813": {"comment":"Out"},
        "10815": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C), through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.","comment":"Error code $0B"},
        "10817": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "10820": {"synopsis":"Takes a number off the calculator stack (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC) as a signed 16-bit value: BC =\n|n|, made 0 - |n| when n is negative.\nExit: BC = the number.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"BC = |n| (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC); Z when positive"},
        "10823": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "10824": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "10827": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "10828": {"comment":"HL = -|n|"},
        "10830": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "10833": {"synopsis":"Tests the pixel at x = BC, y = HL (PIXEL_OP with carry); $5B84 and $5B86 are left alone.\nExit: carry when it is on the screen, with E = the pixel (0 or 1; in modes 1 and 2 its\nbyte); NC when off.","comment":"Carry: a test"},
        "10836": {"synopsis":"Plots the pixel at x = BC, y = HL in the current screen mode (PIXEL_OP), first keeping x at\n$5B84 and y at $5B86: the last point, from which DRAW_MODE_1_15 draws.\nExit: carry when plotted, NC when off the screen.","comment":"x kept at $5B84"},
        "10840": {"comment":"y at $5B86"},
        "10843": {"synopsis":"PLOT_XY without keeping the point (from CIRCLE_PLOT_SWAP).","comment":"NC: a plot"},
        "10844": {"synopsis":"Plots (carry clear) or tests (carry set) the pixel at x = BC, y = HL in the screen mode held\nin $5C7F's low four bits; the carry is kept in F'. Off the screen (y 192 or more, x 256 or\nmore, or 512 or more in mode 9) it returns NC and does nothing.\n1. Modes 1 and 2, one byte a pixel: PXO_ONE_BYTE.\n2. Mode 9, 512 x 192: PXO_HIRES.\n3. The others (mode $0D with page $0B in MMU slot 3 first): PXO_ULA, the ULA screen's bit.\nExit: carry when done; NC off the screen; for a test E as POINT_TEST_XY says.\nChanges: AF, AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"F' = the carry: test or plot"},
        "10845": {"comment":"x 512 or more, or y 256 or more?"},
        "10849": {"comment":"Then off the screen (NC)"},
        "10850": {"comment":"y"},
        "10851": {"comment":"192 or more?"},
        "10853": {"comment":"Off the screen"},
        "10854": {"comment":"The screen mode"},
        "10859": {"comment":"Mode 9: 512 wide?"},
        "10861": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10863": {"comment":"NC"},
        "10864": {"comment":"x 256 or more?"},
        "10866": {"comment":"Then off the screen"},
        "10867": {"comment":"Modes 1 and 2?"},
        "10869": {"comment":"One byte a pixel"},
        "10871": {"comment":"Mode $0D?"},
        "10873": {"comment":"No"},
        "10875": {"comment":"MMU slot 3 = page $0B"},
        "10879": {"synopsis":"The ULA screen's pixel: HL = its byte (PIXELAD, D = y, E = x), A = its bit (SETAE).","comment":"D = y"},
        "10880": {"comment":"E = x"},
        "10881": {"comment":"HL = the pixel's byte"},
        "10883": {"synopsis":"B = the bit inverted; a test is PXO_ULA_TEST. A plot sets the bit; OVER (P_FLAG bit 0) flips\nit instead (the bit kept here, PXO_INV_TEST flips it).","comment":"A = the pixel's bit"},
        "10885": {"comment":"B = all but that bit"},
        "10887": {"comment":"The carry back: a test?"},
        "10888": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10890": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "10891": {"comment":"OVER (P_FLAG bit 0)?"},
        "10895": {"comment":"Yes: the bit kept"},
        "10897": {"comment":"No: the bit cleared"},
        "10898": {"synopsis":"INVERSE (P_FLAG bit 2) set: the byte stays as it is now (the bit cleared, or with OVER\nunchanged). Clear: the bit flipped (XOR B, CPL), which sets a cleared one.","comment":"INVERSE (P_FLAG bit 2)?"},
        "10902": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "10904": {"comment":"No: the bit flipped"},
        "10906": {"synopsis":"The byte written; then the colour byte at $5C6C: $5C7F bit 3 clear, into the cell's\nattribute (PXO_ULA_ATTR); bits 3 and 2 set, into the byte $2000 above the pixel's; bit 3\nalone, nowhere.","comment":"The byte back"},
        "10907": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 3?"},
        "10911": {"comment":"Clear: the cell's attribute"},
        "10913": {"comment":"Bit 2?"},
        "10917": {"comment":"Clear: no attribute"},
        "10919": {"comment":"The byte $2000 above"},
        "10921": {"comment":"The colour byte"},
        "10924": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10925": {"synopsis":"Done: carry; MMU slot 3 = page $11 again.","comment":"Carry: done"},
        "10926": {"comment":"MMU slot 3 = page $11"},
        "10931": {"synopsis":"A test: E = 1 when the pixel's bit is set, 0 when not.","comment":"The bit"},
        "10933": {"comment":"Set in the byte?"},
        "10934": {"comment":"E = 0 when not"},
        "10935": {"comment":"Not set: done"},
        "10937": {"comment":"E = 1"},
        "10941": {"synopsis":"The attribute of the pixel's cell ($58 + the third as the high byte) takes the colour byte\nat $5C6C; carry.","comment":"The pixel's high byte"},
        "10942": {"comment":"Its third (bits 3-4) down to bits 0-1"},
        "10945": {"comment":"Only those"},
        "10947": {"comment":"$58 + the third"},
        "10949": {"comment":"HL = the attribute"},
        "10950": {"comment":"The colour byte"},
        "10953": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10954": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "10956": {"synopsis":"Mode 9, 512 x 192: MMU slot 3 = page $0B; x bits 0-2 pick the bit and bits 4-8 the column (E\nfor PIXELAD = (x / 2 AND $F8) + (x AND 7)); x bit 3 set moves the byte to the $6000 half.\nThen PXO_ULA_MASK.","comment":"MMU slot 3 = page $0B"},
        "10960": {"comment":"x's low three bits"},
        "10963": {"comment":"BC = x / 2"},
        "10967": {"comment":"B = x's low bits"},
        "10968": {"comment":"x / 2's bits 3-7"},
        "10971": {"comment":"with x's low bits"},
        "10972": {"comment":"D = y"},
        "10973": {"comment":"E = the column and the bit"},
        "10974": {"comment":"HL = the byte"},
        "10976": {"comment":"x bit 3?"},
        "10978": {"comment":"Clear: the $4000 half"},
        "10980": {"comment":"Set: the $6000 half"},
        "10984": {"synopsis":"Modes 1 and 2, one byte a pixel: H = y, L = x; mode 2 is PXO_LAYER2. Mode 1 (LoRes, 128 x\n96; more is off the screen): HL = $4000 + y x 128 + x.","comment":"H = y"},
        "10985": {"comment":"L = x"},
        "10986": {"comment":"Mode 2?"},
        "10987": {"comment":"Yes: Layer 2"},
        "10989": {"comment":"LoRes: y 96 or more?"},
        "10992": {"comment":"Off the screen"},
        "10993": {"comment":"x 128 or more?"},
        "10996": {"comment":"Off the screen"},
        "10997": {"comment":"y / 2"},
        "10999": {"comment":"Even y?"},
        "11001": {"comment":"Odd: L + 128"},
        "11003": {"synopsis":"H = $40 + y / 2; from $58 up it moves on by 8, to $6000 on, with page $0B in MMU slot 3.","comment":"$4000 on"},
        "11006": {"comment":"Below $58?"},
        "11008": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11010": {"comment":"$6000 on"},
        "11013": {"comment":"MMU slot 3 = page $0B"},
        "11017": {"synopsis":"The byte at HL: a test is PXO_LORES_TEST; a plot writes (the byte AND $5C6C) XOR $5C6D, the\ncolour word ROM 1's CLASS_9 left there; then PXO_DONE.","comment":"The carry back: a test?"},
        "11018": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11020": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "11021": {"comment":"E, D = the colour word at $5C6C"},
        "11025": {"comment":"AND E"},
        "11026": {"comment":"XOR D"},
        "11027": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11028": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11030": {"synopsis":"A test: E = the pixel's byte.","comment":"E = the byte"},
        "11031": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11033": {"synopsis":"Mode 2, Layer 2 (256 x 192): the 8K page holding row y of the Layer 2 shadow bank (NextReg\n$13, read through ports $243B and $253B: 2 x the bank + y / 32) goes into MMU slot 7, so HL\n= $E000 + (y AND 31) x 256 + x. A plot writes (the byte AND $5C6C) XOR $5C6D; a test gives E\n= the byte (PXO_L2_TEST). Then PXO_L2_DONE.","comment":"y"},
        "11034": {"comment":"y / 32: the 8K page within the bank"},
        "11037": {"comment":"Bits 0-2"},
        "11039": {"comment":"Port $243B: the NextReg number"},
        "11042": {"comment":"NextReg $13: the Layer 2 shadow bank"},
        "11044": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "11046": {"comment":"Port $253B"},
        "11047": {"comment":"D = the bank (16K)"},
        "11049": {"comment":"Plus 2 x the bank: the 8K page"},
        "11051": {"comment":"MMU slot 7 = it"},
        "11054": {"comment":"H = $E0 + (y AND 31)"},
        "11058": {"comment":"The carry back: a test?"},
        "11059": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11061": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "11062": {"comment":"E, D = the colour word at $5C6C"},
        "11066": {"comment":"AND E"},
        "11067": {"comment":"XOR D"},
        "11068": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11069": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 7 = page 1 again; carry.","comment":"MMU slot 7 = page 1"},
        "11073": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "11075": {"synopsis":"A test: E = the pixel's byte.","comment":"E = the byte"},
        "11076": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11078": {"synopsis":"DRAW's straight line in screen modes 1-15 (from ROM 3's DRAW_LINE, through $1FC2 as\nPLOT_MODE_1_15):\n1. y and x (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC) each give a length and a step of -1, 0 or 1 (B for y, C for\n   x). Both 0: RET Z at once.\n2. On the other stack (SWAP_SP): from the last point ($5B84, $5B86) the line runs along the\n   longer of the two a pixel at a time, with a step along the shorter one each time the\n   running sum (half the longer at the start, plus the shorter each pixel) reaches the\n   longer; each pixel by PLOT_XY, the longer length giving the count.\n3. Each time the count's low byte runs out, BREAK (CAPS SHIFT and SPACE, and ROM 1's\n   TAPE_BREAK_TEST giving Z) stops with error code $14 (report L).\nThen GFX_SWAP_EXIT.","comment":"BC = |y|; NZ when negative"},
        "11081": {"comment":"D = -1 for a negative y"},
        "11084": {"comment":"Negative"},
        "11086": {"comment":"y = 0?"},
        "11088": {"comment":"D = 0 then"},
        "11089": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11091": {"comment":"Otherwise D = 1"},
        "11093": {"synopsis":"D = y's step kept with |y|; then x's.","comment":"|y| kept"},
        "11094": {"comment":"Its step kept"},
        "11095": {"comment":"BC = |x|; NZ when negative"},
        "11098": {"comment":"DE = |x|"},
        "11100": {"comment":"B = y's step, C = $FF"},
        "11101": {"comment":"Negative: C = -1"},
        "11103": {"comment":"x = 0?"},
        "11105": {"comment":"C = 0 then"},
        "11106": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11108": {"comment":"Otherwise C = 1"},
        "11110": {"synopsis":"B = y's step, C = x's; HL = |y|, DE = |x|. Both steps 0: nothing drawn.","comment":"HL = |y|"},
        "11111": {"comment":"No step at all?"},
        "11113": {"comment":"Then nothing drawn"},
        "11114": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "11117": {"comment":"|y| kept"},
        "11118": {"comment":"|y| - |x|"},
        "11121": {"comment":"HL = |y|"},
        "11122": {"comment":"Both steps kept: the diagonal step"},
        "11123": {"comment":"|y| the longer?"},
        "11125": {"comment":"No: y's step 0 in the straight step"},
        "11127": {"comment":"HL = |x|, the longer; DE = |y|"},
        "11130": {"synopsis":"|y| the longer: x's step 0 in the straight step.","comment":"x's step 0"},
        "11132": {"synopsis":"The straight step kept; BC = IX = the longer length (the count), HL = half of it (the\nrunning sum).","comment":"The straight step kept"},
        "11133": {"comment":"BC = the longer"},
        "11135": {"comment":"HL = half of it"},
        "11139": {"comment":"IX = the count"},
        "11142": {"synopsis":"One pixel: the shorter added to the sum; reaching the longer (or a carry) is a diagonal\nstep, otherwise a straight one.","comment":"Sum + the shorter"},
        "11143": {"comment":"Past 65535: diagonal"},
        "11145": {"comment":"Below the longer?"},
        "11147": {"comment":"Yes: straight"},
        "11149": {"comment":"Sum back"},
        "11150": {"synopsis":"The longer taken off the sum; DE' = both steps."},
        "11151": {"comment":"Sum - the longer"},
        "11153": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "11154": {"comment":"HL = the straight step"},
        "11155": {"comment":"DE = both steps"},
        "11156": {"comment":"Both kept again"},
        "11158": {"comment":"The pixel"},
        "11160": {"synopsis":"The sum back as it was; DE' = the straight step.","comment":"Sum back"},
        "11161": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "11162": {"comment":"DE = the straight step"},
        "11163": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "11164": {"synopsis":"x + E's step (-1, 0 or 1), y + D's, then the pixel (PLOT_XY).","comment":"HL = the last x"},
        "11167": {"comment":"BC = $FFFF or 0 from E's step"},
        "11169": {"comment":"E = 1?"},
        "11171": {"comment":"Yes: BC = 1"},
        "11173": {"synopsis":"x + the step; then y + D's step.","comment":"x + the step"},
        "11174": {"comment":"BC = x"},
        "11176": {"comment":"HL = the last y"},
        "11179": {"comment":"DE = D's step"},
        "11180": {"comment":"D = 1?"},
        "11181": {"comment":"Yes: DE = 1"},
        "11183": {"comment":"No: D back ($FF or 0)"},
        "11184": {"synopsis":"y + the step; the pixel plotted; the count's low byte down.","comment":"y + the step"},
        "11185": {"comment":"The pixel (PLOT_XY)"},
        "11188": {"comment":"The sum's set again"},
        "11189": {"comment":"The count's low byte"},
        "11191": {"comment":"Not 0: the next pixel"},
        "11193": {"comment":"Keyboard row SPACE to B"},
        "11195": {"comment":"Read"},
        "11197": {"comment":"Bit 0: SPACE"},
        "11198": {"comment":"Not pressed: on"},
        "11200": {"comment":"Keyboard row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "11202": {"comment":"Read"},
        "11204": {"comment":"Bit 0: CAPS SHIFT"},
        "11205": {"comment":"Not pressed: on"},
        "11207": {"comment":"ROM 1's TAPE_BREAK_TEST"},
        "11210": {"comment":"NZ: on"},
        "11212": {"comment":"BREAK: the first stack again"},
        "11215": {"comment":"Error code $14 (report L)"},
        "11217": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11220": {"synopsis":"The count's high byte down; on while it is not negative.","comment":"The count's high byte"},
        "11222": {"comment":"Not past 0: on"},
        "11225": {"comment":"The steps dropped"},
        "11227": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11249": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE in screen modes 1-15: ROM 3's CIRCLE_CMD calls its $2BE5, which comes here through\nits NEXTREG $8C,$80 at $2BED when $5C7F's low four bits are not 0; that call's return is\ndropped. ROM 1 is selected (NextReg $8E = $01); r (ROM 1's FP_TO_BC: |r|), y and x\n(FP_TO_SIGNED_BC, kept at $5CAE and $5CAC) come off the calculator stack. On the other stack\n(SWAP_SP), with D = -r, C = 0 and the error term IX = 2 - 2r, each step plots four points,\n(x - D, y + C), (x - C, y - D), (x + D, y - C) and (x + C, y + D) (CIRCLE_PLOT_SWAP; the\nlast by PLOT_XY, the last point), then C goes up (IX + 2C + 1) when IX is negative or not\nabove C, and D goes up (IX + 2D + 1) when IX is then above C; until D is no longer negative.\nThen GFX_SWAP_EXIT.","comment":"ROM 1 selected; this ROM stays in its place"},
        "11253": {"comment":"CIRCLE_CMD's call dropped"},
        "11254": {"comment":"BC = |r|"},
        "11257": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11258": {"comment":"BC = y"},
        "11261": {"comment":"Kept at $5CAE"},
        "11265": {"comment":"BC = x"},
        "11268": {"comment":"Kept at $5CAC"},
        "11272": {"comment":"DE = r"},
        "11273": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "11276": {"comment":"DE = -r"},
        "11282": {"comment":"D = -r, HL = r"},
        "11283": {"comment":"IX = 2 - 2r"},
        "11291": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "11294": {"synopsis":"One step: D and C kept, D + C and D - C stacked for CIRCLE_PLOT_SWAP; four points plotted.","comment":"D kept"},
        "11295": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "11296": {"comment":"D + C"},
        "11299": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "11300": {"comment":"D - C"},
        "11305": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "11306": {"comment":"x - D"},
        "11312": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11313": {"comment":"y + C"},
        "11317": {"comment":"Plotted"},
        "11320": {"comment":"x - D + (D - C) = x - C"},
        "11321": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11323": {"comment":"BC = D + C"},
        "11325": {"comment":"y + C - (D + C) = y - D"},
        "11327": {"comment":"Plotted"},
        "11330": {"comment":"x - C + (D + C) = x + D"},
        "11331": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11332": {"comment":"BC = D - C"},
        "11334": {"comment":"y - D + (D - C) = y - C"},
        "11335": {"comment":"Plotted"},
        "11339": {"comment":"x + D - (D - C) = x + C"},
        "11341": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11342": {"comment":"BC = D + C"},
        "11343": {"comment":"y - C + (D + C) = y + D"},
        "11344": {"comment":"D - C dropped"},
        "11345": {"comment":"BC = x + C"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Plotted, kept as the last point"},
        "11350": {"comment":"BC = C"},
        "11351": {"comment":"DE = D"},
        "11352": {"comment":"HL = the error term"},
        "11355": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "11357": {"comment":"Yes: C up"},
        "11360": {"comment":"Above C?"},
        "11362": {"comment":"Yes: C stays"},
        "11364": {"synopsis":"C + 1; IX + 2C + 1.","comment":"C + 1"},
        "11365": {"comment":"IX + 2C + 1"},
        "11371": {"synopsis":"D goes up (D + 1, IX + 2D + 1) when IX is above C.","comment":"HL = the error term"},
        "11374": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "11376": {"comment":"Yes: D stays"},
        "11379": {"comment":"Not above C?"},
        "11381": {"comment":"Then D stays"},
        "11383": {"comment":"D + 1"},
        "11384": {"comment":"IX + 2D + 1"},
        "11390": {"synopsis":"Until D is no longer negative; then GFX_SWAP_EXIT.","comment":"D still negative?"},
        "11392": {"comment":"Yes: the next step"},
        "11394": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11397": {"synopsis":"Plots the point x = DE, y = HL (PLOT_XY_ONLY), then swaps the two words under the return\naddress.\nExit: HL = x, DE = y; BC = the word that was on top (now the second).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = x"},
        "11399": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11400": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11401": {"comment":"Plotted"},
        "11404": {"comment":"DE = y"},
        "11405": {"comment":"HL = x"},
        "11406": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "11407": {"comment":"into AF'"},
        "11408": {"comment":"BC = the top word"},
        "11409": {"comment":"The one under it"},
        "11410": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "11412": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "11413": {"comment":"back on top"},
        "11415": {"synopsis":"ERASE \"name\": deletes the files the name matches (reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's $26E6, a\nCALL_ALT with the word $2C97). The name (NAME_ARG, $3526: empty is error code $2C) copied to\n$E090 in bank 7 and parsed (PARSE_FILESPEC); no file name in it is error code $2C ($352C).\nWith a wildcard the question \"Erase \" (ROM 1's MSG_ERASE, PRINT_LOWER_TEXT), the name\n(PRINT_MSG) and \"? (Y/N)\" (ROM 1's $2B76, in ASK_YES_NO) comes first: an NZ answer returns.\nThen ROM 2's DOS_DELETE ($0124) and DOS_RESULT.","comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "11418": {"comment":"To $E090 in bank 7"},
        "11421": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11422": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11423": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11426": {"comment":"HL = $E090"},
        "11428": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11431": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "11434": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "11437": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11440": {"comment":"Bit 3 clear: no file name, an error"},
        "11442": {"comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "11445": {"synopsis":"A name: does it have a wildcard (C bit 2)?","comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "11447": {"comment":"No: delete at once"},
        "11449": {"comment":"\"Erase \" (NextZXOS ROM 1's MSG_ERASE)"},
        "11452": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_LOWER_TEXT"},
        "11455": {"comment":"The name"},
        "11456": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11457": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11460": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG"},
        "11463": {"synopsis":"The name printed: \"? (Y/N)\" and the key (ROM 1's $2B76, in ASK_YES_NO).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11466": {"comment":"\"? (Y/N)\" and the key: ROM 1's $2B76"},
        "11469": {"synopsis":"NZ (no) returns; otherwise the files are deleted in bank 7.","comment":"The name back"},
        "11470": {"comment":"NZ: not deleted"},
        "11471": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11474": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_DELETE"},
        "11477": {"comment":"The result"},
        "11479": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"a\" TO \"b\" (the syntax table's word at $04E3, after classes $0A and $0C): the second\nname (NAME_ARG, $3526) starting '+' or '-' is MOVE_ATTRIB; otherwise it goes to $E090 and\nthe first to $D82B (bank 7, $FF-ended) and ROM 2's DOS_RENAME ($0127) renames the file (HL =\nthe old name, DE = the new); then DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The second name (on top of the stack)"},
        "11482": {"comment":"Its first character"},
        "11483": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "11485": {"comment":"An attribute change"},
        "11487": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "11489": {"comment":"An attribute change"},
        "11491": {"comment":"The new name to $E090"},
        "11494": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11495": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11496": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11499": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11502": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "11505": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11508": {"comment":"The old name"},
        "11511": {"comment":"to $D82B"},
        "11514": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11515": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11516": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11519": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11522": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "11525": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11528": {"comment":"HL = the old name"},
        "11529": {"comment":"DE = the new name"},
        "11530": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11533": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_RENAME"},
        "11536": {"comment":"The result"},
        "11538": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"d:\" IN \"partition\" (the syntax table's word at $04DC): maps drive d to a partition, a\ndevice or an image file:\n1. The second string (PART_NAME_ARG): \"u>name\" is partition name of unit u, looked for by\n   ROM 2's IDE_PARTITION_FIND ($00B5, HL = $F752) for BC, its number; \"u>\" alone the unit\n   itself; anything else an image file ($D82B, A = $FF).\n2. The drive (DRIVE_ARG, L = its letter); ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP ($00F1: A = the unit, BC = the\n   partition or the image's name).\nThen DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The partition, device or image"},
        "11541": {"comment":"A = the unit (or $FF, an image)"},
        "11542": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11543": {"comment":"No partition name: BC as it is"},
        "11545": {"comment":"The partition's name"},
        "11548": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11551": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PARTITION_FIND: BC = its number"},
        "11554": {"comment":"Not found: the error"},
        "11556": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11559": {"synopsis":"The drive letter (DRIVE_ARG) and ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP.","comment":"The partition (or the image's name) kept"},
        "11560": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "11563": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "11564": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "11565": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11568": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP"},
        "11571": {"synopsis":"Ends a ROM 2 call: bank 0; carry returns; otherwise ROM 1's DOS_ERROR reports the error in\nA.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11574": {"comment":"Done"},
        "11575": {"comment":"ROM 1's DOS_ERROR, which reports A"},
        "11578": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"d:\" OUT (the syntax table's word at $04DF): the drive letter (DRIVE_ARG) and ROM 2's\nIDE_DOS_UNMAP ($00F4); then DOS_RESULT.","comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "11581": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11584": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_UNMAP"},
        "11587": {"comment":"The result"},
        "11589": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"name\" TO \"+x\" or \"-x\": the second string must be two characters (error code $47\notherwise), x one of P, S or A in either case (error code $47). The attribute's bit (P 2, S\n1, A 0) goes in D to set ('+') or E to clear ('-'), and ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES ($0148)\nchanges it on the file (the first string, at $F700); then DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The length"},
        "11590": {"comment":"less 2"},
        "11592": {"comment":"0: two characters?"},
        "11593": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11595": {"comment":"Error code $47"},
        "11597": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11600": {"synopsis":"B = the sign; the letter, as a capital, must be P, S or A.","comment":"B = the sign"},
        "11602": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "11604": {"comment":"As a capital"},
        "11606": {"comment":"P?"},
        "11608": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11610": {"comment":"S?"},
        "11612": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11614": {"comment":"A?"},
        "11616": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11618": {"comment":"None of them: error code $47"},
        "11620": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11623": {"synopsis":"The sign and the letter kept; the file's name (NAME_ARG, not empty) to $F700 in bank 7, $FF\nafter it.","comment":"The sign kept"},
        "11624": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "11625": {"comment":"The file's name (not empty)"},
        "11628": {"comment":"to $F700"},
        "11631": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11632": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11635": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11638": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "11641": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11644": {"comment":"No bits to set or clear"},
        "11647": {"comment":"C will hold the bit"},
        "11649": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "11650": {"comment":"P?"},
        "11652": {"comment":"No"},
        "11654": {"comment":"P: bit 2"},
        "11658": {"synopsis":"S: bit 1.","comment":"S?"},
        "11660": {"comment":"No: A"},
        "11662": {"comment":"S: bit 1"},
        "11666": {"synopsis":"A: bit 0.","comment":"A: bit 0"},
        "11668": {"synopsis":"A = the sign: '+' puts the bit in D (to set), '-' in E (to clear).","comment":"The sign (B, pushed with C)"},
        "11669": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "11671": {"comment":"No: clear"},
        "11673": {"comment":"'+': D, the bits to set"},
        "11676": {"synopsis":"'-': the bit in E.","comment":"'-': E, the bits to clear"},
        "11677": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES on the name at $F700 (bank 7).","comment":"The name"},
        "11680": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11683": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES"},
        "11686": {"comment":"The result"},
        "11688": {"synopsis":"Takes a partition, device or image name from the calculator stack (ROM 1's STK_FETCH); a\nstring of 0 or 1 characters, or of 256 or more, is error code $2C:\n1. One or two digits and '>' first: the digits are the unit (D). Nothing after the '>'\n   returns NC with D = the unit. Otherwise the rest (16 characters at most, error code $2C)\n   goes to $F752 in bank 7, padded to 16 with spaces from NextZXOS ROM 1's $3FA2, and\n   returns with carry.\n2. Otherwise the whole string is an image file's name: IMAGE_NAME_ARG.\nExit: carry and D = the unit, the name at $F752; NC and D = the unit (no name); NC, D = $FF\nand BC = $D82B, an image file's name ($FF-ended).","comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH: DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "11691": {"comment":"256 characters or more?"},
        "11693": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "11695": {"comment":"Fewer than 2?"},
        "11698": {"comment":"No: go on"},
        "11700": {"synopsis":"Error code $2C (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "11702": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11705": {"synopsis":"The digits read (DIGIT_ACC); a '>' must follow them.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "11706": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "11707": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11708": {"comment":"The unit, 0 so far"},
        "11710": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "11713": {"comment":"No: an image file's name"},
        "11715": {"comment":"A second digit, if any"},
        "11718": {"comment":"D = the unit"},
        "11719": {"comment":"Nothing left?"},
        "11721": {"comment":"Then not a partition"},
        "11723": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11726": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "11728": {"comment":"No: an image file's name"},
        "11730": {"comment":"Drop the start"},
        "11731": {"comment":"Drop the length"},
        "11732": {"comment":"The name's length"},
        "11734": {"comment":"None: the unit alone (NC)"},
        "11735": {"comment":"More than 16?"},
        "11737": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "11739": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "11740": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "11741": {"comment":"The name to $F752"},
        "11744": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11747": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "11748": {"comment":"16 - the length"},
        "11751": {"comment":"None: no padding"},
        "11753": {"comment":"Spaces in NextZXOS ROM 1"},
        "11756": {"comment":"BC = the spaces wanted"},
        "11757": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11760": {"synopsis":"Carry: a partition name; D = the unit.","comment":"Carry: a partition's name"},
        "11761": {"comment":"D = the unit"},
        "11763": {"synopsis":"An image file: the string to $D82B in bank 7 and an $FF after it (the byte at NextZXOS ROM\n1's $0004); BC = $D82B, D = $FF, NC.","comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11764": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "11765": {"comment":"The image's name to $D82B"},
        "11768": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11769": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11772": {"comment":"NextZXOS ROM 1's $0004, an $FF"},
        "11775": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "11778": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "11781": {"comment":"BC = $D82B, the image's name"},
        "11782": {"comment":"D = $FF: an image file"},
        "11784": {"comment":"NC: no partition name"},
        "11786": {"synopsis":"Adds the decimal digit at HL to E (E = E x 10 + the digit), HL and BC moved on past it.\nExit: NC when it was a digit; carry, nothing changed, when not.\nChanges: AF, D, E, HL, BC.","comment":"The character as a digit"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "11790": {"comment":"D = 10"},
        "11792": {"comment":"10 or more?"},
        "11793": {"comment":"Carry then, NC for a digit"},
        "11794": {"comment":"Not a digit"},
        "11795": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11797": {"comment":"DE = E x 10"},
        "11799": {"comment":"plus the digit"},
        "11801": {"comment":"NC: a digit"},
        "11803": {"synopsis":"FORMAT (the syntax table's word at $03A8, class $0E), A = the character after it: FORMAT\nLINE n (FORMAT_LINE) and FORMAT LPRINT \"x\" [;\"y\"] (FORMAT_LPRINT) only check their operands\nand do nothing more when running. Otherwise a string (ROM 1's CLASS_A) and the statement's\nend; running, that is error code $52.","comment":"LINE?"},
        "11805": {"comment":"Yes: FORMAT LINE"},
        "11807": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "11809": {"comment":"Yes: FORMAT LPRINT"},
        "11811": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A: a string"},
        "11814": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11817": {"comment":"Error code $52"},
        "11819": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11822": {"synopsis":"FORMAT LINE: past LINE, a number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6), the statement's end; then return.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6"},
        "11825": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11828": {"comment":"Running: nothing done"},
        "11829": {"synopsis":"FORMAT LPRINT: past LPRINT, a string (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_A), and when ';' follows another\none.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_A"},
        "11832": {"comment":"The character after the string"},
        "11833": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "11835": {"comment":"No"},
        "11837": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11838": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A"},
        "11841": {"synopsis":"The statement's end ($0149); then return.","comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11844": {"comment":"Running: nothing done"},
        "11845": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (from NextZXOS ROM 1's $05F9, which jumps to CALL_ALT_GO with\nBC = $2E45; T_ADDR's low byte tells which: 0 SAVE, 1 LOAD, 2 VERIFY, 3 MERGE, made from the\ntoken in IXh):\n1. A '*' is skipped; the name (ROM 1's CLASS_A).\n2. When running: the header's room (17 or 34 bytes, ROM 3's WORK_ROOM); LOAD \"*\" alone with\n   a disk drive as LOAD's default calls ROM 2's $0E14 (PORTS_P3_COMPAT) and DOS_BOOT, and on\n   '#' goes on with the name \"disk\" (copied to $5CAC); any other result stops with the +3DOS\n   error (SE_DOS_ERROR).\n3. The device: 'T:' or a drive letter A-P before the name, else the default ($5B7A for SAVE\n   and VERIFY, $5B79 for LOAD and MERGE); a name of just 'x:' sets that default\n   (DOS_SET_DRIVE for a drive).\n4. The name to the header (SAVE needs 1-10 characters, report F) and, for a disk, whole to\n   $F700 in bank 7.\n5. What follows the name: SE_KIND (DATA here, $9A from SE_BANK, the rest past $3000).","comment":"T_ADDR's low byte = 3 for MERGE"},
        "11850": {"comment":"A = the command's token"},
        "11852": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "11856": {"comment":"SAVE 0, LOAD 1, VERIFY 2 from the token"},
        "11860": {"comment":"Into T_ADDR's low byte"},
        "11861": {"synopsis":"The name: a leading '*' skipped.","comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "11862": {"comment":"A '*' before the name?"},
        "11864": {"comment":"Then skipped (SKIP_ONE)"},
        "11867": {"comment":"The name (ROM 1's CLASS_A, a string)"},
        "11870": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "11874": {"comment":"Then on to what follows the name"},
        "11877": {"comment":"17 bytes for one header (SAVE)"},
        "11880": {"comment":"LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE?"},
        "11886": {"comment":"34 bytes: the wanted header and the one read"},
        "11888": {"synopsis":"The header's room (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM), IX at it; 11 spaces.","comment":"The room (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "11891": {"comment":"IX = the header"},
        "11894": {"comment":"11 spaces: the type and the name"},
        "11898": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"One space"},
        "11902": {"comment":"The name's first byte $FF: no name yet"},
        "11906": {"comment":"The name off the calculator stack (ROM 1's STK_FETCH)"},
        "11909": {"comment":"Its start and length kept"},
        "11911": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "11912": {"comment":"The statement ends here? (ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)"},
        "11915": {"comment":"No"},
        "11917": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "11924": {"comment":"LOAD's default drive tape?"},
        "11931": {"comment":"A one-character name"},
        "11936": {"comment":"...which is '*'?"},
        "11941": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0E14 (PORTS_P3_COMPAT)"},
        "11944": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "11946": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11949": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_BOOT"},
        "11952": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11955": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "11957": {"comment":"A '#' back?"},
        "11959": {"comment":"The name dropped"},
        "11961": {"comment":"\"disk\""},
        "11964": {"comment":"copied to $5CAC"},
        "11967": {"comment":"4 characters"},
        "11970": {"comment":"Kept over the copy"},
        "11972": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "11974": {"comment":"BC, DE back"},
        "11976": {"comment":"The new name: $5CAC, 4 characters"},
        "11978": {"comment":"'#': on with the name \"disk\""},
        "11980": {"synopsis":"An error from a +3DOS call: E = $FF, so the code is made from A (SE_ERROR_E). Also from\n$33D4, $3428 and $34CF.","comment":"E = $FF: the code from A"},
        "11982": {"synopsis":"Stops with the error that E names: file 0 closed first (ROM 1's CLOSE_FILE_0), then ROM 1's\nFILE_ERROR_A from $08E4, past its LD E,(HL), so E is the error byte (bit 7 set: the code\nmade from A, a +3DOS error).","comment":"The error kept"},
        "11984": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLOSE_FILE_0"},
        "11987": {"comment":"Back"},
        "11989": {"comment":"ROM 1's FILE_ERROR_A from $08E4"},
        "11992": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code A (SE_ERROR_E with E = A). From the name and DATA checks here and from\n$3203, $3503.","comment":"E = the code"},
        "11995": {"synopsis":"The name \"disk\", 4 bytes and no end mark, copied to $5CAC by TAPE_COMMAND for LOAD \"*\" (a\n'#' back from DOS_BOOT)."},
        "11999": {"synopsis":"A ':' second: the first character may name the device (T, or a drive letter A-P).","comment":"The name's second character"},
        "12002": {"comment":"A ':' second?"},
        "12004": {"comment":"No: no device in the name"},
        "12006": {"comment":"The first character, made capital"},
        "12009": {"comment":"'T': tape"},
        "12013": {"comment":"'A' to 'P': a drive"},
        "12021": {"synopsis":"No device in the name: SAVE's and VERIFY's drive ($5B7A) or LOAD's and MERGE's ($5B79).","comment":"LOAD and MERGE (T_ADDR bit 0)?"},
        "12026": {"comment":"A = SAVE's and VERIFY's default drive ($5B7A)"},
        "12031": {"comment":"A = LOAD's and MERGE's ($5B79)"},
        "12034": {"synopsis":"$5B5E = the device.","comment":"$5B5E = the device"},
        "12037": {"comment":"On with the name"},
        "12039": {"synopsis":"A device in the name: $5B5E = its letter; a name of only \"x:\" sets the default: a drive\nbecomes ROM 2's default too (DOS_SET_DRIVE), then SE_KEEP_DEFAULT.","comment":"$5B5E = the device in the name"},
        "12042": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "12043": {"comment":"The statement does not end here?"},
        "12048": {"comment":"Only \"x:\" in the name?"},
        "12052": {"comment":"No: a name follows"},
        "12054": {"comment":"The device"},
        "12057": {"comment":"Tape: no drive to set"},
        "12061": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "12064": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE"},
        "12067": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12070": {"comment":"Failed: the +3DOS error in A"},
        "12072": {"synopsis":"The letter kept as the default: $5B79 for LOAD and MERGE, $5B7A for SAVE and VERIFY.","comment":"LOAD and MERGE (T_ADDR bit 0)?"},
        "12077": {"comment":"A = the device"},
        "12080": {"comment":"SAVE and VERIFY: $5B7A"},
        "12082": {"comment":"LOAD and MERGE: $5B79 = the device"},
        "12087": {"synopsis":"$5B7A set.","comment":"$5B7A = the device"},
        "12090": {"synopsis":"The length and name dropped: the command ends.","comment":"The name dropped: the command ends"},
        "12093": {"synopsis":"A device and a name: a drive goes on with the whole name; for T: the \"T:\" is skipped.","comment":"The device"},
        "12096": {"comment":"A drive?"},
        "12098": {"comment":"Then the name as it is"},
        "12100": {"comment":"Tape: the \"T:\" skipped"},
        "12108": {"synopsis":"Tape: SE_TAPE_NAME. A drive: an empty name is error code $0E (report F).","comment":"The device"},
        "12111": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "12115": {"comment":"An empty name?"},
        "12117": {"comment":"Error code $0E (report F, Invalid file name)"},
        "12119": {"comment":"Empty: stop"},
        "12122": {"synopsis":"The whole name to $F700 in bank 7 (ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7), $FF after it; the header takes\n10 characters.","comment":"HL = $F700 in bank 7"},
        "12125": {"comment":"HL = the name, DE = $F700"},
        "12126": {"comment":"The whole name copied to bank 7"},
        "12129": {"comment":"The stacked length dropped"},
        "12130": {"comment":"BC = 10: the header's part of the name"},
        "12133": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "12136": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "12139": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12142": {"comment":"On"},
        "12144": {"synopsis":"Tape: BC = the length.","comment":"BC = the name's length"},
        "12145": {"synopsis":"DE = the name.","comment":"DE = the name"},
        "12146": {"synopsis":"The name's length checked: 1-10 characters are copied as they are; SAVE with none or more is\nerror code $0E (report F).","comment":"HL = -10"},
        "12149": {"comment":"BC - 1"},
        "12150": {"comment":"Carry: none, or more than 10"},
        "12151": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "12152": {"comment":"No carry: copied as it is"},
        "12154": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12158": {"comment":"Error code $0E (report F)"},
        "12160": {"comment":"SAVE: stop"},
        "12163": {"comment":"An empty name?"},
        "12165": {"comment":"Then the $FF stays"},
        "12167": {"comment":"Otherwise only 10 characters"},
        "12170": {"synopsis":"The name copied after the type byte.","comment":"DE = the header's name, past its type byte"},
        "12175": {"comment":"The name copied"},
        "12177": {"synopsis":"What follows the name ($5B65 = $FF first: the usual memory): DATA here; otherwise SE_BANK.","comment":"$5B65 = $FF: the usual memory"},
        "12182": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "12183": {"comment":"DATA?"},
        "12185": {"comment":"No"},
        "12187": {"comment":"Not for MERGE ($3092)"},
        "12190": {"comment":"Past DATA"},
        "12191": {"comment":"The array (ROM 3's LOOK_VARS)"},
        "12194": {"comment":"A = T_ADDR"},
        "12197": {"comment":"No carry: found"},
        "12199": {"comment":"Not found: the name's place to K_CUR"},
        "12202": {"comment":"...and DEST, for a new array"},
        "12205": {"comment":"HL = 0: no old array"},
        "12208": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "12209": {"comment":"Then made later"},
        "12211": {"synopsis":"Error code $01 (report 2, Variable not found).","comment":"Error code $01 (report 2, Variable not found)"},
        "12213": {"comment":"Stop"},
        "12216": {"synopsis":"An array found (ROM 3's LOOK_VARS): NZ is report C ($3098); when running its length into the\nheader (SAVE needs B bit 7).","comment":"NZ: report C"},
        "12219": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "12225": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12228": {"comment":"SAVE: B bit 7 clear?"},
        "12230": {"comment":"Then error code $01"},
        "12232": {"synopsis":"The array's length at IX + 11.","comment":"Past the name"},
        "12233": {"comment":"The array's length at IX + 11"},
        "12242": {"comment":"HL at the array's data"},
        "12243": {"synopsis":"The name byte (bit 7 set) at IX + 14.","comment":"The name byte, bit 7 set"},
        "12248": {"comment":"Type 1: a number array"},
        "12250": {"comment":"Bit 6: a string array?"},
        "12254": {"comment":"Type 2"},
        "12255": {"synopsis":"Type 1 (numbers) or 2 (strings, C bit 6).","comment":"The type"},
        "12258": {"synopsis":"Past ')', the statement ends; then on at $3143 with the header made.","comment":"DE = the place, HL = CH_ADD"},
        "12259": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "12260": {"comment":"A ')'?"},
        "12262": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "12264": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12265": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12268": {"comment":"HL = the array's place"},
        "12269": {"comment":"On with the header made ($3143)"},
        "12272": {"synopsis":"$9A n [, offset, length]: a 16K RAM bank (n by ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6; not for MERGE). Without\nthe two: HL = $C000, DE = 16K for SAVE, 0 for the others; with them, on at $300D.","comment":"$9A?"},
        "12274": {"comment":"No: the next kind"},
        "12276": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "12279": {"comment":"Past it, then the bank's number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6)"},
        "12282": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "12284": {"comment":"Yes: the offset and length"},
        "12286": {"comment":"HL = $C000, the bank's start"},
        "12289": {"comment":"DE = 16K"},
        "12292": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12295": {"comment":"SAVE (T_ADDR 0)?"},
        "12296": {"comment":"Then all of it"},
        "12298": {"comment":"The others: length 0, the file's own"},
        "12299": {"comment":"The others too"},
        "12301": {"synopsis":"BANK n, offset, length: past ',' and two numbers (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8); offset + length\nmust stay within the bank's 16K (report B, ERR_B). Then HL = $C000 + the offset and DE = the\nlength.","comment":"Past ',', then two numbers (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "12304": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12307": {"comment":"BC = the length (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "12310": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12311": {"comment":"BC = the offset in the bank (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "12314": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "12316": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "12317": {"comment":"HL = the offset + the length"},
        "12318": {"comment":"Over 64K: report B"},
        "12321": {"comment":"The last byte"},
        "12322": {"comment":"Past the bank's 16K?"},
        "12325": {"comment":"Past the bank's 16K: report B"},
        "12328": {"comment":"HL = $C000 + the offset"},
        "12332": {"comment":"On"},
        "12334": {"synopsis":"The statement must end (STATEMENT_END).","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12337": {"synopsis":"The bank's number (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE) into $5B65 and passed to ROM 1's $330B (2.08's\nBANK_MAP: the bank checked and taken as BASIC's); then SE_START_LEN with the start and\nlength pushed.","comment":"The length and the start kept"},
        "12339": {"comment":"A = the bank's number (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "12342": {"comment":"$5B65 = the bank"},
        "12345": {"comment":"The bank through ROM 1's $330B"},
        "12348": {"comment":"The start and length into the header, type 3"},
        "12351": {"synopsis":"$9C: the current screen mode's picture: modes 0 and 5 as SCREEN$; mode 2 (Layer 2) type 5,\n48K; the others type 4, 12K ($3000); start 0. $5B65 = $FE. Not for MERGE.","comment":"$9C?"},
        "12353": {"comment":"No: $EE or $BA?"},
        "12355": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "12358": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12359": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12362": {"comment":"HL = 0: the start"},
        "12365": {"comment":"The screen mode"},
        "12370": {"comment":"Mode 0: the ULA screen, as SCREEN$"},
        "12372": {"comment":"Mode 1 kind 1 (5): the same"},
        "12374": {"comment":"Mode 5 too"},
        "12376": {"comment":"Mode 2 (Layer 2)?"},
        "12378": {"comment":"$5B65 = $FE: a picture of the layers"},
        "12383": {"comment":"Mode 2"},
        "12385": {"comment":"Others: type 4, 12K ($3000)"},
        "12392": {"comment":"On"},
        "12394": {"synopsis":"Type 5, 48K.","comment":"Mode 2: type 5, 48K ($C000)"},
        "12401": {"synopsis":"The length and start into the header (SE_HEADER_SET).","comment":"The length and start into the header"},
        "12403": {"synopsis":"$EE or $BA: the DivMMC memory's routine at $29E1, with A the keyword, gives the start (HL)\nand length (BC); type 3; $5B65 = $FD. Not for MERGE.","comment":"$EE?"},
        "12407": {"comment":"$BA?"},
        "12409": {"comment":"No: SCREEN$?"},
        "12411": {"synopsis":"Not for MERGE; past the keyword; the statement must end.","comment":"E = the keyword"},
        "12412": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "12415": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12416": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12419": {"comment":"A = the keyword"},
        "12420": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $29E1: HL, BC"},
        "12425": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "12427": {"comment":"$5B65 = $FD"},
        "12432": {"comment":"Type 3, start HL, length DE"},
        "12434": {"synopsis":"Report C for MERGE (T_ADDR 3); returns for the others.","comment":"MERGE?"},
        "12437": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "12440": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, Nonsense in BASIC) through ROM 1's ERROR_128_A.","comment":"Error code $0B: report C, Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "12442": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "12445": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$: 6912 ($1B00) bytes from $4000, type 3. Not for MERGE.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "12447": {"comment":"No: CODE?"},
        "12449": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "12452": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12453": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12456": {"synopsis":"6912 bytes from $4000.","comment":"DE = 6912 bytes"},
        "12459": {"comment":"HL = $4000"},
        "12462": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "12464": {"synopsis":"CODE: start and length; SAVE needs both (report C); for the others a missing one is 0, taken\nfrom the file (ROM 1's STACK_0_IF_RUN). Not for MERGE.","comment":"CODE?"},
        "12466": {"comment":"No: a program"},
        "12468": {"comment":"Not for MERGE"},
        "12471": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12472": {"comment":"The statement ends here (ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)?"},
        "12475": {"comment":"No: a start follows"},
        "12477": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12481": {"comment":"SAVE needs a start: report C"},
        "12483": {"comment":"0 stacked for the start (ROM 1's STACK_0_IF_RUN)"},
        "12486": {"comment":"And for the length"},
        "12488": {"synopsis":"The start (ROM 1's CLASS_6).","comment":"The start (ROM 1's CLASS_6)"},
        "12491": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "12493": {"comment":"Yes: a length follows"},
        "12495": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12499": {"comment":"SAVE needs a length: report C"},
        "12501": {"synopsis":"No length: 0 (ROM 1's STACK_0_IF_RUN).","comment":"0 stacked for the length (STACK_0_IF_RUN)"},
        "12504": {"comment":"On"},
        "12506": {"synopsis":"',' and the length.","comment":"Past ','"},
        "12507": {"comment":"The length (CLASS_6)"},
        "12510": {"synopsis":"The statement must end; the length and start off the calculator stack (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD).","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "12513": {"comment":"BC = the length (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "12516": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12517": {"comment":"BC = the start (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "12520": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12521": {"synopsis":"HL = the start, DE = the length.","comment":"HL = the start"},
        "12522": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "12523": {"synopsis":"Type 3.","comment":"Type 3"},
        "12527": {"synopsis":"The length at IX + 11, the start at IX + 13; then SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD.","comment":"The length at IX + 11"},
        "12533": {"comment":"The start at IX + 13"},
        "12539": {"comment":"On to SAVE or LOAD"},
        "12541": {"synopsis":"A program: LINE (SAVE only) or nothing; without LINE the header's line is $80xx (no\nauto-run).","comment":"LINE?"},
        "12543": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "12545": {"comment":"No: the statement must end"},
        "12548": {"comment":"IX + 14 = $80: no line to run"},
        "12552": {"comment":"On"},
        "12554": {"synopsis":"LINE n (SAVE only, else report C): past LINE, B = 0; the return address on the stack\n(ALT_ROM_OFF) is replaced by ROM 1's $20CD and jumped to. ROM 1 takes the line there (as\nJUMP_CMD does), puts PPC into the header (IX + 13), runs $3AA8 with C = $21 and comes back\nat SE_PROG_HEADER, with STMT_RET ($0941) as the command's return.","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12558": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "12560": {"comment":"Past LINE"},
        "12561": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "12563": {"comment":"ROM 1's $20CD in place of the return address"},
        "12566": {"comment":"HL = the return address (ALT_ROM_OFF)"},
        "12567": {"comment":"Left there: ROM 1 at $20CD takes the line and comes back at $3118"},
        "12568": {"synopsis":"Type 0: the length (E_LINE - PROG - 1, the program and its variables) and the program's own\nlength (VARS - PROG); LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE first clear E_PPC and the word at $D752 in bank\n7 (ROM 0's $0D9A).","comment":"Type 0: a program"},
        "12572": {"comment":"Not SAVE?"},
        "12576": {"comment":"SAVE: on"},
        "12578": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0, the word at $D752 in bank 7 too (ROM 0's $0D9A)"},
        "12583": {"synopsis":"The two lengths into the header (IX + 11, IX + 15); HL = PROG.","comment":"HL = E_LINE - PROG - 1"},
        "12593": {"comment":"...the program and its variables, at IX + 11"},
        "12599": {"comment":"HL = VARS - PROG: the program alone"},
        "12604": {"comment":"At IX + 15"},
        "12610": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "12611": {"synopsis":"SAVE goes to SAVE_CONTROL; the others go on with HL the destination kept and IX at the\nheader's second half: tape LOAD_HEADER_LOOP, a disk LOAD_DISK_HDR.","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "12615": {"comment":"Then SAVE_CONTROL"},
        "12618": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "12619": {"comment":"IX = the second header, for the one read"},
        "12624": {"comment":"The device"},
        "12627": {"comment":"Not tape: the disk"},
        "12629": {"comment":"A disk: LOAD_DISK_HDR"},
        "12631": {"synopsis":"Tape: reads headers (17 bytes, flag 0, ROM 3's LD_BYTES) into the second half until one of\nthe wanted type and name arrives; each one's kind and name are shown on the upper screen\n(ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS).","comment":"IX kept"},
        "12633": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "12636": {"comment":"A = 0: a header's flag"},
        "12637": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "12638": {"comment":"One block (ROM 3's LD_BYTES)"},
        "12641": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "12643": {"comment":"Failed: the next one"},
        "12645": {"comment":"The upper screen's colours (ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS)"},
        "12648": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 3"},
        "12652": {"comment":"C = $80: not the wanted type"},
        "12654": {"comment":"The type read"},
        "12657": {"comment":"The wanted type?"},
        "12662": {"comment":"C = $F6: the wanted type"},
        "12664": {"synopsis":"A type over 5 is skipped; types 4 and 5 show as \"Layer 1: \" and \"Layer 2: \"\n(SHOW_LAYER_KIND, then the text at $2437), 0-3 through LOAD_KIND_MSG.","comment":"Type 6 or more?"},
        "12666": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "12668": {"comment":"Type 4 or 5?"},
        "12670": {"comment":"No: 0-3"},
        "12672": {"comment":"A new line first"},
        "12673": {"comment":"A new line first (ENTER, ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "12679": {"comment":"\"Layer \" and the digit (SHOW_LAYER_KIND)"},
        "12682": {"comment":"\": \" at $2437"},
        "12685": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_BIT7)"},
        "12688": {"comment":"On to the name"},
        "12690": {"synopsis":"Types 0-3: ROM 3's message for the type (PRINT_MESSAGE with the table at $09C0).","comment":"ROM 3's TAPE_KIND_MSGS"},
        "12693": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "12694": {"comment":"\"Program: \" etc. (ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE)"},
        "12698": {"synopsis":"The name shown and compared; a wanted name of $FF (any) counts as all 10.","comment":"DE = the header read"},
        "12701": {"comment":"HL = the wanted one's name"},
        "12705": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "12707": {"comment":"The wanted name $FF (any)?"},
        "12711": {"comment":"Then C + 10: all match"},
        "12714": {"synopsis":"The name: each character printed; C counts the matches up to 0.","comment":"The next character read"},
        "12716": {"comment":"The same as the wanted one?"},
        "12720": {"comment":"C counts the matches"},
        "12721": {"synopsis":"Prints the character (ROM 3's PRINT_A).","comment":"Printed (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "12724": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "12726": {"comment":"C bit 7: not the type, or not the name?"},
        "12728": {"comment":"Then the next header"},
        "12730": {"comment":"A new line (ENTER, ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "12735": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "12736": {"comment":"On to LOAD_CONTROL"},
        "12738": {"synopsis":"LOAD and MERGE from a disk (VERIFY does nothing): the file named at $F700 (bank 7) opened as\nfile 0 for reading through ROM 2's DOS_OPEN (access mode 1, create action 0, open action 1),\nwith bank 7 and the other stack; failing goes to SAVE_DOS_FAIL.","comment":"VERIFY?"},
        "12743": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "12744": {"comment":"VERIFY from a disk does nothing"},
        "12745": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "12746": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "12748": {"comment":"File 0, access mode 1"},
        "12752": {"comment":"Create action 0: no new file"},
        "12754": {"comment":"Open action 1: read its header"},
        "12756": {"comment":"The name at $F700"},
        "12759": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack (SWAP_SP_BANK7)"},
        "12762": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "12765": {"comment":"Failed: SAVE_DOS_FAIL"},
        "12768": {"synopsis":"Opened: its header data (ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD); its type must be the wanted one, or 3 for a\nwanted 4 or 5 (else LOAD_WRONG_TYPE).","comment":"File 0"},
        "12770": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD: IX = its header data"},
        "12773": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "12776": {"comment":"IX back, the file's header stacked"},
        "12778": {"comment":"HL = the file's header"},
        "12779": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "12782": {"comment":"A = the file's type"},
        "12783": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12786": {"comment":"The wanted type?"},
        "12789": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "12791": {"comment":"A CODE file (type 3)"},
        "12793": {"comment":"No: the wrong type"},
        "12795": {"comment":"...for a wanted type 4 or 5?"},
        "12799": {"comment":"Yes: taken"},
        "12801": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1D (the wrong file type) through $2ED8, which closes file 0 first.","comment":"Error code $1D: the wrong file type"},
        "12803": {"comment":"File 0 closed, then the error ($2ED8)"},
        "12806": {"synopsis":"The type and the 6 bytes after it in the file's header into the second half (ROM 1's\nCOPY_BANK7_TO_0).","comment":"The type into the header read"},
        "12809": {"comment":"DE = the header read + 11"},
        "12818": {"comment":"HL = the file's header + 1"},
        "12819": {"comment":"Its 6 bytes: length, start, second word"},
        "12821": {"comment":"Copied out of bank 7 (ROM 1's COPY_BANK7_TO_0)"},
        "12824": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "12825": {"synopsis":"The header is in (tape or disk): CODE and the pictures, and VERIFY of anything, go to\nLOAD_CODE_DATA; LOAD of a program or an array to LOAD_PROG_ARRAY; MERGE to MERGE_LOAD.","comment":"The wanted type"},
        "12828": {"comment":"CODE, or a picture?"},
        "12830": {"comment":"Yes: LOAD_CODE_DATA"},
        "12832": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "12836": {"comment":"A program or an array"},
        "12838": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "12840": {"comment":"Yes: MERGE_LOAD"},
        "12843": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, and LOAD of CODE: a wanted length (when not 0) shorter than the file's loads only\nthat many bytes; a program or array of another length is error code $1A (REPORT_R).","comment":"The destination kept"},
        "12844": {"comment":"HL = the wanted length"},
        "12850": {"comment":"DE = the file's"},
        "12856": {"comment":"No wanted length?"},
        "12858": {"comment":"Then the file's"},
        "12860": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "12864": {"comment":"Then the file's"},
        "12866": {"comment":"Wanted longer: DE stays the file's"},
        "12868": {"comment":"Wanted shorter: DE = the wanted one"},
        "12869": {"synopsis":"Lengths differ: REPORT_R unless CODE or a picture.","comment":"The wanted type"},
        "12872": {"comment":"A program or an array of another length"},
        "12874": {"comment":"is error code $1A (REPORT_R)"},
        "12877": {"synopsis":"HL: the wanted start, or the header's.","comment":"HL = the wanted start"},
        "12878": {"comment":"None?"},
        "12880": {"comment":"Given: kept"},
        "12882": {"comment":"Then the file's own"},
        "12888": {"synopsis":"The length DE into the header, then the block (DATA_AND_CLOSE). Also called by the program,\narray and MERGE paths.","comment":"The length into the header"},
        "12894": {"comment":"The block loaded (DATA_AND_CLOSE)"},
        "12897": {"synopsis":"LOAD of a program or an array (X_PTR keeps IX over ROM 3's calls): a new array is made at\nthe variables' end (ROM 3's COUNT_DEST_NAME, MAKE_ROOM, WRITE_STR_NAME); an old one or the\nprogram goes to LOAD_OLD_LENGTH.","comment":"DE = the length"},
        "12903": {"comment":"X_PTR = IX, kept over ROM 3's calls"},
        "12907": {"comment":"An old array (or a program)?"},
        "12909": {"comment":"An old variable, or a program, to replace?"},
        "12911": {"comment":"A new array: the length kept"},
        "12912": {"comment":"Its name's letters counted (ROM 3's COUNT_DEST_NAME)"},
        "12915": {"comment":"A = the count + 1 (B = $FF less the count)"},
        "12917": {"comment":"Room goes before the variables' $80 end"},
        "12921": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "12923": {"comment":"Plus the count + 1"},
        "12925": {"comment":"The count + 1 kept"},
        "12926": {"comment":"No letters counted?"},
        "12929": {"comment":"One more byte (a long name's $7F)"},
        "12930": {"synopsis":"Two more bytes, for the length word; the room made before the $80 (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), the\nname written into it (ROM 3's WRITE_STR_NAME) and the length word after it; then\nLOAD_ARR_DATA.","comment":"The length word's two bytes"},
        "12932": {"comment":"The room (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "12935": {"comment":"IX back on the loaded header"},
        "12939": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "12940": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "12941": {"comment":"B = the count + 1"},
        "12942": {"comment":"The wanted header's byte 14: the array's letter"},
        "12945": {"comment":"IXh = it, IXl = the count + 1"},
        "12949": {"comment":"The name into the room (ROM 3's WRITE_STR_NAME)"},
        "12952": {"comment":"HL = past the name"},
        "12953": {"comment":"DE = the array's length"},
        "12954": {"comment":"The length word after the name"},
        "12958": {"comment":"On to load the array into it"},
        "12960": {"synopsis":"An old array, or a program: only a new length longer than the old one needs more room, and\nthat is tested (ROM 3's TEST_ROOM with the difference + 5); then LOAD_KIND.","comment":"The new length kept"},
        "12961": {"comment":"And the old variable's address"},
        "12962": {"comment":"HL = the old length (the wanted header's)"},
        "12968": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12969": {"comment":"HL = new, DE = old"},
        "12970": {"comment":"New - old - 1: not longer?"},
        "12973": {"comment":"Not longer: no test"},
        "12975": {"comment":"The difference + 5"},
        "12979": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "12981": {"comment":"Room for it? (ROM 3's TEST_ROOM)"},
        "12984": {"synopsis":"A program: LOAD_PROGRAM. An array: the type, old length and new length go on the calculator\nstack as a string value (ROM 1's STK_STORE_STR), then the old array is replaced through ROM\n3's LET_WHOLE_STR, IXh = the array's letter; then LOAD_ARR_DATA.","comment":"DE = the old length"},
        "12985": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "12986": {"comment":"The type: 0, a program?"},
        "12990": {"comment":"A program: LOAD_PROGRAM"},
        "12992": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "12994": {"comment":"The old variable kept"},
        "12995": {"comment":"A, DE, BC stacked as a string value (ROM 1's STK_STORE_STR)"},
        "12998": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "12999": {"comment":"BC = the old length"},
        "13001": {"comment":"The wanted header's array letter"},
        "13004": {"comment":"Into IXh"},
        "13006": {"comment":"Replaced (ROM 3's LET_WHOLE_STR)"},
        "13009": {"comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "13010": {"synopsis":"IX back on the header (X_PTR), HL on the array's data: on to load DE bytes there\n(LOAD_BLOCK_LEN).","comment":"IX = the header again"},
        "13014": {"comment":"HL = the data's first byte"},
        "13015": {"comment":"Store the length and load"},
        "13018": {"synopsis":"LOAD of a program: the old program and variables removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL, from DE to\nE_LINE - 1), room made for the new length (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), VARS set from the header's\nprogram length, the DivMMC memory's routine at $29FD and STACK_TO_LINES before the data is\nloaded (LOAD_BLOCK_LEN), LOADED_PROG_FIX after it. Then an auto-start line (the header's\nbytes 13-14, under $4000) is gone to: A = $FF (the main program), BC = the line, and the\nstack made so that ALT_ROM_OFF leads to ROM 1's GO_TO_LINE ($2189), which returns to ROM 1's\nSTMT_BREAK ($091F) in place of the caller.","comment":"DE = the old program's start"},
        "13019": {"comment":"HL = the variables' end marker"},
        "13023": {"comment":"X_PTR = the header"},
        "13027": {"comment":"The old program and variables gone (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL)"},
        "13030": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "13032": {"comment":"The room's place kept"},
        "13033": {"comment":"The room (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "13036": {"comment":"IX = the header again"},
        "13040": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "13041": {"comment":"BC = the header's program length"},
        "13047": {"comment":"HL = the variables' start"},
        "13048": {"comment":"VARS"},
        "13051": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $29FD"},
        "13056": {"comment":"STACK_TO_LINES"},
        "13059": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "13060": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "13061": {"comment":"The header kept"},
        "13063": {"comment":"The data loaded"},
        "13066": {"comment":"And put to use (LOADED_PROG_FIX)"},
        "13069": {"comment":"IX = the header"},
        "13071": {"comment":"B = the auto-start line's high byte"},
        "13074": {"comment":"$4000 or more: none?"},
        "13077": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "13078": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "13081": {"comment":"A = $FF: the main program"},
        "13083": {"comment":"DE = this routine's return (ALT_ROM_OFF)"},
        "13084": {"comment":"The caller's return replaced by ROM 1's STMT_BREAK"},
        "13088": {"comment":"ROM 1's GO_TO_LINE"},
        "13091": {"comment":"Kept for after ALT_ROM_OFF"},
        "13093": {"comment":"ALT_ROM_OFF first, then GO_TO_LINE"},
        "13094": {"synopsis":"After a program is loaded or merged: ROM 1's $10C3 (the program index rebuilt, as 2.08's\nBUILD_INDEX_MAIN, with the 8K page in $5B33 at MMU 1), then STACK_TO_PLACES.","comment":"The program index (ROM 1's $10C3)"},
        "13097": {"comment":"The GO SUB stack's places (STACK_TO_PLACES)"},
        "13101": {"synopsis":"MERGE: STACK_TO_LINES first; the program loaded into the workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM, an\n$80 after it, then LOAD_BLOCK_LEN), then its lines (MERGE_LINES) and variables (MERGE_VARS)\nput into the program one by one.","comment":"STACK_TO_LINES first"},
        "13104": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "13110": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13111": {"comment":"One more for the $80"},
        "13112": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "13115": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "13117": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "13118": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "13119": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "13120": {"comment":"The program loaded into it"},
        "13123": {"comment":"HL = the merged program"},
        "13124": {"comment":"DE = the old program"},
        "13128": {"synopsis":"The next merged line, until the variables start (bits 6-7 of its first byte).","comment":"Its first byte"},
        "13129": {"comment":"A variable, or the end?"},
        "13131": {"comment":"Yes: MERGE_VARS"},
        "13133": {"synopsis":"Compares the merged line's number with the program's: a bigger one moves on through the\nprogram (ROM 3's NEXT_LINE).","comment":"The high bytes"},
        "13137": {"comment":"Different: that decides"},
        "13139": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "13141": {"synopsis":"Both pointers back to the lines' starts."},
        "13143": {"comment":"The merged line not bigger: put it in"},
        "13145": {"comment":"The merged line kept"},
        "13146": {"comment":"HL = the program's line"},
        "13150": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "13152": {"comment":"Compare again"},
        "13154": {"synopsis":"Puts the line in through the DivMMC memory's routine at $2200 (Z replaces the line with the\nsame number); then the next one.","comment":"Into the program (Z: replacing)"},
        "13159": {"comment":"The next merged line"},
        "13161": {"synopsis":"The merged variables, one by one, until the $80; then LOADED_PROG_FIX.","comment":"The variable's first byte"},
        "13162": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "13163": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "13165": {"comment":"Yes: finish"},
        "13167": {"comment":"The merged variable kept"},
        "13168": {"comment":"The program's variables"},
        "13171": {"synopsis":"Looks for a variable with the same first byte in the program's.","comment":"Its first byte"},
        "13172": {"comment":"The end: not there"},
        "13174": {"comment":"Not there: put it in"},
        "13176": {"comment":"The same first byte?"},
        "13179": {"synopsis":"The next one (ROM 3's VAR_SKIP).","comment":"Past this variable (ROM 3's VAR_SKIP)"},
        "13182": {"comment":"Try it"},
        "13184": {"synopsis":"The same first byte: $7F (a string with a long name) has its name's first letter compared\nbefore the letters; a long number name ($A0 type) goes to MERGE_VAR_LONG; any other is the\nsame variable.","comment":"A long-named string?"},
        "13186": {"comment":"No: a long number name?"},
        "13188": {"comment":"DE = the merged one"},
        "13190": {"comment":"The program's kept"},
        "13191": {"comment":"The bytes after the $7F"},
        "13193": {"comment":"Its first letter the same?"},
        "13195": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "13197": {"comment":"Yes: the other letters"},
        "13199": {"synopsis":"A long name ($A0 type): the letters must match too.","comment":"Bits 7-5"},
        "13201": {"comment":"A long name?"},
        "13203": {"comment":"No: the same variable"},
        "13205": {"comment":"DE = the merged one"},
        "13207": {"comment":"The program's kept"},
        "13208": {"synopsis":"Letter by letter, to the one with bit 7.","comment":"The next letters"},
        "13210": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "13212": {"comment":"No"},
        "13214": {"comment":"The last letter?"},
        "13217": {"comment":"Yes: the same variable"},
        "13220": {"synopsis":"Not the same: on.","comment":"Not the same: on"},
        "13221": {"comment":"The next variable"},
        "13223": {"synopsis":"The same: A = $FF, so Z (replace).","comment":"The same: A = $FF"},
        "13225": {"synopsis":"Puts the variable in through the DivMMC memory's routine at $2200 (Z replaces the one\nfound); then the next one.","comment":"DE = where it goes"},
        "13226": {"comment":"HL = the merged variable"},
        "13227": {"comment":"Z when one is replaced"},
        "13229": {"comment":"Into the variables (DivMMC memory, $2200)"},
        "13234": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "13236": {"synopsis":"SAVE once the header is made (from SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD): tape ($5B5E = 'T') goes to SAVE_TAPE. A\ndisk:\n1. File 0 opened, with bank 7 and the other stack (SWAP_SP_BANK7), through ROM 2's DOS_OPEN:\nthe name at $F700, access mode 3, create action 1 (a new file with a header), open action\n3 (an old file renamed to .BAK first).\n2. Its header data located (DOS_REF_HEAD).\n3. The type into it, then the length and the two parameter words (6 bytes from the header's\nbyte 11, ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7).\nA failing call goes to SAVE_DOS_FAIL. Then DATA_AND_CLOSE.","comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "13241": {"comment":"Yes: SAVE_TAPE"},
        "13243": {"comment":"The data's start kept"},
        "13244": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "13247": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13249": {"comment":"Access mode 3"},
        "13251": {"comment":"Create: a new file with a header"},
        "13253": {"comment":"Open: the old one renamed to .BAK"},
        "13255": {"comment":"The name, in bank 7"},
        "13258": {"comment":"The header kept"},
        "13260": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "13263": {"comment":"Opened?"},
        "13265": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS call failed (also from LOAD_DISK_HDR): bank 0 and the normal stack back\n(SWAP_SP_BANK0), then $2ECC, which closes file 0 and stops with the +3DOS error in A.","comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "13268": {"comment":"File 0 closed, stop with the +3DOS error ($2ECC)"},
        "13271": {"synopsis":"Opened: its header data located (ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD).","comment":"File 0"},
        "13273": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD: IX = its header data"},
        "13276": {"comment":"Failed: SAVE_DOS_FAIL"},
        "13278": {"synopsis":"The type, length, start and second word into the file's header data; then DATA_AND_CLOSE.","comment":"IX = the header, the header data kept"},
        "13280": {"comment":"HL = the header data"},
        "13281": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13284": {"comment":"The type"},
        "13287": {"comment":"Into the header data, in bank 7"},
        "13291": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "13292": {"comment":"DE = the header"},
        "13295": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = the header data"},
        "13296": {"comment":"The header's byte 11"},
        "13300": {"comment":"Length, start and second word"},
        "13303": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13306": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7 (ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7)"},
        "13309": {"comment":"HL = the data's start"},
        "13310": {"comment":"The data, then the file closed"},
        "13312": {"synopsis":"SAVE to tape: the 17-byte header at IX (ROM 3's SA_BYTES, flag 0), then a gap of 50 HALTs\nbefore the data (DATA_AND_CLOSE).","comment":"The data's start kept"},
        "13313": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "13316": {"comment":"Flag 0: a header"},
        "13317": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "13319": {"comment":"Saved (ROM 3's SA_BYTES)"},
        "13322": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13324": {"comment":"50 frames"},
        "13326": {"synopsis":"The gap: 50 HALTs.","comment":"The gap: 50 HALTs"},
        "13329": {"comment":"HL = the data's start"},
        "13330": {"synopsis":"The data block of SAVE, LOAD or VERIFY (also from LOAD_BLOCK_LEN): tape goes straight to\nDATA_BLOCK. A disk file: DATA_BLOCK, then file 0 closed (ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE) with bank 7 and\nthe other stack; failing goes to $2ECC (the +3DOS error in A).","comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "13335": {"comment":"Yes: the block only"},
        "13337": {"comment":"The block"},
        "13340": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13342": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "13345": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "13348": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "13351": {"comment":"Closed: done"},
        "13352": {"comment":"File 0 closed, stop with the +3DOS error ($2ECC)"},
        "13355": {"synopsis":"Saves, loads or verifies the data block at HL (IX = the header) by where it lives, the byte\nat $5B65: $FF ordinary memory (DATA_IN_BANK7 with A = 0, no bank); $FE the screen\n(DATA_SCREEN); $FD through bank 7's $C000 (DATA_VIA_BANK7); otherwise a 16K bank\n(DATA_IN_BANK).","comment":"Where the data lives"},
        "13358": {"comment":"$FF: ordinary memory"},
        "13359": {"comment":"Plain memory: no bank"},
        "13362": {"comment":"$FE: the screen"},
        "13366": {"comment":"$FD?"},
        "13368": {"comment":"No: a bank number"},
        "13370": {"synopsis":"$5B65 = $FD: the block goes through bank 7 at $C000: the DivMMC memory's routine at $2A0F\n(with bank 7 and the other stack), the block transferred with bank 7 (DATA_IN_BANK7), then\nfor LOAD $2A0F once more.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "13376": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13377": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "13378": {"comment":"Bank 7's $C000"},
        "13382": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "13385": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2A0F"},
        "13390": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "13393": {"comment":"HL = $C000"},
        "13395": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "13397": {"comment":"Transferred with bank 7"},
        "13400": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "13403": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "13407": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "13408": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "13411": {"comment":"$2A0F again"},
        "13416": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "13420": {"synopsis":"$5B65 a bank number: C = it, the bank passed to ROM 1's $330B; then the block transferred\nwith it (DATA_LEN).","comment":"C = the bank"},
        "13421": {"comment":"Through ROM 1's $330B"},
        "13424": {"comment":"Transfer"},
        "13426": {"synopsis":"$5B65 = $FE, the screen: with bit 1 of $5C7F set, Layer 2's three banks (DATA_LAYER2);\notherwise two $1800-byte blocks of bank 5 (the pixels at $4000 and those at $6000, seen at\n$C000 and $E000), each through DATA_GO.","comment":"Layer 2 shown?"},
        "13430": {"comment":"Yes: DATA_LAYER2"},
        "13432": {"comment":"Bank 5's first $1800 bytes"},
        "13438": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "13439": {"comment":"Bank 5"},
        "13441": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "13444": {"comment":"Then its $2000-$37FF"},
        "13448": {"comment":"Bank 5"},
        "13450": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "13452": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: its first 16K bank read from NextReg $13 (Layer 2's shadow RAM bank) through ports\n$243B/$253B, then three banks of $4000 bytes from it on, each at $C000 (DATA_GO).","comment":"Port $243B: NextReg select"},
        "13455": {"comment":"NextReg $13: Layer 2's shadow RAM bank"},
        "13457": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "13459": {"comment":"Port $253B"},
        "13460": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "13462": {"comment":"Three banks"},
        "13464": {"synopsis":"One 16K bank at $C000.","comment":"The bank at $C000"},
        "13467": {"comment":"16K"},
        "13470": {"comment":"Count and bank kept"},
        "13471": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "13475": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "13476": {"comment":"Three banks"},
        "13479": {"synopsis":"DATA_LEN with C = A (the bank; 0 for none).","comment":"C = the bank (0: none)"},
        "13480": {"synopsis":"DATA_GO with DE = the header's length (bytes 11-12).","comment":"DE = the header's length"},
        "13486": {"synopsis":"Saves, loads or verifies DE bytes at HL, with bank C (0: none); nothing for DE = 0. A disk\nfile: ROM 2's DOS_WRITE for SAVE, DOS_READ otherwise, file 0, with bank 7 and the other\nstack; failing goes to $2ECC (the +3DOS error in A). Tape: DATA_TAPE.","comment":"Nothing to do?"},
        "13489": {"comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "13494": {"comment":"Yes: DATA_TAPE"},
        "13496": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "13500": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the other stack"},
        "13503": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13505": {"comment":"Not SAVE: read"},
        "13507": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_WRITE"},
        "13510": {"comment":"Then the check"},
        "13512": {"synopsis":"LOAD or VERIFY: ROM 2's DOS_READ.","comment":"ROM 2's DOS_READ"},
        "13515": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the normal stack back; carry is success, otherwise $2ECC.","comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "13518": {"comment":"Done"},
        "13519": {"comment":"File 0 closed, stop with the +3DOS error ($2ECC)"},
        "13522": {"synopsis":"Tape: bank C (when not 0) through ROM 1's $330B, then paged at $C000-$FFFF (MMU 6 and 7) on\nthe other stack; IX = the start; SAVE through ROM 3's SA_BYTES, LOAD and MERGE (carry) or\nVERIFY (no carry) through ROM 3's LD_BYTES, flag $FF. Then TAPE_RESULT.","comment":"A bank?"},
        "13524": {"comment":"No bank: on"},
        "13526": {"comment":"The bank through ROM 1's $330B (A = its upper 8K page)"},
        "13529": {"comment":"Onto the other stack ($5B6A)"},
        "13532": {"comment":"The bank's upper page at $E000"},
        "13535": {"comment":"And its lower one at $C000"},
        "13539": {"synopsis":"IX = the start; SAVE or not?","comment":"IX = the start"},
        "13542": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "13546": {"comment":"No: load or verify"},
        "13548": {"comment":"The data block's flag"},
        "13550": {"comment":"Saved (ROM 3's SA_BYTES)"},
        "13553": {"comment":"Success"},
        "13554": {"synopsis":"The tape result in carry: kept while the normal stack is put back (SWAP_SP_BANK0, when SP is\nbelow $5C00, so on the other stack); success returns, failing goes to REPORT_R.","comment":"The flags kept in C"},
        "13556": {"comment":"SP below $5C00?"},
        "13563": {"comment":"Yes: the normal stack back (SWAP_SP_BANK0)"},
        "13566": {"comment":"The flags again"},
        "13568": {"comment":"Success: done"},
        "13569": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1A (report R, Tape loading error) through $2ED8, which closes file 0\nfirst (also from LOAD_LEN_CHECK, a length that does not fit).","comment":"Error code $1A: report R"},
        "13571": {"comment":"File 0 closed, then the error ($2ED8)"},
        "13574": {"synopsis":"LOAD, VERIFY or MERGE: carry for all but VERIFY (T_ADDR 2), then ROM 3's LD_BYTES with flag\n$FF.","comment":"T_ADDR - 2: 0 VERIFY, else carry (load)"},
        "13579": {"comment":"The data block's flag"},
        "13581": {"comment":"Loaded or verified (ROM 3's LD_BYTES)"},
        "13584": {"comment":"The result"},
        "13586": {"synopsis":"Prints a header type of 4 or 5 (from LOAD_HEADER_SHOW and $23BF) as \"Layer \" (LAYER_TEXT,\nthrough PRINT_BIT7) and the digit A + $2D (1 or 2, ROM 3's PRINT_A).","comment":"The digit: '1' for 4, '2' for 5"},
        "13588": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13589": {"comment":"The text \"Layer \""},
        "13592": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_BIT7)"},
        "13596": {"comment":"The digit (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "13600": {"synopsis":"The text \"Layer \" (bit 7 set on its last character), printed by SHOW_LAYER_KIND."},
        "13606": {"synopsis":"Takes a string from the calculator stack (ROM 1's STK_FETCH): DE = its start, BC = its\nlength; an empty one is error code $2C (REPORT_BAD_NAME).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE (what STK_FETCH changes).","comment":"DE = the start, BC = the length (ROM 1's STK_FETCH)"},
        "13609": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "13611": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "13612": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $2C (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "13614": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "13617": {"synopsis":"Copies a string from the calculator stack (NAME_ARG) to $F700 in bank 7 (ROM 1's\nCOPY_BANK0_TO_7).\nExit: HL = $F700, DE past the copy (where the caller puts its $FF).","comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "13620": {"comment":"The copy's start"},
        "13623": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13624": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "13625": {"comment":"Copied (ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7)"},
        "13628": {"comment":"HL = $F700"},
        "13630": {"synopsis":"Copies up to B characters from HL to DE, bit 7 off, stopping at a space (catalogue names are\npadded with spaces).\nExit: HL and DE past what was copied.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nThe same job as the +3E's COPY_TO_SPACE.","comment":"A space ends the name"},
        "13633": {"comment":"Done at it"},
        "13634": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "13636": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13639": {"comment":"Up to B characters"},
        "13642": {"synopsis":"Takes a drive name from the calculator stack: copied to $E090 (NAME_TO_E090) and parsed\n(PARSE_FILESPEC). It must be a drive letter alone, such as \"C:\" (flags exactly 1), else\nerror code $4E.\nExit: L = the drive letter, bank 0.","comment":"The name to $E090"},
        "13645": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "13648": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "13651": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13654": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "13655": {"comment":"Flags 1: a drive letter alone?"},
        "13656": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13657": {"comment":"No: error code $4E"},
        "13659": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "13662": {"synopsis":"Takes a name from the calculator stack to $E090 in bank 7 (NAME_TO_HL).","comment":"To $E090"},
        "13665": {"synopsis":"Copies a string from the calculator stack (NAME_ARG, not empty) to HL in bank 7, 255\ncharacters at most, and puts $FF after it.\nExit: HL = the copy, bank 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Kept"},
        "13666": {"comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "13669": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13670": {"synopsis":"256 characters or more are cut to 255.","comment":"256 characters or more?"},
        "13672": {"comment":"No"},
        "13674": {"comment":"Yes: 255"},
        "13677": {"synopsis":"The copy (ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7).","comment":"DE = the place, HL = the string"},
        "13678": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "13679": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7"},
        "13682": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "13683": {"synopsis":"$FF at DE, in bank 7; bank 0.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "13686": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "13689": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13693": {"synopsis":"CAT's name to $E090 in bank 7: BC = its length and DE its start (from STK_FETCH, at $200A);\nan empty name becomes a lone $FF.","comment":"The place"},
        "13696": {"comment":"The length"},
        "13698": {"comment":"Not 0: copied"},
        "13700": {"comment":"DE = $E090"},
        "13701": {"comment":"Just the $FF"},
        "13703": {"synopsis":"Parses the file name at HL (bank 7, $FF-ended): an optional prefix, a user area (one or two\ndigits, below 16) and/or a drive letter (A-P, either case), ended by ':'; then a path with\n'/' or '\\' separators and the file name after the last one.\nExit: HL = the file name (past the prefix and the path); D = the drive letter and E = the\nuser area (the defaults, from ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE and DOS_SET_USER with A = $FF, unless\ngiven); A = C = flags: bit 0 a drive given, bit 1 a user area given, bit 2 a wildcard ('*'\nor '?') in the file name, bit 3 a file name follows, bit 4 a path given. A wildcard before a\nseparator is error code $2C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The name kept"},
        "13704": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "13706": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE: A = the default drive"},
        "13709": {"comment":"D = the drive"},
        "13711": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "13713": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_USER: A = the default user area"},
        "13717": {"comment":"E = the user area"},
        "13718": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "13719": {"comment":"No flags yet"},
        "13721": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "13722": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "13723": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "13731": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "13733": {"comment":"E = the user area"},
        "13734": {"comment":"Bit 1: a user area"},
        "13736": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "13738": {"comment":"A second digit?"},
        "13746": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "13748": {"comment":"D = it (for now)"},
        "13749": {"comment":"E x 10"},
        "13754": {"comment":"plus the digit"},
        "13757": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "13759": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix after all"},
        "13761": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "13763": {"synopsis":"After the digits: ':' ends a user-area prefix.","comment":"':'?"},
        "13765": {"comment":"Yes: a user-area prefix"},
        "13767": {"synopsis":"A drive letter A-P must be followed by ':'.","comment":"As a capital"},
        "13769": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "13771": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix"},
        "13773": {"comment":"Above 'P'?"},
        "13775": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix"},
        "13777": {"comment":"D = the drive letter"},
        "13778": {"comment":"Bit 0: a drive"},
        "13780": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "13782": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "13784": {"comment":"No: no prefix"},
        "13786": {"synopsis":"A prefix: the name starts past its ':'.","comment":"Past the ':'"},
        "13787": {"comment":"Drop the old start"},
        "13788": {"comment":"The name starts here"},
        "13789": {"comment":"Then the scan"},
        "13791": {"synopsis":"No prefix (C = 0): the name starts at its first character.","comment":"No flags"},
        "13793": {"comment":"HL = the start again"},
        "13795": {"synopsis":"The name's characters, up to its $FF.","comment":"The next character"},
        "13797": {"comment":"$FF, the end?"},
        "13799": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "13801": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name follows"},
        "13803": {"comment":"'/'?"},
        "13807": {"comment":"'\\'?"},
        "13811": {"comment":"'*'?"},
        "13815": {"comment":"'?'?"},
        "13817": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "13819": {"synopsis":"A wildcard: bit 2.","comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard"},
        "13823": {"synopsis":"A separator: a wildcard before it is an error; otherwise bit 4 set, bit 3 cleared, and the\nfile name starts after it.","comment":"A wildcard before it?"},
        "13825": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "13827": {"comment":"No file name yet"},
        "13829": {"comment":"Bit 4: a path"},
        "13831": {"comment":"Drop the old start"},
        "13832": {"comment":"The file name starts after it"},
        "13835": {"synopsis":"HL = where the file name starts; A = the flags.","comment":"HL = where the file name starts"},
        "13836": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "13838": {"synopsis":"A wildcard in the path: error code $2C, in bank 0.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13841": {"comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "13843": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "13846": {"synopsis":"Checks a rectangle on the current screen and works out the address of its top-left pixel\n(called from $0E8D and $115F):\n1. E (the left x) + C (the width less one) must stay within 255, and below 128 unless $5C7F\n   bit 1 is set (Layer 2, 256 x 192; otherwise LoRes, 128 x 96).\n2. B (the height) 0 is error code $0A ($102D); D (the top y) + B - 1 must stay below 192, or\n   96 for LoRes. A rectangle off the screen is error code 4, SP swapped back first ($00EC).\n3. Layer 2: PRECT_ADDRESS. LoRes: LORES_ADDRESS.\nExit: DE = the address; C = the row length less one ($FF or $7F); B = the high byte at which\nthe paged-in block ends ($40, $58 or $78).","comment":"C + E, the right edge"},
        "13848": {"comment":"Past 255: off the screen"},
        "13850": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 1: Layer 2?"},
        "13854": {"comment":"Yes: 256 wide"},
        "13856": {"comment":"LoRes: 128 wide"},
        "13860": {"synopsis":"The rows.","comment":"The height"},
        "13862": {"comment":"0: report B"},
        "13865": {"comment":"The bottom edge"},
        "13867": {"comment":"Past 255: off the screen"},
        "13869": {"comment":"Row 192 or more?"},
        "13871": {"comment":"Yes: off the screen"},
        "13873": {"comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "13883": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 4 (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A), SP swapped back first.","comment":"SP swapped back first"},
        "13886": {"comment":"Error code 4"},
        "13888": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "13891": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: the 16K third holding row D is paged in at $0000-$3FFF for writing (port $123B,\nL2_PAGE_SET): DE = (D AND $3F) x 256 + E; BC = $40FF.","comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "13895": {"comment":"No: LORES_ADDRESS"},
        "13897": {"comment":"The row's top two bits"},
        "13900": {"comment":"B = the third (as port bits 7-6)"},
        "13901": {"comment":"D = the row within the third"},
        "13905": {"comment":"$5B7B's other bits"},
        "13910": {"comment":"The third added"},
        "13911": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 3: write paging, the shadow banks"},
        "13913": {"synopsis":"Port $123B = A, the third (bits 7-6; third 3 becomes third 0) and the paging bits, kept at\n$5B7B.","comment":"Third 3 or more?"},
        "13915": {"comment":"No"},
        "13917": {"comment":"Yes: back to the first third"},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"Port $123B written; BC = $40FF.","comment":"Kept"},
        "13922": {"comment":"Port $123B, Layer 2 access"},
        "13927": {"comment":"B = $40, the third's end; C = $FF"},
        "13931": {"synopsis":"LoRes: DE = $4000 + D x 128 + E, rows 48 and more at $6000 on; B = $58 (or $78 for the lower\nhalf); C = $7F; MMU slot 3 gets page $0B (LORES_PAGE_IN).","comment":"D / 2, the odd row bit into the carry"},
        "13933": {"comment":"An even row"},
        "13935": {"comment":"Odd: the right half of 256 bytes"},
        "13937": {"synopsis":"D = $40 + D / 2.","comment":"D + $40: at $4000 on"},
        "13939": {"comment":"B = $58, the upper half's end; C = $7F"},
        "13942": {"comment":"The address's high byte"},
        "13943": {"comment":"Below $5800?"},
        "13944": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13946": {"comment":"Rows 48 on: $6000 on"},
        "13949": {"comment":"B = $78, the lower half's end"},
        "13951": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 3 ($6000-$7FFF) = page $0B.","comment":"Page $0B"},
        "13953": {"synopsis":"NextReg $53 (MMU slot 3) = A.","comment":"MMU slot 3"},
        "13957": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 3 = page $11 again.","comment":"Page $11"},
        "13961": {"synopsis":"The next row: DE = HL (this row's start) + C + 1. When that crosses B: Layer 2 pages the\nnext third in (L2_NEXT_THIRD), LoRes moves on to the lower half at $6000 (LORES_LOWER).\nCalled from $116D.\nChanges: AF, DE, and B and the paging when a block is crossed.","comment":"DE = C + 1, the row's length"},
        "13965": {"comment":"plus the row's start"},
        "13966": {"comment":"DE = the next row's"},
        "13967": {"comment":"Still below the block's end?"},
        "13969": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "13970": {"comment":"C = $FF: Layer 2?"},
        "13972": {"comment":"No: LoRes"},
        "13974": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: D back to $00-$3F, the next third ($5B7B + $40) paged in. Also called from $0F6C.","comment":"D back to the third's start"},
        "13976": {"comment":"The paged third"},
        "13979": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "13981": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "13983": {"synopsis":"LoRes: on to $6000 on (D + 8); B = $78. Also called from $0F78.","comment":"D + 8: on to $6000"},
        "13987": {"comment":"B = $78, the lower half's end"},
        "13990": {"synopsis":"Ends drawing (from $0F89 and $1174): LoRes (C = $7F) gives MMU slot 3 page $11 back\n(LORES_PAGE_OUT); Layer 2 (C = $FF) leaves only the visibility bit of $5B7B (bit 1) in port\n$123B, so the paging is off.","comment":"C = $FF: Layer 2?"},
        "13991": {"comment":"No: page $11 back"},
        "13993": {"comment":"The visibility bit alone"},
        "13996": {"comment":"(bit 1)"},
        "13998": {"comment":"Port $123B: paging off"},
        "14000": {"synopsis":"A = the low four bits of $5C7F (the screen mode): 0 returns Z, 1-2 return with carry; 3 and\nup return A / 4 - 1 (NC). Called from $0ED0, $0FC9 and $10BB. The same job as NextZXOS ROM\n1's MODE_5C7F_GET (the bytes are the same).","comment":"The screen mode"},
        "14003": {"comment":"Its low four bits"},
        "14005": {"comment":"0: Z"},
        "14006": {"comment":"1 or 2?"},
        "14008": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14009": {"comment":"A / 4"},
        "14013": {"comment":"less 1"},
        "14015": {"synopsis":"Before the program is changed (NextZXOS ROM 1's AR_FINISH, and LOAD_PROGRAM and MERGE_LOAD\nhere, call it first): when $5B66 bit 1 is set, it is cleared and the GO SUB stack is walked\nfrom its newest entry (ERR_SP + 3, each entry's type byte). In each type-1 entry whose byte\nbefore the type is 0 the place it records (a bank byte and an offset, 8 bytes below its end)\nis made a line number: the line holding that place is looked for in the main program (the\noffset + PROG) or in the bank (paged in at $C000, its lines from $C002), and its number\nwritten over the offset (STACK_TO_PLACES turns it back). Bank $FE records no place. Other\nentries are passed: types 0 and 1 by their length word, 2-$3D by 11 bytes, $3F up by the\ntype with bit 6 cleared; $3E ends the walk.","comment":"$5B66 bit 1: places to convert?"},
        "14020": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "14021": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "14023": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "14026": {"comment":"+ 3: the newest entry's type byte"},
        "14028": {"synopsis":"HL on to the next entry's type byte."},
        "14029": {"synopsis":"An entry, by its type.","comment":"The type"},
        "14030": {"comment":"1?"},
        "14032": {"comment":"Yes: STL_TYPE_1"},
        "14034": {"comment":"0: a variable entry"},
        "14036": {"comment":"$3E, the end marker?"},
        "14038": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "14039": {"comment":"2-$3D: 11 bytes"},
        "14041": {"comment":"Higher: bit 6 off"},
        "14043": {"comment":"is the entry's size"},
        "14047": {"synopsis":"Types 0 and 1: passed by the length word after the type.","comment":"Past the type"},
        "14048": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14052": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14055": {"synopsis":"Types 2-$3D: 11 bytes.","comment":"11 bytes on"},
        "14061": {"synopsis":"Type 1: the byte before the type not 0 is passed as STL_SKIP_VAR; 0 has a place to convert.","comment":"The byte before the type"},
        "14064": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "14065": {"comment":"Then passed as type 0"},
        "14067": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14072": {"comment":"HL = the entry's end"},
        "14076": {"comment":"The end kept"},
        "14077": {"comment":"8 bytes back: the place's bank"},
        "14082": {"comment":"$FE: no place"},
        "14084": {"comment":"Then nothing to do"},
        "14086": {"comment":"The offset's address"},
        "14087": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14088": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "14091": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "14094": {"comment":"$FF, the main program?"},
        "14095": {"comment":"Yes: STL_MAIN"},
        "14097": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14098": {"comment":"Bank 7 (SP swapped)"},
        "14101": {"comment":"Its two 8K pages"},
        "14102": {"comment":"at MMU slot 6"},
        "14106": {"comment":"and 7: the bank at $C000"},
        "14109": {"comment":"The bank's first line"},
        "14112": {"comment":"The search"},
        "14114": {"synopsis":"The main program: DE = PROG + the offset.","comment":"PROG"},
        "14117": {"comment":"DE = PROG + the offset"},
        "14120": {"synopsis":"One line: BC = its number (high byte first), then past its length, until the line reaches\npast DE.","comment":"BC = the line's number"},
        "14124": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14125": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "14129": {"comment":"The text's start kept"},
        "14130": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "14131": {"comment":"Past DE?"},
        "14133": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "14134": {"comment":"Yes: this line"},
        "14136": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "14137": {"comment":"Drop the number"},
        "14140": {"synopsis":"The line found: bank 0 again for a bank; its number written over the offset.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "14141": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "14144": {"comment":"A bank ($FF + 1 not 0)?"},
        "14145": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "14148": {"comment":"The offset's address"},
        "14149": {"comment":"The line number written over it"},
        "14152": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"The entry's end back"},
        "14155": {"synopsis":"STACK_TO_PLACES for a direct command (from NextZXOS ROM 1's RUN_SETUP): the main program\nselected (ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK with A = $FF) and T_ADDR = $80, whose bit 7 makes\nSTP_ENTRY_11 check the 11-byte entries; then STACK_TO_PLACES.","comment":"$FF: the main program"},
        "14157": {"comment":"Selected (ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK)"},
        "14160": {"comment":"T_ADDR = $80: bit 7 set, the 11-byte entries checked"},
        "14164": {"synopsis":"After the program has changed (from STP_RUN_SETUP and LOADED_PROG_FIX): sets $5B66 bit 1 and\nmakes the GO SUB stack's entries point at the program again, keeping the current place:\n1. CH_ADD's offset from PROG_BASE (ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC), PPC and the program's bank\n($5B77) saved.\n2. With T_ADDR bit 7 set (STP_RUN_SETUP), each 11-byte entry (types 2-$3D and $4B) is found\nagain by its line (entry bytes 7-8) and statement (byte 9): NXTLIN's and CH_ADD's offsets\n(bytes 5-6 and 3-4) and $5EB6 (bytes 1-2) are set again. CH_ADD's place: for type $22\nafter PROC name(...) (possibly after BANK n), for $4B after ON ERROR, for the others the\nnext statement. An entry whose line or statement is gone, or that belongs to a direct\ncommand (line bit 15), gets bank $FE. With bit 7 clear (after LOAD or MERGE) these\nentries are left as they are.\n3. Each type-1 entry with a line number (from STACK_TO_LINES): the variable is looked for in\nthe line's PRIVATE statements (token $82), each name after a hidden number; its number's\nplace is written back as the entry's offset. Not found: bank $FE and the name's low five\nbits $1E.\n4. At the end ($3E) the bank, PPC, NXTLIN and CH_ADD are set again.","comment":"Places held from now on"},
        "14169": {"comment":"HL = PROG_BASE for PPC (ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC)"},
        "14172": {"comment":"DE = PROG_BASE"},
        "14173": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
        "14177": {"comment":"less PROG_BASE"},
        "14179": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14180": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "14183": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14184": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14187": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14188": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "14191": {"comment":"+ 3: the newest entry's type byte"},
        "14193": {"synopsis":"HL on to the next entry's type byte."},
        "14194": {"synopsis":"An entry, by its type: 0 STP_SKIP_VAR; 1 STP_TYPE_1; 2-$3D and $4B STP_ENTRY_11; $3E\nSTP_END; others passed by the type with bit 6 cleared.","comment":"The type"},
        "14195": {"comment":"1?"},
        "14197": {"comment":"Yes: STP_TYPE_1"},
        "14199": {"comment":"0: a variable entry"},
        "14201": {"comment":"$3E, the end marker?"},
        "14203": {"comment":"Yes: STP_END"},
        "14205": {"comment":"2-$3D: an 11-byte entry"},
        "14208": {"comment":"$4B (ON ERROR)?"},
        "14210": {"comment":"Also an 11-byte entry"},
        "14213": {"comment":"Higher: bit 6 off"},
        "14215": {"comment":"is the entry's size"},
        "14219": {"synopsis":"The end: the program's bank set again ($FE as $FF, main memory); line PPC found again;\nNXTLIN = the line after it; CH_ADD = PROG_BASE + its offset.","comment":"The bank saved"},
        "14220": {"comment":"$FE?"},
        "14222": {"comment":"No"},
        "14224": {"comment":"$FE becomes $FF, the main program"},
        "14225": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK; then line PPC found again (LINE_FIND, LINE_PPC_NEXT).","comment":"ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK"},
        "14228": {"comment":"BC = the PPC saved"},
        "14229": {"comment":"Line PPC (ROM 1's LINE_FIND)"},
        "14232": {"comment":"NXTLIN (ROM 1's LINE_PPC_NEXT)"},
        "14235": {"comment":"NXTLIN = the line after it"},
        "14238": {"comment":"HL = PROG_BASE (ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC)"},
        "14241": {"comment":"CH_ADD's offset"},
        "14242": {"comment":"plus PROG_BASE"},
        "14243": {"comment":"CH_ADD again"},
        "14247": {"synopsis":"Passed by the length word after the type.","comment":"Past the type"},
        "14248": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14252": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14255": {"synopsis":"Type 1: the byte before the type not 0 is passed; 0: $5C5F = the entry's data (the name);\nthe line it records (bank, number) looked for (SET_PROG_BANK, LINE_FIND, LINE_PPC_NEXT); its\nPRIVATE statements (token $82, FIND_STMT_CHAR) searched.","comment":"The byte before the type"},
        "14258": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "14259": {"comment":"Then passed as type 0"},
        "14261": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14265": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14266": {"comment":"X_PTR = the entry's data"},
        "14269": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "14270": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14271": {"comment":"8 bytes back: the bank"},
        "14276": {"comment":"$FE: no place?"},
        "14278": {"comment":"Yes: the next entry"},
        "14280": {"comment":"The line number's address"},
        "14281": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14282": {"comment":"BC = the line number"},
        "14285": {"comment":"The bank (ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK)"},
        "14288": {"comment":"The line (ROM 1's LINE_FIND)"},
        "14291": {"comment":"Gone: STP_T1_GONE"},
        "14294": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_PPC_NEXT"},
        "14297": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "14298": {"comment":"Any statement, starting PRIVATE"},
        "14301": {"comment":"The first PRIVATE (ROM 1's FIND_STMT_CHAR)"},
        "14304": {"synopsis":"No PRIVATE statement left: STP_T1_GONE.","comment":"None: STP_T1_GONE"},
        "14306": {"synopsis":"One item: a hidden number ($0E and 5 bytes) must come next; then the name after it is\ncompared with the entry's.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL + 1, the next character"},
        "14309": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "14311": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "14313": {"comment":"Its 5 bytes"},
        "14314": {"comment":"kept"},
        "14315": {"comment":"Past them: the name"},
        "14319": {"comment":"The entry's name"},
        "14323": {"comment":"The name's first character"},
        "14326": {"comment":"In lower case"},
        "14329": {"comment":"The entry's first letter"},
        "14330": {"comment":"Its low five bits"},
        "14332": {"comment":"as a lower-case letter"},
        "14334": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "14335": {"comment":"No: the next item"},
        "14337": {"comment":"The entry's first byte again"},
        "14338": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14339": {"comment":"Bit 6: a name of one letter?"},
        "14341": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14343": {"synopsis":"One more character of a long name (bit 7 marks the last).","comment":"The next character"},
        "14344": {"comment":"In lower case"},
        "14347": {"comment":"The entry's next character"},
        "14348": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "14350": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "14351": {"comment":"No: the next item"},
        "14353": {"comment":"Again"},
        "14355": {"comment":"Bit 7 into the carry: the last?"},
        "14356": {"comment":"No: the next character"},
        "14358": {"synopsis":"The name ended: a letter or digit after it is a different name (ROM 1's ALPHANUM).","comment":"The character after the name"},
        "14359": {"comment":"A letter or digit (ROM 1's ALPHANUM)?"},
        "14362": {"comment":"Yes: a longer name"},
        "14364": {"comment":"DE = the hidden number"},
        "14365": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14368": {"comment":"$FF, main memory?"},
        "14369": {"comment":"No: STP_BANK_PLACE"},
        "14371": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "14374": {"comment":"HL = the number's address"},
        "14375": {"comment":"less PROG: the offset"},
        "14377": {"comment":"On"},
        "14379": {"synopsis":"In a bank: the number's address in the bank (ROM 1's CACHE_TO_BANK).","comment":"ROM 1's CACHE_TO_BANK"},
        "14382": {"synopsis":"The place written into the entry.","comment":"DE = the place"},
        "14383": {"comment":"The line number's address"},
        "14384": {"comment":"The place written over it"},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"The entry's end"},
        "14388": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "14391": {"synopsis":"Not this name: on to the next ',' (another item) or the statement's end.","comment":"Drop the item's start"},
        "14392": {"synopsis":"One character; a hidden number is passed.","comment":"The character"},
        "14393": {"comment":"','?"},
        "14395": {"comment":"Yes: the next item"},
        "14397": {"comment":"The statement's end (ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)?"},
        "14400": {"comment":"The statement's end: the next one"},
        "14402": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14403": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "14405": {"comment":"No: the next character"},
        "14407": {"comment":"Its 5 bytes passed"},
        "14413": {"synopsis":"The next statement, then the next PRIVATE (ROM 1's SKIP_STMT).","comment":"The next PRIVATE"},
        "14416": {"comment":"Outside quotes"},
        "14418": {"comment":"ROM 1's SKIP_STMT"},
        "14421": {"comment":"Then FIND_STMT_CHAR's result"},
        "14423": {"synopsis":"Not found: bank $FE; the low five bits of the name's first byte made $1E.","comment":"The line number's address"},
        "14424": {"comment":"The bank byte"},
        "14425": {"comment":"$FE: no place"},
        "14427": {"comment":"The entry's name"},
        "14430": {"comment":"Its first byte"},
        "14431": {"comment":"Its top three bits"},
        "14433": {"comment":"with $1E below them"},
        "14436": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "14438": {"synopsis":"An 11-byte entry: bank (the byte below the type) and line (bytes 7-8). With T_ADDR bit 7\nclear (after LOAD or MERGE) it is left as it is (STP_ENTRY_KEEP); otherwise bank $FE or a\ndirect command's line (bit 15) is dropped (STP_DROP), and the line is found again\n(SET_PROG_BANK, LINE_FIND, LINE_PPC_NEXT).","comment":"The type's address kept"},
        "14439": {"comment":"The bank byte"},
        "14440": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "14441": {"comment":"Entry bytes 7-8"},
        "14445": {"comment":"BC = the line number"},
        "14448": {"comment":"T_ADDR bit 7 clear (after LOAD or MERGE)?"},
        "14452": {"comment":"Yes: the entry left as it is"},
        "14455": {"comment":"Bit 15: a direct command?"},
        "14457": {"comment":"Yes: dropped"},
        "14460": {"comment":"Bank $FE?"},
        "14462": {"comment":"Yes: dropped"},
        "14465": {"comment":"The bank (ROM 1's SET_PROG_BANK)"},
        "14468": {"comment":"The line (ROM 1's LINE_FIND)"},
        "14471": {"comment":"Gone: dropped"},
        "14474": {"comment":"ROM 1's LINE_PPC_NEXT"},
        "14477": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "14481": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14484": {"comment":"$FF, main memory?"},
        "14485": {"comment":"No: a bank address already"},
        "14487": {"comment":"The next line's offset"},
        "14490": {"synopsis":"Bytes 1-2 = $5EB6, bytes 5-6 = NXTLIN's offset; CH_ADD = the line's start; statement byte 9\nfound (ROM 1's FIND_STMT_CH).","comment":"DE = it, HL = the line"},
        "14491": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the line"},
        "14494": {"comment":"The type's address"},
        "14496": {"comment":"Bytes 1-2"},
        "14497": {"comment":"= $5EB6"},
        "14504": {"comment":"Past bytes 3-4"},
        "14507": {"comment":"Bytes 5-6 = NXTLIN's offset"},
        "14512": {"comment":"Byte 9"},
        "14513": {"comment":"D = the statement number"},
        "14514": {"comment":"Any first character"},
        "14516": {"comment":"Statement D (ROM 1's FIND_STMT_CH)"},
        "14519": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the statement"},
        "14522": {"comment":"Not there: dropped"},
        "14524": {"comment":"The type's address"},
        "14526": {"comment":"The type"},
        "14527": {"comment":"Type $22?"},
        "14529": {"comment":"No"},
        "14531": {"comment":"The statement's first character"},
        "14532": {"comment":"BANK?"},
        "14534": {"comment":"No: PROC?"},
        "14536": {"comment":"Outside quotes"},
        "14538": {"synopsis":"BANK n ...: the statement scanned, quotes skipped, for PROC; ENTER or ':' first drops the\nentry.","comment":"The next character"},
        "14539": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "14541": {"comment":"Yes: dropped"},
        "14543": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "14545": {"comment":"Yes: flip"},
        "14547": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "14549": {"comment":"Yes: the next"},
        "14551": {"comment":"PROC?"},
        "14553": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14555": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "14557": {"comment":"Yes: dropped"},
        "14559": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "14561": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "14563": {"comment":"Its 5 bytes passed"},
        "14567": {"comment":"CH_ADD past them"},
        "14570": {"comment":"The next"},
        "14572": {"synopsis":"A quote: C bit 0 flips.","comment":"Inside or outside quotes"},
        "14575": {"synopsis":"Not BANK: it must be PROC.","comment":"PROC?"},
        "14577": {"comment":"No: dropped"},
        "14579": {"synopsis":"PROC: past the name and its bracketed list (ROM 1's CHECK_NAME_PAREN, SKIP_BRACKETS).","comment":"Past PROC"},
        "14580": {"comment":"The name and '(' (ROM 1's CHECK_NAME_PAREN)"},
        "14583": {"comment":"Past '('"},
        "14584": {"comment":"Past the list (ROM 1's SKIP_BRACKETS)"},
        "14587": {"comment":"One back"},
        "14590": {"synopsis":"Type $4B: ON ERROR must follow; CH_ADD past it.","comment":"$4B?"},
        "14592": {"comment":"No: the other types"},
        "14594": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "14595": {"comment":"ON?"},
        "14597": {"comment":"No: dropped"},
        "14599": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "14600": {"comment":"ERROR?"},
        "14602": {"comment":"No: dropped"},
        "14604": {"comment":"CH_ADD past it"},
        "14607": {"synopsis":"Other types: the start of the next statement (FIND_STMT_CH with D = 2).","comment":"Within 2 statements: the next one's start"},
        "14609": {"comment":"ROM 1's FIND_STMT_CH"},
        "14612": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD's offset from PROG_BASE into entry bytes 3-4; the next entry.","comment":"DE = the place"},
        "14613": {"comment":"HL = PROG_BASE (ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC)"},
        "14616": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "14618": {"comment":"less PROG_BASE"},
        "14620": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "14621": {"comment":"The type's address"},
        "14622": {"comment":"Bytes 3-4"},
        "14625": {"comment":"= CH_ADD's offset"},
        "14628": {"comment":"HL = byte 10, the entry's last"},
        "14632": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "14635": {"synopsis":"T_ADDR bit 7 clear (after LOAD or MERGE): the 11-byte entry is left as it is\n(STP_ENTRY_PAST).","comment":"The type's address"},
        "14636": {"comment":"The bank byte, left as it is"},
        "14637": {"comment":"On to the entry's end"},
        "14639": {"synopsis":"The entry dropped: its bank byte $FE.","comment":"The type's address"},
        "14640": {"comment":"The bank byte"},
        "14641": {"comment":"$FE: no place"},
        "14643": {"comment":"HL = byte 10, the entry's last","synopsis":"HL = byte 10, the entry's last; the next entry."},
        "14647": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "14650": {"synopsis":"KEPT_VARS_SET's (NextZXOS ROM 1) 5 new bytes, just written into a line before DE, put into\nthe GO SUB stack's type-1 entries that record that place too: $5CA8 = their address; the\nplace as an offset from PROG (main program) or a bank address (ROM 1's CACHE_TO_BANK); every\ntype-1 entry whose byte before the type is 0, whose bank is $5B77 and whose place matches\ngets the 5 bytes. Other entries are passed as STACK_TO_LINES passes them.\nEntry: DE = the address just past the 5 bytes.\nExit: DE as on entry.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "14651": {"comment":"DE = the 5 bytes' start"},
        "14655": {"comment":"Kept at $5CA8"},
        "14659": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14662": {"comment":"$FF, main memory?"},
        "14663": {"comment":"No: KVU_BANK"},
        "14665": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "14669": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "14670": {"comment":"less PROG: the offset"},
        "14674": {"synopsis":"In a bank: CACHE_TO_BANK.","comment":"ROM 1's CACHE_TO_BANK"},
        "14677": {"synopsis":"The place kept on the stack; the walk from ERR_SP + 3.","comment":"The place kept"},
        "14678": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "14681": {"comment":"+ 3: the newest entry's type byte"},
        "14683": {"synopsis":"HL on to the next entry's type byte."},
        "14684": {"synopsis":"An entry, by its type.","comment":"The type"},
        "14685": {"comment":"1?"},
        "14687": {"comment":"Yes: KVU_TYPE_1"},
        "14689": {"comment":"0: a variable entry"},
        "14691": {"comment":"$3E, the end marker?"},
        "14693": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "14695": {"comment":"2-$3D: 11 bytes"},
        "14697": {"comment":"Higher: bit 6 off"},
        "14699": {"comment":"is the entry's size"},
        "14703": {"synopsis":"$3E, the end: done.","comment":"Drop the place"},
        "14704": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "14706": {"synopsis":"Types 0 and 1: passed by their length word.","comment":"Past the type"},
        "14707": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14711": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14714": {"synopsis":"Types 2-$3D: 11 bytes.","comment":"11 bytes on"},
        "14720": {"synopsis":"Type 1: does it record this place?","comment":"The byte before the type"},
        "14723": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "14724": {"comment":"Then passed as type 0"},
        "14726": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "14731": {"comment":"HL = the entry's end"},
        "14732": {"comment":"BC = the place"},
        "14734": {"comment":"The end kept"},
        "14735": {"comment":"8 bytes back: the bank"},
        "14739": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14742": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "14743": {"comment":"No: the next entry"},
        "14745": {"comment":"DE = the place it records"},
        "14749": {"comment":"HL at its 5 bytes"},
        "14750": {"comment":"DE = them, HL = the place"},
        "14751": {"comment":"The same place?"},
        "14753": {"comment":"No: the next entry"},
        "14755": {"comment":"The new 5 bytes"},
        "14758": {"comment":"copied into the entry"},
        "14763": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"The entry's end back"},
        "14764": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "14766": {"synopsis":"PALETTE FORMAT n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE FORMAT, the word at its\n$050D): the ULANext ink mask n through NextZXOS ROM 1's SET_ULANEXT (0 turns ULANext off;\notherwise one less than a power of 2, report B otherwise).","comment":"A = the mask (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14769": {"comment":"The ULANext ink mask (ROM 1's SET_ULANEXT)"},
        "14773": {"synopsis":"SPRITE PALETTE n ... (jumped to from $0591, the SPRITE command's PALETTE): past PALETTE and\nits number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6), then PAL_LAYER_GO for the sprites' palettes ($28).","comment":"Past PALETTE, then a number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6)"},
        "14776": {"comment":"$28: the sprites' palettes (NextReg $43 bits 6-4 = 010)"},
        "14778": {"comment":"On"},
        "14780": {"synopsis":"LAYER PALETTE n ... (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER PALETTE, the word at its\n$0519): the palettes of the current mode's layer ($14 for Layer 2, $02 for the ULA and\nLoRes), then PAL_LAYER_GO.","comment":"$14: Layer 2's palettes (bits 6-4 = 001)"},
        "14782": {"comment":"A Layer 2 mode ($5C7F bit 1)?"},
        "14786": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14788": {"comment":"$02: the ULA's palettes (bits 6-4 = 000)"},
        "14790": {"synopsis":"The palette commands, n (0 or 1, the first or second palette) on the calculator stack and\n$5B8A = the layer (bits 5-4 its value for NextReg $43 bits 5-4, bits 3-1 its active-palette\nbit there):\n1. n alone: palette n becomes the layer's active one (PAL_SELECT).\n2. n BANK b, o: palette n loaded from bank b at offset o (PAL_BANK_LOAD).\n3. n, i, v: entry i of palette n = the 9-bit colour v (0-511, report B otherwise), through\n   NextRegs $40 and $44.\n4. Anything else: report C (REPORT_C, $0688).","comment":"$5B8A = the layer: bits 5-4 select, bits 3-1 its active-palette bit"},
        "14793": {"comment":"A = the character after the number"},
        "14794": {"comment":"The statement's end (ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)?"},
        "14797": {"comment":"Yes: choose the active palette"},
        "14799": {"comment":"BANK?"},
        "14801": {"comment":"Yes: load a palette from a bank"},
        "14803": {"comment":"','?"},
        "14805": {"comment":"Anything else: report C"},
        "14808": {"comment":"Past ',', then two numbers (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "14811": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "14814": {"comment":"BC = the colour (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "14817": {"comment":"Over 511?"},
        "14820": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "14823": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14824": {"comment":"A = the entry (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14827": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14828": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14831": {"comment":"It chosen for writing"},
        "14834": {"comment":"A = the entry"},
        "14835": {"comment":"The palette's index"},
        "14838": {"comment":"DE = the colour"},
        "14839": {"comment":"E = bits 8-1, D bit 0 = bit 0"},
        "14845": {"comment":"The first byte, RRRGGGBB"},
        "14849": {"comment":"Then the last blue bit"},
        "14854": {"synopsis":"n alone: palette n (0 or 1, report B otherwise) becomes the layer's active one: its bit in\nNextReg $43 set or cleared (PAL_CTRL_MASK).","comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "14857": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14860": {"comment":"0 or 1 only"},
        "14862": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "14865": {"comment":"L = the palette"},
        "14866": {"comment":"D = the layer's active-palette bit"},
        "14872": {"comment":"E = every other bit"},
        "14874": {"comment":"The second palette?"},
        "14876": {"comment":"Yes: the bit set"},
        "14878": {"comment":"The first: the bit cleared"},
        "14880": {"synopsis":"NextReg $43 = (NextReg $43 AND E) OR D (PAL_CTRL_MASK).","comment":"NextReg $43 changed"},
        "14882": {"synopsis":"n BANK b, o: palette n chosen for writing from entry 0; bank b paged at $C000 (checked\nthrough NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3, offset o below $4000) on the other stack; its 256\nentries from $C000 + o: one byte each (NextReg $41), or two each (NextReg $44 twice) when\nPALETTE DIM 9 set $5C7F bit 4. Running past the bank's end is report B ($1035). RAM bank 0\nand the normal stack back at the end (SWAP_SP_BANK0).","comment":"Past BANK, then two numbers (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "14885": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "14888": {"comment":"BC = the offset (ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "14891": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14892": {"comment":"A = the bank (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14895": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14896": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14899": {"comment":"It chosen for writing"},
        "14902": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "14906": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14907": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "14908": {"comment":"Bank A, offset HL checked (ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3)"},
        "14911": {"comment":"Onto the other stack ($5B6A)"},
        "14914": {"comment":"The offset at $C000-$FFFF"},
        "14918": {"comment":"A = the bank's upper 8K page"},
        "14921": {"comment":"And the lower one, at $C000"},
        "14925": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "14926": {"comment":"BC = 255: the last byte of 256"},
        "14929": {"comment":"9-bit entries ($5C7F bit 4)?"},
        "14933": {"comment":"No"},
        "14935": {"comment":"511: the last of 512"},
        "14936": {"synopsis":"Does the palette run past $FFFF?","comment":"Past the bank's end?"},
        "14937": {"comment":"DE = the start"},
        "14938": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "14941": {"comment":"256 entries"},
        "14943": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"A = the next byte"},
        "14945": {"comment":"9-bit entries?"},
        "14949": {"comment":"No"},
        "14951": {"comment":"The first byte, RRRGGGBB"},
        "14954": {"comment":"Then the second, its blue bit"},
        "14959": {"comment":"On"},
        "14961": {"synopsis":"An 8-bit entry.","comment":"One 8-bit entry"},
        "14964": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"One entry less"},
        "14965": {"comment":"More?"},
        "14967": {"comment":"RAM bank 0 and the normal stack back"},
        "14971": {"synopsis":"Chooses palette A (0 or 1, report B otherwise) of the layer in $5B8A for reading and\nwriting: NextReg $43 bit 6 = A, bits 5-4 = the layer's; bits 7 and 3-0 kept (PAL_CTRL_MASK).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"0 or 1 only"},
        "14973": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "14976": {"comment":"Bit 6: the palette"},
        "14979": {"comment":"Bits 5-4: the layer's"},
        "14986": {"comment":"E: bits 7 and 3-0 kept"},
        "14988": {"synopsis":"NextReg $43 = (NextReg $43 AND E) OR D: read through READ_NEXTREG, $09D7 (port $243B\nselected, port $253B read), written back through port $253B.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"A = NextReg $43, read through port $253B (READ_NEXTREG, $09D7)"},
        "14993": {"comment":"Its kept bits"},
        "14994": {"comment":"With the new ones"},
        "14995": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "14998": {"synopsis":"PALETTE DIM n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE DIM, the word at its $050A): n\n8 or 9 (report B otherwise): the width of the entries PAL_BANK_LOAD reads, kept in $5C7F bit\n4 (set for 9).","comment":"A = 8 or 9 (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "15001": {"comment":"8 or 9 less 8"},
        "15003": {"comment":"Below 8: report B"},
        "15006": {"comment":"0 or 1?"},
        "15008": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "15011": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 4 cleared: 8-bit entries"},
        "15015": {"comment":"8?"},
        "15016": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "15017": {"comment":"9: $5C7F bit 4 set"},
        "15022": {"synopsis":"PALETTE OVER n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE OVER, the word at its $0510):\nA = n (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE) to the DivMMC memory's routine at $2993; the DE it gives goes to\nHL, then ROM 1's $163E: NextReg $14 (the global transparent colour) = A, and NextReg $4B\n(the sprites' transparent index) too unless bit 4 of L is set.","comment":"A = the colour (ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "15025": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2993"},
        "15030": {"comment":"HL = the DE it gave"},
        "15031": {"comment":"NextReg $14, and $4B unless L bit 4 (ROM 1's $163E)"},
        "15035": {"synopsis":"Unused, $00 to the end of the page ($3ABB-$3FFF)."}
      }
    }
  },
